window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0027", [{"word":"prospect","ipa_uk":"/ˈprɒspekt/","ipa_us":"/ˈprɑːspekt/","definition_zh":"前景；可能性；景象；潜在客户；勘探；展望","definition_en":"the view ahead, whether seen by the eye or expected by the mind, and the act of searching the ground for what it may hold","core_image":"一个人站在高处向前看，视线越过地平线，既看见眼前的景，也看见将要发生的事","scene":"A young engineer stands on a ridge at dawn, looking across a valley where a mine may lie, and says: The prospect of finding copper here is good, but he would rather have a quiet life.","sceneCN":"这里 prospect 是「可能性、机会」（第 2 个义项：某事将会发生或成功的可能性）；句意：这里找到铜的可能性很大，但他宁愿过安稳日子。画面里有山脊、晨雾和尚未开挖的谷地。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"前景；可能性；景象；潜在客户"},{"tag":"v.","zh":"勘探；勘察；探测"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the prospect of","zh":"……的前景/可能性"},{"phrase":"job prospects","zh":"就业前景"},{"phrase":"in prospect","zh":"有望；即将发生"},{"phrase":"prospect for gold","zh":"勘探黄金"},{"phrase":"a promising prospect","zh":"有前途的人选/潜在客户"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"prospects"},{"label":"三单","form":"prospects"},{"label":"过去式","form":"prospected"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"prospected"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"prospecting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"prospective","pos":"adj.","zh":"预期的；未来的；潜在的"},{"word":"prospector","pos":"n.","zh":"勘探者；探矿者"},{"word":"prospectus","pos":"n.","zh":"（学校、企业的）章程；招股说明书"},{"word":"prospection","pos":"n.","zh":"展望；勘探"},{"word":"prospectively","pos":"adv.","zh":"预期地；未来地"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The future in view: what lies ahead","titleCN":"前景：前方等待的那幅图景","definition":"the possibility or expectation of something happening in the future, especially something good","definitionCN":"对未来某事的可能性或预期，尤指好事","example":"The prospect of a long winter worried the farmers.","exampleCN":"漫长冬季的前景让农民们忧心。","why":"The noun appears in the 1660s as 'expectation, ground of expectation', from the habit of looking forward. What the eye does in space, the mind does in time: it scans the horizon of coming events.","whyCN":"这个名词在 17 世纪 60 年代出现，义为“预期、期待的依据”，来自“向前看”的动作。眼睛在空间里做的事，心智在时间里也做：它扫视将要发生之事的地平线。"},{"no":"02","title":"A chance that may come true","titleCN":"可能性、机会：尚未兑现的那份可能","definition":"a chance or possibility that something will happen or succeed","definitionCN":"某事将会发生或成功的可能性","example":"There is little prospect of finding survivors after so long.","exampleCN":"过了这么久，找到幸存者的可能性很小。","why":"The 1620s sense 'mental view or survey' let people speak of viewing a future outcome. Once an outcome is 'in view', it is a chance on the horizon rather than a certainty in hand.","whyCN":"17 世纪 20 年代“心中的审视”这一义项，让人可以“看见”未来的结果。一个结果一旦“在视野里”，它就是地平线上的机会，而不是握在手里的确定。"},{"no":"03","title":"The sweep of the eye: a wide view","titleCN":"景象、视野：眼睛扫过的那一大片","definition":"a view or scene, especially a wide one seen from a high place","definitionCN":"景色、景象，尤指从高处看到的广阔视野","example":"From the hilltop we had a fine prospect of the valley.","exampleCN":"从山顶上，我们看到了山谷的美丽景色。","why":"From 1530s English, prospect meant 'extensive view of the landscape', straight from Latin prospectus 'distant view'. The word still carries the physical sweep of the eye before it carries hope.","whyCN":"从 16 世纪 30 年代起，prospect 指“广阔的风景视野”，直接来自拉丁语 prospectus“远处的景色”。这个词先有眼睛的物理扫视，后才有希望之义。"},{"no":"04","title":"Someone worth watching: the promising person","titleCN":"潜在客户、有前途的人选：值得盯住的那个人","definition":"a person or thing seen as likely to succeed, or a possible customer or candidate","definitionCN":"被认为可能成功的人或事物；潜在客户或候选人","example":"The agent spends her mornings calling new prospects.","exampleCN":"这位经纪人每天上午给新潜在客户打电话。","why":"From 1922, prospect named 'a person or thing considered promising', out of the 1660s sense of expectation of advantage. A good customer is someone in whom the seller sees a future.","whyCN":"从 1922 年起，prospect 指“被认为有前途的人或事物”，源自 17 世纪 60 年代“预期好处”的义项。好客户，就是卖方在其身上看得见未来的人。"},{"no":"05","title":"Grounds for hoping","titleCN":"预期的依据：凭什么盼着","definition":"grounds for expecting something; a reasonable basis for anticipation","definitionCN":"对某事的预期依据；合理的盼望理由","example":"The deal offers no prospect of profit this year.","exampleCN":"这笔交易今年没有获利的指望。","why":"The 1660s sense was not the hope itself but its ground: 'expectation, ground of expectation'. The landscape metaphor persists — a prospect is what the situation lets you see coming.","whyCN":"17 世纪 60 年代的义项不是希望本身，而是希望的依据：“预期、期待的依据”。风景的隐喻仍在：prospect 就是局势允许你看见的、即将到来的东西。"},{"no":"06","title":"Looking for ore: to prospect the ground","titleCN":"勘探、探矿：把地面看穿","definition":"to search an area for gold, oil, or other minerals","definitionCN":"在某地区寻找黄金、石油或其他矿藏","example":"They prospected the valley for copper throughout the summer.","exampleCN":"整个夏天他们都在那个山谷里勘探铜矿。","why":"The verb dates from 1841, from a specialized 1832 noun sense 'a spot giving prospects of ore'. The miner literally looks out over the land to see what it promises.","whyCN":"动词始于 1841 年，来自 1832 年的名词专义“有矿苗的地方”。矿工字面上就是在土地上四处张望，看它许诺了什么。"},{"no":"07","title":"Surveying the site before building","titleCN":"勘察、探测：动工之前先看一遍","definition":"to examine land or a site, especially to judge its potential or value","definitionCN":"勘查土地或场地，尤指评估其潜力或价值","example":"Engineers prospected the site before the dam was approved.","exampleCN":"大坝获批之前，工程师们勘察了坝址。","why":"English had an older verb prospect 'look forth, look out over' (1550s) from Latin prospectare, a frequentative of prospicere. The mining sense revived that old surveying gesture.","whyCN":"英语早有动词 prospect“向外看、俯瞰”（16 世纪 50 年代），来自拉丁语 prospectare，是 prospicere 的反复体。采矿义让这个古老的勘看动作重新流行。"},{"no":"08","title":"A mental survey: the wide view of a subject","titleCN":"宏观审视：把一门学问摊开来看","definition":"a broad mental view or survey of a subject, situation, or period","definitionCN":"对某一主题、局势或时期的宏观心理审视","example":"The book gives a broad prospect of a century of science.","exampleCN":"这本书对百年科学史作了宏观的审视。","why":"The transferred sense 'mental view or survey' is recorded from the 1620s. The eye's sweep over a valley becomes the mind's sweep over a field of knowledge.","whyCN":"“心中的视野/审视”这一转移义记录于 17 世纪 20 年代。眼睛扫过山谷的动作，变成了心智扫过一片知识领域。"},{"no":"09","title":"The long straight avenue","titleCN":"大街、大道：一眼望不到头的那条路","definition":"a wide, straight street or avenue, especially in a Russian city","definitionCN":"宽阔笔直的大街或大道，尤指俄罗斯城市中的","example":"Nevsky Prospect runs straight through the heart of the city.","exampleCN":"涅瓦大街笔直地穿过城市中心。","why":"In 1866 English borrowed Russian prospekt 'avenue', which itself came from Latin prospectus. A grand avenue is a street designed to give the eye a long, uninterrupted prospect.","whyCN":"1866 年英语借入俄语 prospekt“大街”，而俄语这个词又来自拉丁语 prospectus。宏伟的大道，就是一条为了让视线获得漫长而不中断的前景而设计的街。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Prospect is one of the spec- words: all of them are about looking. Latin prospicere 'look forward' gives the noun prospectus 'a distant view', and English extends the same word from landscape to expectation, to customers, and finally to mining.","cn":"prospect 是 spec- 词族的一员：它们都与“看”有关。拉丁语 prospicere“向前看”给出名词 prospectus“远处的景色”，英语再把同一个词从风景扩展到预期、客户，最后扩展到采矿。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (classical)","en":"Prospicere meant 'to look out on, look forward', built from pro 'forward' plus specere 'to look at'. Specere goes back to PIE *spek- 'to observe', a reconstruction with no written record, so that deepest layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"prospicere 意为“眺望、向前看”，由 pro“向前”加 specere“看”构成。specere 可追溯到印欧语 *spek-“观察”，但这是没有书面记录的重构，因此最深层标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"LATIN NOUN","en":"Prospectus, the past-participle stem used as a noun, meant 'distant view, look out; sight, faculty of sight'. It named both the thing seen and the power of seeing it.","cn":"prospectus 由过去分词词干用作名词，意为“远处的景色、眺望；视觉、视力”。它既指被看见之物，也指看见的能力。"},{"era":"EARLY 15c. ENGLISH","en":"The noun enters English as 'the act of looking into the distance; the condition of facing something or a certain direction'. The looking is still literal.","cn":"名词进入英语时意为“向远处看的动作；朝向某物或某个方向的状态”。这里的“看”仍是字面义。"},{"era":"1530s–1630s ENGLISH","en":"The meaning widens to 'an extensive view of the landscape' (1530s), then to 'mental view or survey' (1620s), then to 'that which is presented to the eye, a scene' (1630s).","cn":"词义先扩展为“广阔的风景视野”（16 世纪 30 年代），再扩展为“心中的审视”（17 世纪 20 年代），又扩展为“呈现于眼前之物、景象”（17 世纪 30 年代）。"},{"era":"1660s–1922 ENGLISH","en":"'Expectation, ground of expectation, especially of advantage' appears in the 1660s on the notion of looking forward. From it come 'person or thing considered promising' (1922) and the plural prospects, 'things looked forward to'.","cn":"“预期、期待的依据，尤指好处”于 17 世纪 60 年代出现，基于“向前看”的意象。由此派生出“被认为有前途的人或事物”（1922）以及复数 prospects“所期待之事”。"},{"era":"1832–1841 ENGLISH","en":"Mining uses a specialized noun sense 'a spot giving prospects of ore' (1832), and the verb 'explore for gold or minerals' follows in 1841, from prospect (n.).","cn":"采矿业先有名词专义“有矿苗的地点”（1832），动词“勘探黄金或矿物”于 1841 年随后出现，来自名词 prospect。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the spec- look or the -spect shape; the meaning group shares the idea of a future chance, but not its spelling.","cn":"形近组共享 spec-“看”或 -spect 的外形；近义组共享“未来的机会”这一概念，但拼写不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"prospectus","ipa":"/prəˈspektəs/","tag":"same root, noun ending","definition":"a printed plan describing a school, company, or proposed enterprise. It is prospect plus the Latin noun ending -us.","definitionCN":"介绍学校、公司或拟办事业的印刷章程。它就是 prospect 加上拉丁名词词尾 -us。"},{"word":"respect","ipa":"/rɪˈspekt/","tag":"re- 'back' + specere","definition":"to look back at someone with esteem. It uses the same specere 'look' but with re- 'back'.","definitionCN":"尊重；回头看某人并怀有敬意。它用同一个 specere“看”，但前缀是 re-“向后”。"},{"word":"spectator","ipa":"/spekˈteɪtə/","tag":"specere + -ator","definition":"a person who watches an event. The root is pure 'look', with no pro- 'forward'.","definitionCN":"观众；旁观者。词根是纯粹的“看”，没有 pro-“向前”。"},{"word":"perspective","ipa":"/pəˈspektɪv/","tag":"per- 'through' + specere","definition":"a way of seeing things from a particular point. It looks through a situation rather than forward.","definitionCN":"视角；透视法。它是透过一个情境去看，而不是向前看。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"outlook","ipa":"/ˈaʊtlʊk/","tag":"future view","definition":"the likely future of a situation. It is the closest everyday synonym of prospect in the sense of expectation.","definitionCN":"前景；展望。在“预期”这一义项上，它是最接近 prospect 的日常同义词。"},{"word":"likelihood","ipa":"/ˈlaɪklihʊd/","tag":"probability","definition":"the chance that something will happen. It measures probability, while prospect often adds hope or dread.","definitionCN":"可能性；或然性。它衡量概率，而 prospect 常带有希望或忧虑的色彩。"},{"word":"vista","ipa":"/ˈvɪstə/","tag":"long view","definition":"a long, wide view, especially between rows of trees. It matches the landscape sense of prospect.","definitionCN":"远景；狭长的视野，尤指树列之间的。它对应 prospect 的风景义。"},{"word":"anticipation","ipa":"/ænˌtɪsɪˈpeɪʃn/","tag":"looking forward","definition":"the act of expecting something and preparing for it. It names the mental act that prospect describes as a view.","definitionCN":"预期；期待。它命名的是 prospect 以“视野”来描绘的那种心理活动。"},{"word":"possibility","ipa":"/ˌpɒsəˈbɪləti/","tag":"may happen","definition":"something that may exist or happen. It is neutral, where prospect usually implies evaluation.","definitionCN":"可能性；可能之事。它是中性的，而 prospect 通常含有评价意味。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin specere 'to look', the spec- family, and the mining and customer senses that grew from the same gaze.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 specere“看”、spec- 词族，以及从同一道目光里长出的采矿义和客户义。"},"normal":[{"en":"prospect = pro- 'forward' + spect 'look': to look forward is to see a prospect.","cn":"prospect = pro-“向前”+ spect“看”：向前看，看见的就是前景。"},{"en":"The spec- family is all eyes: spectator, inspect, respect, perspective, circumspect.","cn":"spec- 词族全是眼睛：spectator、inspect、respect、perspective、circumspect。"},{"en":"A prospectus is the same word in a brochure: a school lets you look ahead at what it offers.","cn":"prospectus 就是同一个词做成的小册子：学校让你提前看见它能提供什么。"},{"en":"A prospector looks over the ground exactly as you look over the future.","cn":"prospector（勘探者）打量土地的样子，正像你打量未来。"},{"en":"Job prospects are literally 'things looked forward to' in the plural.","cn":"job prospects 字面上就是复数形式的“被向前看的事情”。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Future is treated as a landscape: you stand here and scan what is coming.","cn":"未来被当作一片风景：你站在此处，扫视将要到来的一切。"},{"en":"Looking and hoping are one gesture in this word; the eye and the mind share a horizon.","cn":"在这个词里，看与盼是同一个动作；眼睛和心智共享一条地平线。"},{"en":"The word travels from landscape to time to market: a view, a chance, a customer.","cn":"这个词从风景走到时间，再走到市场：一片景、一个机会、一位客户。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The prospect of moving abroad excited her more than it frightened her.","cn":"移居国外的前景让她兴奋多过害怕。"},{"en":"Geologists spent three years prospecting for oil in the desert.","cn":"地质学家在沙漠里花了三年勘探石油。"},{"en":"The sales team treats every inquiry as a potential prospect.","cn":"销售团队把每一次询价都当作潜在客户。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"pro（向前）+ spect（看）——向前看，前景就在眼前；谐音“普罗斯佩克特”：普查（pro）一遍，向前看矿藏 → prospect 前景；勘探","word":"prospect"},"root":"源自拉丁语 prospicere“向前看、眺望”，由 pro“向前”加 specere“看”构成，名词 prospectus 意为“远处的景色”；核心是“向前看所得到的那片景”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses, one gaze. The eye first sweeps a landscape, then the mind sweeps the future; what is seen becomes a chance, a customer, a subject surveyed, a street, and finally ground to be searched for ore.","cn":"九个义项，一道目光。眼睛先扫过风景，心智再扫过未来；被看见的东西依次变成机会、客户、被审视的学科、一条大街，最后成为要去地下搜寻矿藏的土地。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: standing high and looking forward — the view ahead, in space or in time.","cn":"核心意象：站在高处向前看——空间或时间中前方的那片景。"},"chain":["LOOK FORWARD","SWEEP THE LANDSCAPE","HOLD THE VIEW IN MIND","EXPECT WHAT MAY COME","SEE A CHANCE IN A PERSON","SEARCH THE GROUND"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S05","en":"THE EXPECTED FUTURE: prospect as what is anticipated, and the grounds for that anticipation.","cn":"被期待的未来：作为预期内容的前景，以及支撑这份预期的依据。"},{"senses":"S02 · S04","en":"THE CHANCE AND THE PERSON: a possibility on the horizon, and someone in whom a future is seen.","cn":"机会与人：地平线上的可能性，以及被人看见未来的人。"},{"senses":"S03 · S08","en":"THE WIDE VIEW: the landscape before the eyes, and the broad survey before the mind.","cn":"广阔视野：眼前的风景，以及心智对学科的宏观审视。"},{"senses":"S06 · S07","en":"LOOKING INTO THE EARTH: mining for ore, and surveying a site for what it may yield.","cn":"向地下看：探矿，以及为评估潜力而勘察场地。"},{"senses":"S09","en":"THE LONG AVENUE: a street built to give the eye an unbroken prospect.","cn":"长长的大道：一条为了让视线获得不中断前景而建的街。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Prospect is pro- plus spec- plus -t. Its family shows the prefix pro-, re-, per-, circum- and in-, the root spec- 'look', and the noun and agent endings -tus, -tor, -ive and -ion.","cn":"prospect 是 pro- 加 spec- 再加 -t。它的词族展示前缀 pro-、re-、per-、circum-、in-，词根 spec-“看”，以及名词与施事后缀 -tus、-tor、-ive、-ion。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin specere 'to look at' is the base of spectator, inspect and respect; with prefixes it yields prospicere, respicere, perspicere and circumspicere, and the noun prospectus.","cn":"拉丁语 specere“看”是 spectator、inspect、respect 的基础；加前缀又给出 prospicere、respicere、perspicere、circumspicere，以及名词 prospectus。"},"items":[{"word":"prospect","structure":"pro- (forward) + specere (to look) + -t (noun)","meaning":"a view ahead; expectation; to search the ground","meaningCN":"前景；预期；勘探（向前看）","example":"The prospect of promotion kept her working late.","exampleCN":"升职的前景让她一直工作到很晚。"},{"word":"inspect","structure":"in- (into) + specere (to look)","meaning":"to look closely into something","meaningCN":"检查；视察（向里看）","example":"Officials came to inspect the factory.","exampleCN":"官员们来检查这家工厂。"},{"word":"respect","structure":"re- (back) + specere (to look)","meaning":"to look back at with esteem","meaningCN":"尊重（回头看、看重）","example":"Students respect a teacher who listens.","exampleCN":"学生尊敬愿意倾听的老师。"},{"word":"spectator","structure":"spectare (to watch) + -ator (agent)","meaning":"one who watches","meaningCN":"观众；旁观者（看的人）","example":"The stadium held fifty thousand spectators.","exampleCN":"体育场容纳了五万名观众。"},{"word":"perspective","structure":"per- (through) + specere (to look) + -ive","meaning":"a way of seeing through a scene","meaningCN":"视角；透视（看穿之法）","example":"Travel gives you a new perspective on home.","exampleCN":"旅行让你对家乡有了新的视角。"},{"word":"speculate","structure":"specere (to look) + -ulate (verb)","meaning":"to look out mentally; to guess or invest","meaningCN":"推测；投机（向外看、猜）","example":"Reporters speculated about the reason for her resignation.","exampleCN":"记者们推测她辞职的原因。"},{"word":"aspect","structure":"a- (ad-, to) + specere (to look)","meaning":"the side something presents to the eye","meaningCN":"方面；外观（看过去的那一面）","example":"We discussed every aspect of the plan.","exampleCN":"我们讨论了计划的每个方面。"},{"word":"circumspect","structure":"circum- (around) + specere (to look)","meaning":"looking around before acting; cautious","meaningCN":"谨慎的（四周看遍再行动）","example":"She was circumspect in accepting the offer.","exampleCN":"她在接受这个提议时很谨慎。"},{"word":"introspection","structure":"intro- (within) + specere (to look) + -ion","meaning":"looking inward at one's own mind","meaningCN":"内省（向内看）","example":"His diary is a record of quiet introspection.","exampleCN":"他的日记是一份安静内省的记录。"},{"word":"prospectus","structure":"prospectus (Latin noun from prospicere)","meaning":"a printed plan that lets you look ahead","meaningCN":"章程；招股书（让人预先看清全貌）","example":"The university's prospectus lists every course.","exampleCN":"这所大学的章程列出了每一门课程。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"specere","structure":"specere (verb)","meaning":"to look at, observe","meaningCN":"看；观察"},{"word":"prospicere","structure":"pro- + specere","meaning":"to look forward, look out on","meaningCN":"向前看；眺望"}]}},{"word":"protocol","ipa_uk":"/ˈprəʊtəkɒl/","ipa_us":"/ˈproʊtəkɔːl/","definition_zh":"协议；礼仪；规程；实验方案；计算机协议","definition_en":"the first sheet of a document, and by extension the formal rules — diplomatic, scientific, medical, or digital — that govern how people and machines deal with one another","core_image":"一卷羊皮纸的开头贴着一张写满条目的小纸片，规定这份文件如何被读、被签、被遵守","scene":"A junior diplomat is told: Follow protocol, sign in the right order, and never speak before the ambassador.","sceneCN":"这里 protocol 是「礼仪、礼节」（第 2 个义项：外交或仪式中公认的正式行为与位次规则）；句意：按礼节来，按顺序签字，绝不要抢在大使之前发言。画面里有长桌、座椅次序和一份摊开的文件。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"协议；议定书；礼仪；规程；实验方案；（计算机）协议"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"diplomatic protocol","zh":"外交礼节"},{"phrase":"follow protocol","zh":"遵守规程"},{"phrase":"safety protocol","zh":"安全规程"},{"phrase":"research protocol","zh":"研究方案"},{"phrase":"network protocol","zh":"网络协议"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"protocols"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"protocolar","pos":"adj.","zh":"礼仪的；协议的（较少用）"},{"word":"protocolist","pos":"n.","zh":"礼宾官；协议起草者（罕用）"},{"word":"protocolize","pos":"v.","zh":"使规程化；将……纳入协议（技术用语）"},{"word":"protocolled","pos":"adj.","zh":"已记入议定书的（英式拼写）"},{"word":"protocolling","pos":"n.","zh":"记录议定书；按规程处理"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The treaty on paper: a formal agreement","titleCN":"协议、议定书：写在纸上的正式约定","definition":"a formal agreement or treaty, especially one between states or organizations","definitionCN":"正式的协议或条约，尤指国家或组织之间的","example":"The two governments signed a protocol on border patrols.","exampleCN":"两国政府签署了一份关于边境巡逻的议定书。","why":"From the 1540s sense 'draft of a document, original of any writing', a protocol became the official record of a transaction. When that record is signed by friendly powers, the sheet of paper is the agreement itself.","whyCN":"从 16 世纪 40 年代“文件草稿、任何文书的原件”这一义项起，protocol 成为交易的官方记录。当这份记录由友好国家签署，那张纸本身就是协议。"},{"no":"02","title":"The order of the room: diplomatic etiquette","titleCN":"礼仪、礼节：房间里谁先谁后","definition":"the accepted rules of formal behavior and precedence in diplomacy or ceremony","definitionCN":"外交或仪式中公认的正式行为与位次规则","example":"The young attaché was criticized for breaking protocol.","exampleCN":"那位年轻随员因违反礼节而受到批评。","why":"French extended the word to 'formula of diplomatic etiquette', attested in English by 1896. The first sheet of a treaty recorded the order of ceremony, so the sheet became the order itself.","whyCN":"法语把这个词扩展为“外交礼仪的程式”，1896 年在英语中出现。条约的首张贴纸记录仪式次序，于是那张纸就变成了次序本身。"},{"no":"03","title":"The prescribed steps: an operating procedure","titleCN":"规程：一步一步照做的那套规矩","definition":"an official procedure or set of rules for carrying out a task","definitionCN":"执行某项任务的官方程序或规则","example":"Staff must follow the safety protocol when handling chemicals.","exampleCN":"员工处理化学品时必须遵守安全规程。","why":"Once protocol means the official record of how something is done, it easily means the prescribed way to do it. The written order of a ceremony becomes the written order of any operation.","whyCN":"一旦 protocol 指“某事如何进行的官方记录”，它就很容易指“规定的进行方式”。仪式的书面次序，变成了任何操作的书面次序。"},{"no":"04","title":"The plan of the experiment","titleCN":"实验方案：写在前面的研究步骤","definition":"a detailed written plan for a scientific experiment or clinical trial","definitionCN":"科学实验或临床试验的详细书面计划","example":"The trial protocol specifies doses, check-ups and stopping rules.","exampleCN":"试验方案规定了剂量、检查和终止规则。","why":"Science keeps the old 'draft, minutes' sense alive: before anything is done, the plan is written down on the first sheet. A protocol is the document that tells the researcher what may be done.","whyCN":"科学保留了古老的“草稿、记录”义：在做任何事之前，计划先被写在首页上。方案就是告诉研究者可以做什么的那份文件。"},{"no":"05","title":"Rules between machines: the computer protocol","titleCN":"计算机协议：机器之间的外交礼节","definition":"a set of rules governing how data is exchanged between computers or devices","definitionCN":"规定计算机或设备之间如何交换数据的规则集合","example":"HTTP is the protocol your browser uses to fetch a web page.","exampleCN":"HTTP 是浏览器抓取网页时使用的协议。","why":"Computers need the same thing diplomats need: an agreed order for who speaks first and how a message is acknowledged. The 20c technical sense borrows the word for rules of exchange.","whyCN":"计算机需要的东西与外交官相同：约定谁先发言、消息如何确认的次序。20 世纪的技术义借用了这个表示“交换规则”的词。"},{"no":"06","title":"The first sheet: original draft and minutes","titleCN":"原始记录、草案：贴在卷首的那张纸","definition":"the original draft of a document, or the minutes of a transaction (now obsolete)","definitionCN":"文件的原始草稿，或交易的会议记录（现已废弃）","example":"The clerk kept the protocol of the negotiations in a leather ledger.","exampleCN":"书记员把谈判的原始记录保存在一本皮面账册里。","why":"Greek prōtokollon literally meant 'first sheet glued onto a manuscript', where the contents were listed. English took it in the 1540s as the draft or minutes — the literal sheet before the finished text.","whyCN":"希腊语 prōtokollon 字面就是“贴在文稿上的第一张纸”，上面列着目录。英语在 16 世纪 40 年代借入时指草稿或会议记录——成文之前的那张实指纸片。"},{"no":"07","title":"The standard treatment plan","titleCN":"治疗方案：医院里的标准流程","definition":"a standard plan for treating a particular illness or condition","definitionCN":"治疗某种疾病或状况的标准方案","example":"Patients on the new protocol showed fewer side effects.","exampleCN":"采用新治疗方案的患者副作用更少。","why":"Medicine borrowed the research-protocol sense and applied it to care: a fixed sequence of tests and drugs that every patient on the plan receives.","whyCN":"医学借用了研究方案的义项，并把它用到治疗上：一套固定的检查与用药顺序，凡进入该方案的患者都照此接受。"},{"no":"08","title":"The diplomatic instrument","titleCN":"外交文书：正式归档的那份文件","definition":"a formal diplomatic document, especially one recording an agreement or understanding","definitionCN":"正式的外交文件，尤指记录某项协议或谅解的文件","example":"The protocol was deposited with the foreign ministry.","exampleCN":"这份议定书已交存外交部。","why":"In 19c diplomacy, protocol named the document signed by friendly powers to secure certain ends by peaceful means. It is the treaty sense given a formal, archival body.","whyCN":"在 19 世纪外交中，protocol 指友好国家为以和平方式实现某些目标而签署的文件。它是条约义项获得了正式、可归档的形体。"},{"no":"09","title":"Precedence at a state occasion","titleCN":"礼宾次序：国事场合的座次表","definition":"the order of precedence and ceremony observed on formal state or institutional occasions","definitionCN":"正式国事或机构场合所遵循的位次与仪式次序","example":"Seating followed strict protocol, with the dean at the head of the table.","exampleCN":"座次遵循严格的礼宾次序，院长坐在长桌首位。","why":"The etiquette sense widened from diplomacy to any formal hierarchy. Who walks in first, who sits where — the old first sheet still dictates the order of the room.","whyCN":"礼仪义从外交扩展到任何正式等级场合。谁先入场、谁坐哪里——那张古老的首张贴纸仍在规定房间里的次序。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Protocol begins as bookbinding: a sheet of contents glued to the front of a manuscript. From that 'first sheet' come the draft, the official record, the treaty, the etiquette of diplomats, the plan of an experiment, and finally the rules that let computers talk.","cn":"protocol 起于书籍装订：一张目录纸贴在文稿卷首。从这张“首张贴纸”衍生出草稿、官方记录、条约、外交礼节、实验方案，最后是让计算机彼此交谈的规则。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK (ancient)","en":"Prōtokollon meant 'first sheet glued onto a manuscript', from prōtos 'first' plus kolla 'glue'. The origin of kolla itself is uncertain, so that element is marked source uncertain.","cn":"prōtokollon 意为“贴在文稿上的第一张纸”，由 prōtos“第一”加 kolla“胶水”构成。kolla 本身的来源不确定，因此这一成分标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN (13c.)","en":"Protocollum meant 'draft', literally 'the first sheet of a volume', on which contents and errata were written. The physical sheet becomes a textual record.","cn":"protocollum 意为“草稿”，字面是“一卷书的第一张纸”，上面写着目录和勘误。实指的纸片变成了文本记录。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (c. 1200)","en":"Prothocole passed into French, where the sense developed from 'rough draft; original copy of a treaty' to 'official record of a transaction' to 'diplomatic document'.","cn":"prothocole 传入法语，词义从“粗略草稿、条约原件”发展为“交易的官方记录”，再发展为“外交文件”。"},{"era":"MID-15c. ENGLISH","en":"English first records prothogol 'prologue' (mid-15c.), then prothogall 'draft of a document, minutes of a transaction, original of any writing' (1540s). These senses are now obsolete.","cn":"英语最早记录 prothogol“序言”（15 世纪中），随后记录 prothogall“文件草稿、交易记录、任何文书的原件”（16 世纪 40 年代）。这些义项今已废弃。"},{"era":"17c.–1896 ENGLISH","en":"'Diplomatic document signed by friendly powers' develops through the 17c.–19c.; the French sense 'formula of diplomatic etiquette' is attested in English by 1896.","cn":"“友好国家签署的外交文件”一义在 17 至 19 世纪发展起来；法语“外交礼仪程式”这一义项于 1896 年在英语中出现。"},{"era":"20c. ENGLISH","en":"'Conventional proper conduct' is recorded from 1952. The technical sense 'rules for exchanging data between computers' arose in the 20c. as engineers borrowed the idea of an agreed order of exchange.","cn":"“约定俗成的得体举止”记录于 1952 年。技术义“计算机之间交换数据的规则”在 20 世纪出现，工程师们借用了“约定的交换次序”这一观念。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the proto- opening but differs in the second element; the meaning group shares the idea of rules or formal agreement, not the shape.","cn":"形近组共享 proto- 开头，但第二成分不同；近义组共享“规则或正式约定”的概念，而非外形。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"prototype","ipa":"/ˈprəʊtətaɪp/","tag":"proto- + type","definition":"a first model from which later versions are developed. It shares proto- 'first' but ends in -type, not -col.","definitionCN":"原型；最初模型。它共享 proto-“第一”，但词尾是 -type，不是 -col。"},{"word":"protocell","ipa":"/ˈprəʊtəsel/","tag":"proto- + cell","definition":"a hypothetical first cell. It looks like protocol but its second element is 'cell'.","definitionCN":"原始细胞（假想中的最初细胞）。它形似 protocol，但第二成分是“细胞”。"},{"word":"proton","ipa":"/ˈprəʊtɒn/","tag":"proto- + -on","definition":"a positively charged particle in the nucleus. The word means 'the first one', with no 'glue' element.","definitionCN":"质子。这个词意为“第一个”，没有“胶水”这一成分。"},{"word":"prologue","ipa":"/ˈprəʊlɒɡ/","tag":"pro- + logos","definition":"the opening of a play or book. It also means 'first speech', but from logos rather than kolla.","definitionCN":"序言；开场白。它也指“最先的话”，但来自 logos 而非 kolla。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"agreement","ipa":"/əˈɡriːmənt/","tag":"general pact","definition":"an arrangement people accept. It is broader and less formal than a protocol.","definitionCN":"协议；一致意见。它比 protocol 更宽泛、更不正式。"},{"word":"etiquette","ipa":"/ˈetɪket/","tag":"social rules","definition":"the conventional rules of polite behavior. It matches protocol's ceremonial sense.","definitionCN":"礼节；礼仪。它对应 protocol 的仪式义。"},{"word":"procedure","ipa":"/prəˈsiːdʒə/","tag":"steps to follow","definition":"an established way of doing something. It matches protocol as an operating sequence.","definitionCN":"程序；步骤。它对应 protocol 作为操作流程的义项。"},{"word":"convention","ipa":"/kənˈvenʃn/","tag":"accepted custom","definition":"a widely accepted custom or practice. It is unwritten where protocol is often written.","definitionCN":"惯例；公约。它常是不成文的，而 protocol 常是成文的。"},{"word":"treaty","ipa":"/ˈtriːti/","tag":"formal state pact","definition":"a formal written agreement between states. It is the legal core of protocol sense 01.","definitionCN":"条约。它是 protocol 第 1 义项的法律核心。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Greek kolla 'glue', prōtokollon 'first sheet', and the modern protocol stack that keeps machines in order.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：希腊语 kolla“胶水”、prōtokollon“首张贴纸”，以及让机器守秩序的现代协议栈。"},"normal":[{"en":"proto- 'first' + kollon 'glue': the first sheet glued to the scroll — protocol.","cn":"proto-“第一”+ kollon“胶水”：贴在卷首的第一张纸——protocol。"},{"en":"The first sheet listed contents, so protocol came to mean the plan and the record.","cn":"首张贴纸列着目录，所以 protocol 后来既指方案也指记录。"},{"en":"Diplomatic protocol is a treaty's first page turned into behaviour.","cn":"外交礼节就是条约的第一页变成了行为举止。"},{"en":"A lab protocol is the first sheet of an experiment, written before anyone starts.","cn":"实验室方案就是实验的首张贴纸，在任何人动手之前写好。"},{"en":"A network protocol is etiquette for machines: who speaks, in what order, and how to reply.","cn":"网络协议就是机器的礼节：谁先说、按什么次序、如何回应。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"One idea runs through all senses: an agreed order written at the front and then obeyed.","cn":"一个观念贯穿所有义项：写在最前面、随后被遵守的约定次序。"},{"en":"The word moves from paper to people to machines without changing its logic.","cn":"这个词从纸面走到人，再走到机器，逻辑始终没变。"},{"en":"Protocol is the price of cooperation: someone must go first, and everyone must know it.","cn":"协议是合作的代价：总得有人先来，而所有人都得知道这一点。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The Kyoto Protocol set binding targets for greenhouse gases.","cn":"《京都议定书》为温室气体设定了有约束力的目标。"},{"en":"Nurses check the protocol before administering a new drug.","cn":"护士在给新药之前会核对规程。"},{"en":"The two networks could not talk because they used different protocols.","cn":"这两个网络因使用不同的协议而无法通信。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"proto（第一）+ col（胶水）——贴在卷首的第一张纸，写着规矩；谐音“普罗托科尔”：先（pro）把规矩贴在开头，大家照做 → protocol 协议；礼仪","word":"protocol"},"root":"源自希腊语 prōtokollon“贴在文稿卷首的第一张纸”，由 prōtos“第一”加 kolla“胶水”构成，经中世纪拉丁语 protocollum 与古法语进入英语；核心是“写在前头、必须遵守的次序”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses built on one physical thing: the first sheet glued to a document. That sheet held the contents and the order, so protocol became draft, record, treaty, etiquette, procedure, experiment plan, treatment plan, and the rules by which computers exchange data.","cn":"九个义项都建筑在同一个实物上：贴在文件卷首的第一张纸。那张纸写着目录与次序，于是 protocol 依次成为草稿、记录、条约、礼节、规程、实验方案、治疗方案，以及计算机交换数据的规则。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: the first sheet glued to the front of a scroll, listing the order of what follows.","cn":"核心意象：贴在卷首的第一张纸，列明后续内容的次序。"},"chain":["GLUE THE FIRST SHEET","WRITE THE CONTENTS","KEEP THE OFFICIAL RECORD","SIGN THE TREATY","OBSERVE THE CEREMONY","OBEY THE RULES"],"branches":[{"senses":"S06 · S01","en":"THE DOCUMENT: the original draft and minutes, and the formal agreement they grow into.","cn":"文书：原始草稿与会议记录，以及由此长成的正式协议。"},{"senses":"S02 · S09","en":"THE ORDER OF PEOPLE: diplomatic etiquette and the precedence observed at state occasions.","cn":"人的次序：外交礼节，以及国事场合遵循的位次。"},{"senses":"S03 · S04 · S07","en":"THE WRITTEN PLAN: operating procedures, experiment protocols and standard treatment plans.","cn":"书面方案：操作规程、实验方案与标准治疗方案。"},{"senses":"S08","en":"THE INSTRUMENT: the formal diplomatic document deposited with a ministry.","cn":"正式文书：交存外交部的正式外交文件。"},{"senses":"S05","en":"THE RULES OF EXCHANGE: the protocol that lets machines speak to one another.","cn":"交换规则：让机器彼此交谈的协议。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Protocol is proto- plus koll- plus -on. Its family shows the Greek prefix prōto- 'first' and the glue-root kolla, which also reaches English through collage and collagen.","cn":"protocol 是 proto- 加 koll- 再加 -on。它的词族展示希腊前缀 prōto-“第一”与“胶水”词根 kolla，后者也通过 collage、collagen 进入英语。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek prōtos 'first' yields the combining form proto-; Greek kolla 'glue' is the base of protocol, collage and collagen, though the deeper origin of kolla is uncertain.","cn":"希腊语 prōtos“第一”给出构词成分 proto-；希腊语 kolla“胶水”是 protocol、collage、collagen 的基础，不过 kolla 更深层的来源不确定。"},"items":[{"word":"protocol","structure":"proto- (first) + kolla (glue) + -on (noun)","meaning":"the first sheet glued on; rules and records","meaningCN":"协议；礼仪；规程（首张贴纸）","example":"The hospital follows a strict protocol for infection control.","exampleCN":"这家医院遵循严格的感染控制规程。"},{"word":"prototype","structure":"proto- (first) + typos (impression, model)","meaning":"a first model","meaningCN":"原型；最初模型","example":"The team built a prototype before mass production.","exampleCN":"团队在大规模生产之前造了一个原型。"},{"word":"protagonist","structure":"proto- (first) + agōnistēs (contestant)","meaning":"the first actor; the leading character","meaningCN":"主角；首要人物","example":"The protagonist narrates the whole novel.","exampleCN":"主角叙述了整部小说。"},{"word":"protozoa","structure":"proto- (first) + zōia (animals)","meaning":"the 'first animals'; single-celled organisms","meaningCN":"原生动物（“最初的动物”）","example":"Protozoa live in pond water.","exampleCN":"原生动物生活在池水中。"},{"word":"proton","structure":"proto- (first) + -on (particle)","meaning":"the 'first' particle in the nucleus","meaningCN":"质子（核中的“第一个”粒子）","example":"A proton carries a positive charge.","exampleCN":"质子带正电荷。"},{"word":"protoplasm","structure":"proto- (first) + plasma (formed thing)","meaning":"the original living substance of a cell","meaningCN":"原生质（细胞的原初生命物质）","example":"Early biologists studied the protoplasm of cells.","exampleCN":"早期生物学家研究细胞的原生质。"},{"word":"protohistory","structure":"proto- (first, before) + history","meaning":"the period just before written history","meaningCN":"原史时期（有文字记载之前的那一段）","example":"Protohistory covers cultures that left no writing.","exampleCN":"原史时期涵盖没有留下文字的文化。"},{"word":"collage","structure":"kolla (glue) + -age (French noun)","meaning":"a picture made by gluing pieces together","meaningCN":"拼贴画（把碎片粘在一起）","example":"The artist made a collage from old photographs.","exampleCN":"这位艺术家用旧照片做了一幅拼贴画。"},{"word":"collagen","structure":"kolla (glue) + -gen (producing)","meaning":"the protein that 'produces glue' in skin and bone","meaningCN":"胶原蛋白（生胶之物）","example":"Collagen keeps the skin firm.","exampleCN":"胶原蛋白让皮肤紧致。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"prōtos","structure":"prōtos (adjective)","meaning":"first","meaningCN":"第一的"},{"word":"kolla","structure":"kolla (noun)","meaning":"glue","meaningCN":"胶水（来源不确定）"}]}},{"word":"psychology","ipa_uk":"/saɪˈkɒlədʒi/","ipa_us":"/saɪˈkɑːlədʒi/","definition_zh":"心理学；心理；心理状态；心理战；洞察人心的策略","definition_en":"the study of the soul and then of the mind, and by extension the mental life of a person or group and the practical art of reading it","core_image":"一个人俯身倾听自己胸腔里的呼吸，试图从那口看不见的气息里读出心灵的模样","scene":"A coach leans toward a nervous player and says: I'm not a therapist, but a little psychology won't hurt — I know how your mind works before a final.","sceneCN":"这里 psychology 是「心理/洞察人心的策略」（第 5 个义项，兼含第 2 个义项）；句意：我不是心理医生，但用一点心理学不会有害——我知道你在决赛前心里怎么想。画面里有场边、毛巾和低着头的球员。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"心理学；心理；心理状态；心理战术"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"child psychology","zh":"儿童心理学"},{"phrase":"reverse psychology","zh":"反向心理（欲擒故纵）"},{"phrase":"the psychology of","zh":"……的心理"},{"phrase":"a degree in psychology","zh":"心理学学位"},{"phrase":"psychological warfare","zh":"心理战（同族形容词搭配）"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"psychologies"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"psychological","pos":"adj.","zh":"心理的；心理学的"},{"word":"psychologist","pos":"n.","zh":"心理学家"},{"word":"psychometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"心理测量的"},{"word":"psychologize","pos":"v.","zh":"作心理学解释；用心理分析"},{"word":"psychologism","pos":"n.","zh":"心理主义（用心理事实解释一切的倾向）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The science of the mind","titleCN":"心理学：研究心灵的那门科学","definition":"the scientific study of the mind and behavior","definitionCN":"对心理与行为的科学研究","example":"She studied psychology to understand how memory works.","exampleCN":"她学习心理学，以理解记忆如何运作。","why":"The word is recorded in the 1650s as 'the study of the soul', from Modern Latin psychologia, probably coined in Germany in the mid-16c. By 1748 it meant the science of mental phenomena; by the early 1890s, a behavioral science.","whyCN":"这个词在 17 世纪 50 年代记录为“对灵魂的研究”，来自新拉丁语 psychologia，很可能是 16 世纪中在德国造出的。到 1748 年它指“心理现象的科学”，到 19 世纪 90 年代初成为行为科学。"},{"no":"02","title":"The mind of a person: mental makeup","titleCN":"心理、心理状态：一个人心里的那套构造","definition":"the mental and emotional makeup of a person or group","definitionCN":"个人或群体的心理与情感构成","example":"The psychology of the crowd turned angry within minutes.","exampleCN":"人群的心理在几分钟内变得愤怒。","why":"The name of the discipline slid over to its object. If psychology is the study of the mind, 'the psychology of X' is the mind of X — the thing studied rather than the study.","whyCN":"学科名滑向了它的研究对象。如果 psychology 是研究心灵的学问，那么“X 的 psychology”就是 X 的心灵——是研究对象，而不是研究本身。"},{"no":"03","title":"Weapons of the mind: psychological warfare","titleCN":"心理战：不动枪炮，先动人心","definition":"the use of propaganda, threats, or staged information to weaken an enemy's morale","definitionCN":"利用宣传、威胁或安排好的信息削弱敌方士气","example":"The leaflets were pure psychology: they made the enemy doubt itself.","exampleCN":"那些传单纯粹是心理战：它们让敌人开始怀疑自己。","why":"Psychological warfare is recorded in the early 20c.; in compounds and headlines the adjective is clipped, so psychology alone can name the campaign that attacks morale rather than bodies.","whyCN":"psychological warfare 记录于 20 世纪初；在复合词和标题里形容词常被省略，于是 psychology 本身就能指那场攻击士气而非身体的行动。"},{"no":"04","title":"A school of thought: one system among many","titleCN":"心理学体系、学派：一家之言","definition":"a particular system or school of psychological theory","definitionCN":"某一特定的心理学理论体系或学派","example":"Freudian psychology dominated the clinic for decades.","exampleCN":"弗洛伊德心理学在诊所里主导了数十年。","why":"-logia means 'study of', but a named body of doctrine also takes the name: Jungian psychology, cognitive psychology. The discipline splits into psychologies, each with its own mind-model.","whyCN":"-logia 意为“对……的研究”，但一套有名字的学说也沿用这个名称：荣格心理学、认知心理学。学科分裂成多种 psychology，每一种都有自己的心灵模型。"},{"no":"05","title":"Reading people: practical psychology","titleCN":"洞察人心：能当场用的那点心理学","definition":"a shrewd practical understanding of how people think, used to persuade or calm them","definitionCN":"对他人如何思考的敏锐实际理解，用来说服或安抚他人","example":"The coach used a little psychology to settle the team before the final.","exampleCN":"教练用了点心理策略，让球队在决赛前平静下来。","why":"When theory is applied in the moment, 'psychology' becomes a skill rather than a science: knowing which word will move a person. The abstract noun turns into a countable trick.","whyCN":"当理论被当场应用时，psychology 就成了技能而非科学：知道哪个词能打动一个人。这个抽象名词于是变成了可数的小手段。"},{"no":"06","title":"The empirical science of behavior","titleCN":"行为科学：从实验里长出的那门学问","definition":"the modern empirical science of behavior, especially since the 1890s","definitionCN":"现代的经验性行为科学，尤指 19 世纪 90 年代以来","example":"Modern psychology relies on controlled experiments and statistics.","exampleCN":"现代心理学依赖受控实验和统计。","why":"The behavioral-sciences sense is dated to the early 1890s. Laboratories replaced the armchair: the soul was no longer the object — measurable behavior was.","whyCN":"行为科学义可追溯到 19 世纪 90 年代初。实验室取代了扶手椅：研究对象不再是灵魂，而是可测量的行为。"},{"no":"07","title":"The old study of the soul","titleCN":"灵魂学：这个词最初的意思","definition":"the original 1650s sense: the study of the soul or spirit","definitionCN":"17 世纪 50 年代的本义：对灵魂或精神的研究","example":"Early psychology was closer to theology than to statistics.","exampleCN":"早期心理学更接近神学，而不是统计学。","why":"Greek psykhē meant 'breath, spirit, soul', and -logia 'study of'. Before the mind was measured, it was the breath-like soul that the word set out to study.","whyCN":"希腊语 psykhē 意为“呼吸、精神、灵魂”，-logia 意为“研究”。在心智被测量之前，这个词要研究的是那口气息般的灵魂。"},{"no":"08","title":"The mind of a group: consumer and social psychology","titleCN":"群体心理：一群人共享的那颗心","definition":"the mental processes of a group, market, or public considered as a subject of study","definitionCN":"作为一个研究对象的群体、市场或公众的心理过程","example":"The psychology of consumers shapes every advertising campaign.","exampleCN":"消费者的心理塑造着每一场广告活动。","why":"'The psychology of X' extends the discipline to any collective mind. Advertising, politics and sport all borrow the laboratory's name for the crowd's inner life.","whyCN":"“X 的 psychology”把学科扩展到任何集体心智。广告、政治和体育都借实验室的名字，来指人群的内心生活。"},{"no":"09","title":"Inner life in a story","titleCN":"人物心理：小说里被写出来的内心","definition":"the inner mental life of a character or work as revealed in art and literature","definitionCN":"艺术与文学中所揭示的人物或作品的内心生活","example":"The novel's psychology is revealed through small gestures, not speeches.","exampleCN":"这部小说的心理是通过细小动作而非言谈揭示的。","why":"Critics borrowed the discipline's name for what a text shows of the mind. The psychology of a character is the mind the writer has built, studied as if from outside.","whyCN":"评论家借用了学科名，指文本所展示的心灵。人物的 psychology 就是作者建造的那颗心，像从外部一样被研究。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Psychology starts as the study of the soul, not the brain. Greek psykhē 'breath, spirit' plus -logia 'study of' produced a Modern Latin coinage of the 16c.; English took it in the 1650s, and the object shifted from soul to mind to measurable behavior.","cn":"psychology 起初研究的是灵魂，不是大脑。希腊语 psykhē“呼吸、精神”加 -logia“对……的研究”造出一个 16 世纪的新拉丁语词；英语在 17 世纪 50 年代借入，研究对象从灵魂转到心智，再转到可测量的行为。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK (ancient)","en":"Psykhē meant 'breath, spirit, soul, life', probably akin to psykhein 'to blow, breathe'. The deeper PIE *bhes- 'to blow' is a reconstruction with no written record, so that layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"psykhē 意为“呼吸、精神、灵魂、生命”，可能与 psykhein“吹、呼吸”同源。更深的印欧语 *bhes-“吹”是没有书面记录的重构，因此该层标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"GREEK","en":"-Logia 'study of' comes from logos 'word, reason, account'. A psychology is literally an account of the soul.","cn":"-logia“对……的研究”来自 logos“言词、理性、论述”。一门 psychology 字面上就是“关于灵魂的论述”。"},{"era":"MODERN LATIN (mid-16c.)","en":"Psychologia was probably coined in Germany in the mid-16c., attributed to Melanchthon. It joined the Latinized Greek psykhē to -logia.","cn":"psychologia 很可能是 16 世纪中在德国造出的，常归于梅兰希顿。它把拉丁化的希腊语 psykhē 与 -logia 结合。"},{"era":"1650s ENGLISH","en":"The word enters English as 'the study of the soul'. The soul, not behavior, is the first object of the new discipline.","cn":"这个词进入英语时意为“对灵魂的研究”。新学科最初的对象是灵魂，而不是行为。"},{"era":"1748 ENGLISH","en":"The meaning 'science or study of the phenomena of the mind' is attested by 1748, in reference to Christian Wolff's Psychologia empirica (1732).","cn":"“研究心理现象的科学”这一义项于 1748 年出现，指的是克里斯蒂安·沃尔夫的《经验心理学》（1732）。"},{"era":"EARLY 1890s ENGLISH","en":"The modern behavioral-sciences sense dates from the early 1890s, when laboratories and statistics redefined what counted as the mind's evidence.","cn":"现代行为科学义可追溯到 19 世纪 90 年代初，那时实验室与统计重新定义了什么才算心灵的证据。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the psych- or -ology shape but belongs to different roots; the meaning group shares the study or the mind itself.","cn":"形近组共享 psych- 或 -ology 的外形，但属于不同词根；近义组共享“研究”或“心灵本身”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"psychiatry","ipa":"/saɪˈkaɪətri/","tag":"psych- + iatreia 'healing'","definition":"the branch of medicine that treats mental illness. It shares psych- but ends in 'healing', not 'study'.","definitionCN":"治疗精神疾病的医学分支。它共享 psych-，但词尾是“治疗”而非“研究”。"},{"word":"physiology","ipa":"/ˌfɪziˈɒlədʒi/","tag":"-ology but physio-","definition":"the study of how living bodies work. It looks like psychology but its root is physis 'nature'.","definitionCN":"生理学；研究活体如何运作。它形似 psychology，但词根是 physis“自然”。"},{"word":"psychopathy","ipa":"/saɪˈkɒpəθi/","tag":"psych- + pathos 'suffering'","definition":"a personality disorder marked by lack of empathy. It shares psych- but ends in 'suffering'.","definitionCN":"以缺乏共情为特征的人格障碍。它共享 psych-，但词尾是“痛苦”。"},{"word":"psychologist","ipa":"/saɪˈkɒlədʒɪst/","tag":"psychology + -ist","definition":"a person who studies the mind. It is the same word plus the agent suffix -ist.","definitionCN":"心理学家。它是同一个词加上施事后缀 -ist。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"psychiatry","ipa":"/saɪˈkaɪətri/","tag":"medical treatment","definition":"the medical specialty that diagnoses and treats mental illness. It is clinical where psychology is academic.","definitionCN":"诊断与治疗精神疾病的医学专科。它偏临床，而 psychology 偏学术。"},{"word":"mind","ipa":"/maɪnd/","tag":"the object itself","definition":"the seat of thought, feeling and memory. It is the thing psychology studies, not the study.","definitionCN":"思想、情感与记忆的所在。它是心理学研究的对象，而不是研究本身。"},{"word":"mentality","ipa":"/menˈtæləti/","tag":"way of thinking","definition":"a person's or group's characteristic way of thinking. It matches the 'psychology of X' sense.","definitionCN":"个人或群体特有的思维方式。它对应“X 的 psychology”这一义项。"},{"word":"psychoanalysis","ipa":"/ˌsaɪkəʊəˈnæləsɪs/","tag":"Freudian method","definition":"the therapeutic method founded by Freud for exploring the unconscious. It is one school within psychology.","definitionCN":"弗洛伊德创立、用于探索无意识的治疗方法。它是心理学内部的一个学派。"},{"word":"behavior","ipa":"/bɪˈheɪvjə/","tag":"observable action","definition":"observable action and conduct. It is the evidence that modern psychology prefers to the soul.","definitionCN":"可观察的行动与举止。它是现代心理学取代灵魂之后所偏好的证据。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Greek psykhē 'soul, breath', the -logia 'study' ending, and the modern split into psychiatry and psychoanalysis.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：希腊语 psykhē“灵魂、呼吸”、-logia“研究”词尾，以及现代分出的 psychiatry 与 psychoanalysis。"},"normal":[{"en":"psychology = psyche 'soul' + -logy 'study': first the soul, later the mind.","cn":"psychology = psyche“灵魂”+ -logy“研究”：先研究灵魂，后研究心智。"},{"en":"Psyche was also the Greek girl loved by Eros, often drawn with butterfly wings — a soul with wings.","cn":"Psyche 还是希腊神话中被厄洛斯所爱的少女，常被画上蝶翼——一个长了翅膀的灵魂。"},{"en":"Psychiatry treats the sick mind; psychology studies the mind in general. Same psyche, different second half.","cn":"psychiatry 治疗生病的心智；psychology 研究一般的心智。同一个 psyche，后半截不同。"},{"en":"A psychologist is a psychologist; a psychiatrist is a doctor. The -ist and the -iatrist tell you.","cn":"psychologist 是心理学家；psychiatrist 是精神科医生。-ist 与 -iatrist 告诉你区别。"},{"en":"Reverse psychology works because knowing the mind is already half of controlling it.","cn":"反向心理之所以有效，是因为了解心智已经是控制它的一半。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word is a mirror: it names both the study and the thing studied.","cn":"这个词是一面镜子：它既命名研究，也命名被研究之物。"},{"en":"It travels inward: from soul, to mind, to behavior, to the mind of a crowd.","cn":"它一路向内：从灵魂，到心智，到行为，再到人群的心。"},{"en":"Psychology is breath made legible: something invisible, turned into something you can describe.","cn":"心理学是把呼吸变得可读：某种看不见的东西，被转写成可以描述的东西。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"He took a course in psychology and started noticing his own habits.","cn":"他上了一门心理学课程，开始注意到自己的习惯。"},{"en":"The marketing team studies the psychology of impulse buying.","cn":"营销团队研究冲动购物的心理。"},{"en":"Using reverse psychology on a stubborn child often backfires.","cn":"对固执的孩子使用反向心理，常常适得其反。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"psycho（心理）+ logy（学科）——研究心理的学问；谐音“赛可乐鸡”：赛前（psy）喝可乐（cho）吃鸡，琢磨对手心里想什么 → psychology 心理学；心理","word":"psychology"},"root":"源自希腊语 psykhē“呼吸、灵魂、心灵”加 -logia“对……的研究”，经新拉丁语 psychologia 进入英语；核心是“对那口看不见的气息——灵魂与心智——的探究”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses around one object: the invisible mind. The word begins as the study of the soul, becomes the science of mental phenomena, then the mind of a person or crowd, a school of theory, a practical trick, a wartime weapon, and finally the inner life a novel reveals.","cn":"九个义项围绕同一个对象：看不见的心智。这个词从“研究灵魂”开始，变成“研究心理现象的科学”，再指个人或群体的心理、一个理论学派、一种实用手段、一件战时武器，最后指小说所揭示的内心生活。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: leaning inward to listen to the breath-like mind and describe what it is doing.","cn":"核心意象：向内俯身，倾听那口气息般的心智，并描述它在做什么。"},"chain":["BREATHE, LIVE","NAME THE SOUL","STUDY THE MIND","MEASURE BEHAVIOR","READ A PERSON","SHAPE A CROWD"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S06 · S07","en":"THE DISCIPLINE: its birth as soul-study, its 1748 mind-science, and its 1890s behavioral form.","cn":"学科：作为灵魂研究的诞生、1748 年的心理科学，以及 1890 年代的行为科学形态。"},{"senses":"S02 · S08 · S09","en":"THE MIND ITSELF: a person's makeup, a group's inner life, and a character's inner life in art.","cn":"心智本身：个人的心理构成、群体的内心生活，以及艺术中人物的内心。"},{"senses":"S04","en":"THE SCHOOL: one theory-system among many, each with its own model of the mind.","cn":"学派：众多理论体系中的一支，每一支都有自己的心灵模型。"},{"senses":"S05","en":"THE PRACTICAL TRICK: reading and steering a person in the moment.","cn":"实用手段：当场读懂并引导一个人。"},{"senses":"S03","en":"THE WEAPON: psychology applied to morale, as psychological warfare.","cn":"武器：作用于士气的心理学，即心理战。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Psychology is psych- plus -ology. Its family shows the Greek root psych- 'soul, mind' and the suffix -logy 'study', plus the related endings -ologist, -ological and -iatry.","cn":"psychology 是 psych- 加 -ology。它的词族展示希腊词根 psych-“灵魂、心智”与后缀 -logy“研究”，以及相关词尾 -ologist、-ological、-iatry。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek psykhē 'soul, breath' is the base of psyche, psychology and psychiatry; Greek logos 'word, reason' supplies -logy, -logical and -logue.","cn":"希腊语 psykhē“灵魂、呼吸”是 psyche、psychology、psychiatry 的基础；希腊语 logos“言词、理性”提供 -logy、-logical、-logue。"},"items":[{"word":"psychology","structure":"psych- (soul, mind) + -ology (study of)","meaning":"the study of the mind","meaningCN":"心理学（研究心智）","example":"Psychology explains why we forget names so easily.","exampleCN":"心理学解释了为什么我们那么容易忘记名字。"},{"word":"psyche","structure":"psyche (Greek noun, via Latin)","meaning":"the soul or mind","meaningCN":"灵魂；心灵","example":"The poem explores the wounded psyche of a soldier.","exampleCN":"这首诗探索一名士兵受伤的心灵。"},{"word":"psychiatry","structure":"psych- (mind) + -iatry (healing)","meaning":"the medical treatment of mental illness","meaningCN":"精神病学（治疗心智）","example":"She trained in psychiatry before opening a clinic.","exampleCN":"她在开设诊所前接受了精神病学训练。"},{"word":"psychoanalysis","structure":"psycho- (mind) + analysis (breaking up)","meaning":"the Freudian method of exploring the unconscious","meaningCN":"精神分析（拆解心智）","example":"Psychoanalysis asks what a dream hides.","exampleCN":"精神分析追问一个梦隐藏了什么。"},{"word":"psychologist","structure":"psychology + -ist (person)","meaning":"one who studies the mind","meaningCN":"心理学家","example":"The school hired a psychologist for its students.","exampleCN":"学校为学生聘请了一位心理学家。"},{"word":"psychological","structure":"psychology + -ical (adjective)","meaning":"of the mind or of psychology","meaningCN":"心理的；心理学的","example":"The injury was psychological rather than physical.","exampleCN":"这处伤是心理上的，而非身体上的。"},{"word":"psychopath","structure":"psycho- (mind) + -path (suffering)","meaning":"a person with a severe personality disorder","meaningCN":"精神变态者（心智患病）","example":"The character is written as a charming psychopath.","exampleCN":"这个角色被写成一个有魅力的精神变态者。"},{"word":"psychosomatic","structure":"psycho- (mind) + soma (body) + -tic","meaning":"having bodily symptoms caused by the mind","meaningCN":"心身性的（心智影响身体）","example":"Stress can produce psychosomatic headaches.","exampleCN":"压力可以引起心身性头痛。"},{"word":"parapsychology","structure":"para- (beside) + psychology","meaning":"the study of phenomena outside orthodox psychology","meaningCN":"超心理学（正统心理学之外）","example":"Parapsychology studies telepathy and clairvoyance.","exampleCN":"超心理学研究传心术与千里眼。"},{"word":"psychedelic","structure":"psyche (mind) + dēlos (visible) + -ic","meaning":"mind-revealing; producing altered perception","meaningCN":"致幻的；心灵显现的","example":"The album's psychedelic colours swirl on screen.","exampleCN":"专辑的致幻色彩在屏幕上旋转。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"psykhē","structure":"psykhē (Greek noun)","meaning":"breath, spirit, soul","meaningCN":"呼吸；精神；灵魂"},{"word":"logos","structure":"logos (Greek noun)","meaning":"word, reason, account","meaningCN":"言词；理性；论述"}]}},{"word":"publication","ipa_uk":"/ˌpʌblɪˈkeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌpʌblɪˈkeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"出版；出版物；发表；公布；发行","definition_en":"the act of making something known to everyone, and the printed or digital thing that results when writing is issued to the public","core_image":"一叠写好的稿子被推到印刷机下，几分钟后变成成千上万份，散到所有陌生人手里","scene":"A researcher refreshes the journal page and says: Publication is not the same as acceptance — the paper was accepted in March, but the issue is not out until June.","sceneCN":"这里 publication 是「发表」（第 3 个义项：使研究或文章为公众可得）；句意：发表不等于录用——论文三月被录用，但那期六月才出。画面里有屏幕、校样和日历。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"出版；出版物；发表；公布；发行"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the publication of","zh":"……的出版/公布"},{"phrase":"a monthly publication","zh":"月刊；每月出版物"},{"phrase":"publication date","zh":"出版日期"},{"phrase":"scientific publication","zh":"科学出版物；学术发表"},{"phrase":"prior publication","zh":"先前发表"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"publications"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"publish","pos":"v.","zh":"出版；发表；公布"},{"word":"publisher","pos":"n.","zh":"出版者；出版商"},{"word":"public","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"公众的；公众"},{"word":"publicize","pos":"v.","zh":"宣传；使公开"},{"word":"publicity","pos":"n.","zh":"宣传；公众注意"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Putting a book into the world","titleCN":"出版：把一本书推进世界","definition":"the act of producing a book, magazine, or other work and offering it to the public","definitionCN":"制作书籍、杂志或其他作品并向公众提供的行为","example":"The publication of her memoir took two years.","exampleCN":"她回忆录的出版花了两年时间。","why":"The sense 'issuing of a written or printed work to the public by sale or distribution' is recorded from the 1570s. The older 'making known' turns into a physical process: print, bind, sell.","whyCN":"“通过销售或分发向公众发行文字或印刷作品”这一义项记录于 16 世纪 70 年代。更早的“使人知晓”变成了物理过程：印刷、装订、销售。"},{"no":"02","title":"The thing issued: a publication","titleCN":"出版物：被推出去的那件东西","definition":"a book, journal, or other work that has been published","definitionCN":"已出版的书籍、期刊或其他作品","example":"The library subscribes to several scientific publications.","exampleCN":"图书馆订阅了几种科学出版物。","why":"From the 1650s the word also names the thing issued and offered. The noun of action becomes a countable object — the deed and its product share one form.","whyCN":"从 17 世纪 50 年代起，这个词也命名被发行、被提供的那个东西。动作名词变成了可数物体——行为与产物共用同一个形式。"},{"no":"03","title":"Making research public","titleCN":"发表：把研究交到同行手里","definition":"the act of making research, writing, or an article available to the public, especially in a journal","definitionCN":"使研究、文字或文章为公众可得的行为，尤指在期刊上","example":"Publication in a peer-reviewed journal is required for promotion.","exampleCN":"在同行评审期刊上发表是晋升的必要条件。","why":"Academic life narrowed the 1570s issuing sense to the author's act: a paper is 'published' when it enters the public record. Publication becomes the currency of a career.","whyCN":"学术生活把 16 世纪 70 年代的发行义收窄为作者的行为：论文进入公共记录即“发表”。publication 于是成了学术生涯的通货。"},{"no":"04","title":"Making it known: the original sense","titleCN":"公布、公开宣布：最初的那个意思","definition":"the act of making something publicly known; official notification to the people at large","definitionCN":"使某事为公众所知的行为；向大众的官方通告","example":"The publication of the findings surprised the whole industry.","exampleCN":"研究结果的公布震动了整个行业。","why":"Late 14c. publicacioun meant 'the act of making publicly known, notification to the people at large'. Before print, publication was simply speech made public.","whyCN":"14 世纪后期的 publicacioun 意为“使公众知晓的行为、向大众通告”。在印刷术之前，publication 只是把话公开说出来。"},{"no":"05","title":"The release of an edition","titleCN":"发行、发售：某一版次被放出去","definition":"the release of a particular edition or issue for sale or distribution","definitionCN":"某一版本或期次为销售或分发而发行","example":"The publication of the new edition was timed for the holidays.","exampleCN":"新版的发行被安排在假期。","why":"Once publication is an event in the market, it can be scheduled, delayed, and dated. The abstract act becomes a release date on a calendar.","whyCN":"一旦 publication 成为市场中的事件，它就可以被排期、推迟、标注日期。抽象的行为变成了日历上的发行日。"},{"no":"06","title":"A periodical you can hold","titleCN":"刊物：按期出的一本东西","definition":"a periodical, such as a magazine or journal, issued at regular intervals","definitionCN":"定期发行的期刊，如杂志或学报","example":"She writes a column for a trade publication.","exampleCN":"她为一家行业刊物撰写专栏。","why":"The object sense specializes: a publication is not any book but one of a series that keeps appearing. The issue is the unit, the publication is the title.","whyCN":"物体义发生专门化：publication 不是任意一本书，而是持续出现的一系列中的一种。一期是单位，publication 是刊名。"},{"no":"07","title":"Exposing private material","titleCN":"披露、公开：把私下的东西摊到阳光下","definition":"the act of making private letters, records, or images open to public view","definitionCN":"使私人信件、记录或影像向公众开放的行为","example":"The publication of the private letters caused a scandal.","exampleCN":"这些私人信件的公开引发了一场丑闻。","why":"The original 'making known' sense survives strongly when the material was never meant to be known. Publication here is exposure, not commerce.","whyCN":"当材料本不该被知道时，最初的“使人知晓”义就强烈地存活着。这里的 publication 是曝光，而不是买卖。"},{"no":"08","title":"Publication in media law","titleCN":"法律上的传播、发表：让第三方看到","definition":"in media law, the communication of defamatory or protected material to a third party","definitionCN":"媒体法中，向第三方传播诽谤性或受保护材料的行为","example":"The court asked whether the email amounted to publication.","exampleCN":"法院要判断这封电子邮件是否构成“传播”。","why":"Law needs a precise moment when words leave private hands. 'Publication' supplies it: any communication to a third party, even one reader, can be publication.","whyCN":"法律需要一个精确的时刻，判定言语何时离开私人之手。publication 提供了它：向第三方——哪怕只有一位读者——的任何传达都可构成“传播”。"},{"no":"09","title":"The publishing trade","titleCN":"出版业、出版工作：这一行的总称","definition":"the business or activity of publishing as a profession","definitionCN":"作为职业的出版业务或活动","example":"She has worked in publication for twenty years.","exampleCN":"她在出版行业工作了二十年。","why":"The noun of action can name an entire trade, just as 'education' names a field. What began as one act of making public becomes an industry.","whyCN":"动作名词可以命名整个行业，正如 education 命名一个领域。最初“使公开”的一个动作，变成了一个产业。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Publication is from Latin publicare 'make public', built on publicus 'of the people'. It begins as the act of telling everyone, gains the printing sense in the 1570s, and then splits into the act, the object, the edition, and the law.","cn":"publication 来自拉丁语 publicare“使公开”，其基础是 publicus“属于人民的”。它起初指“告诉所有人”的行为，16 世纪 70 年代获得印刷义，随后分裂为行为、物体、版次与法律义。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Publicare meant 'to make public', from publicus 'of the people, common'. Publicus was altered from Old Latin poplicus, from populus 'people'; the deeper origin of populus is uncertain and is marked source uncertain.","cn":"publicare 意为“使公开”，来自 publicus“属于人民的、公共的”。publicus 由古拉丁语 poplicus 变来，后者来自 populus“人民”；populus 更深的来源不确定，标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"LATIN NOUN","en":"Publicatio meant 'a making public', also 'an adjudging to the public treasury'. The legal sense of handing something to the state runs beside the sense of announcing.","cn":"publicatio 意为“使公开”，也指“判归国库”。把某物交给国家的法律义，与“宣布”的义项并行。"},{"era":"LATE 14c. ENGLISH","en":"Publicacioun enters English as 'the act of making publicly known, notification to the people at large'. Print does not exist yet; publication is an act of speech and notice.","cn":"publicacioun 进入英语时意为“使公众知晓的行为、向大众通告”。印刷术尚未出现；publication 是一种言说与公告的行为。"},{"era":"1570s ENGLISH","en":"The meaning 'the issuing of a written or printed work to the public by sale or distribution' is recorded by the 1570s. The printing press gives the word a product.","cn":"“通过销售或分发向公众发行文字或印刷作品”这一义项记录于 16 世纪 70 年代。印刷机给了这个词一个产品。"},{"era":"1650s ENGLISH","en":"From the 1650s the word also names the thing so issued and offered. Act and object now share one noun.","cn":"从 17 世纪 50 年代起，这个词也命名被发行、被提供的那个东西。行为与物体如今共用一个名词。"},{"era":"19c.–20c. ENGLISH","en":"Academic publication becomes a career measure, periodicals multiply, and media law fixes 'communication to a third party' as publication. The old 'making known' sense survives in every one.","cn":"学术发表成为职业衡量标准，期刊大量增加，媒体法把“向第三方传达”确定为 publication。古老的“使人知晓”义在每一个新义里都存活下来。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the publ- opening or the -ation ending but differs in meaning; the near group names the act, the object, and the audience.","cn":"形近组共享 publ- 开头或 -ation 结尾，但意义不同；近义组则分别命名行为、物体与受众。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"publicity","ipa":"/pʌbˈlɪsəti/","tag":"-ity, not -ation","definition":"attention given to someone by the media. It ends in -ity and names attention, not an issued work.","definitionCN":"媒体给予的公众关注。它以 -ity 结尾，指注意力，而不是被发行的作品。"},{"word":"publicization","ipa":"/ˌpʌblɪsaɪˈzeɪʃn/","tag":"-ization","definition":"the act of publicizing something. It looks like publication but its ending is -ization, not -ation.","definitionCN":"宣传、使公开的行为。它形似 publication，但词尾是 -ization 而非 -ation。"},{"word":"republication","ipa":"/ˌriːpʌblɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"re- + publication","definition":"the act of publishing something again. The prefix re- marks a second issuing.","definitionCN":"再出版；重新发表。前缀 re- 标记第二次发行。"},{"word":"publican","ipa":"/ˈpʌblɪkən/","tag":"looks like public + -an","definition":"a tavern keeper or, in older use, a tax collector. It shares the publi- opening but ends in -an, not -ation.","definitionCN":"酒馆老板，旧时也指收税人。它共享 publi- 开头，但词尾是 -an 而非 -ation。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"publishing","ipa":"/ˈpʌblɪʃɪŋ/","tag":"the industry","definition":"the business of producing books and periodicals. It names the trade, where publication can name a single act or object.","definitionCN":"图书与期刊的生产行业。它命名行业，而 publication 可指单次行为或单个物体。"},{"word":"issue","ipa":"/ˈɪʃuː/","tag":"one release","definition":"a particular edition or number of a periodical, or the act of releasing it.","definitionCN":"期刊的某一版次或期号，或发行它的行为。"},{"word":"release","ipa":"/rɪˈliːs/","tag":"make available","definition":"the act of making a film, record, or statement available to the public.","definitionCN":"使电影、唱片或声明向公众可得的行为。"},{"word":"announcement","ipa":"/əˈnaʊnsmənt/","tag":"making known","definition":"a public statement that informs people of something. It matches publication's original sense.","definitionCN":"告知公众某事的公开声明。它对应 publication 的本义。"},{"word":"circulation","ipa":"/ˌsɜːkjəˈleɪʃn/","tag":"copies distributed","definition":"the number of copies of a publication sold or distributed.","definitionCN":"出版物售出或分发的份数。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin publicus 'of the people', publicare 'make public', and the 1570s printing sense that turned an announcement into an object.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 publicus“属于人民的”、publicare“使公开”，以及 16 世纪 70 年代把公告变成物品的印刷义。"},"normal":[{"en":"publication = public + -ation: the act of making something public.","cn":"publication = public + -ation：使某物公开的行为。"},{"en":"publicare 'make public' is the same verb behind publish: publication is the noun of that act.","cn":"publicare“使公开”也是 publish 背后的动词：publication 就是那个动作的名词。"},{"en":"Before print, publication was a voice in the square; after print, it is a book on a shelf.","cn":"印刷术之前，publication 是广场上的一个声音；印刷术之后，它是书架上的一本书。"},{"en":"A publication can be both the deed and the thing: 'the publication of the book' and 'a scientific publication'.","cn":"publication 既可以是行为也可以是东西：“这本书的出版”和“一份科学出版物”。"},{"en":"In law, publication needs only a third pair of eyes — even one reader can count.","cn":"在法律上，publication 只需要第三双眼睛——哪怕只有一位读者也算。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is a door opened: what was private becomes available to all.","cn":"核心是一扇被打开的门：原本私下的东西变成人人可得。"},{"en":"One act, three products: knowledge, a printed object, and an industry.","cn":"一个动作，三种产物：知识、一件印刷品、一个产业。"},{"en":"The word keeps its original promise: publication is first of all making known.","cn":"这个词始终守着最初的承诺：publication 首先是使人知晓。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The publication of the report was delayed by legal review.","cn":"报告的公布因法律审查而推迟。"},{"en":"She lists three publications on her academic CV.","cn":"她在学术简历上列了三项出版物。"},{"en":"The newspaper is a daily publication with a large circulation.","cn":"这份报纸是一份发行量很大的日报。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"public（公众）+ ation（行为）——把东西送到公众面前；谐音“帕布利凯申”：把稿子“扑”到印刷机上，公开（public）地发出去 → publication 出版；公布","word":"publication"},"root":"源自拉丁语 publicare“使公开”，由 publicus“属于人民的”加动词后缀构成，名词 publicatio 经古法语进入英语；核心是“把原本私下的东西交给所有人”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses on one movement: from private to public. The word begins as an announcement, becomes the printing and sale of a work, then the work itself, an edition, a periodical, an exposure, a legal communication, and finally an industry.","cn":"九个义项围绕同一个动作：从私下到公开。这个词从“公告”开始，变成作品的印刷与销售，再指作品本身、一个版次、一种期刊、一次曝光、一次法律意义上的传达，最后指一个行业。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a private manuscript pushed through the press and handed out to strangers.","cn":"核心意象：一份私人手稿被送进印刷机，然后分发到陌生人手里。"},"chain":["OF THE PEOPLE","MAKE IT PUBLIC","TELL EVERYONE","PUT IT IN PRINT","OFFER IT FOR SALE","HOLD THE ISSUE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S05","en":"THE ACT OF ISSUING: producing a work, and releasing a particular edition.","cn":"发行行为：制作一部作品，以及发行某个版次。"},{"senses":"S02 · S06","en":"THE THING ISSUED: a published work, and a periodical that keeps appearing.","cn":"被发行之物：已出版的作品，以及持续出现的期刊。"},{"senses":"S03 · S04","en":"MAKING KNOWN: academic publication, and the original sense of public announcement.","cn":"使人知晓：学术发表，以及公开宣告的本义。"},{"senses":"S07","en":"EXPOSURE: private material brought into the light, willing or not.","cn":"曝光：私人材料被带到光下，无论当事人是否愿意。"},{"senses":"S08 · S09","en":"THE PUBLIC SPHERE: publication in media law, and publishing as a trade.","cn":"公共领域：媒体法中的“传播”，以及作为行业的出版。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Publication is publ- plus -ication. Its family shows Latin publicus 'of the people', the verb publicare, the noun ending -ation, and the agent and quality endings -er, -ist, -ity and -ize.","cn":"publication 是 publ- 加 -ication。它的词族展示拉丁语 publicus“属于人民的”、动词 publicare、名词词尾 -ation，以及施事与性质词尾 -er、-ist、-ity、-ize。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin publicus 'of the people' is the base of public, publish and publication; publicare 'make public' yields publication and publication's verb publish, while -ity and -ize build publicity and publicize.","cn":"拉丁语 publicus“属于人民的”是 public、publish、publication 的基础；publicare“使公开”给出 publication 及其动词 publish，而 -ity 与 -ize 构成 publicity 与 publicize。"},"items":[{"word":"publication","structure":"publicare (make public) + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of making public; a published work","meaningCN":"出版；公布；出版物","example":"The publication of the atlas took ten years.","exampleCN":"这本图集的出版花了十年。"},{"word":"public","structure":"publicus (of the people)","meaning":"open to all; the people as a whole","meaningCN":"公共的；公众","example":"The garden is open to the public.","exampleCN":"这座花园向公众开放。"},{"word":"publish","structure":"publicare (make public) + -ish (verb)","meaning":"to make public; to issue a work","meaningCN":"公布；出版","example":"They publish four issues a year.","exampleCN":"他们一年出版四期。"},{"word":"publisher","structure":"publish + -er (agent)","meaning":"a person or company that issues works","meaningCN":"出版者；出版商","example":"The publisher accepted her manuscript.","exampleCN":"出版商接受了她的手稿。"},{"word":"publicize","structure":"public + -ize (verb)","meaning":"to bring something to public attention","meaningCN":"宣传；使公开","example":"The team publicized the event on social media.","exampleCN":"团队在社交媒体上宣传了这场活动。"},{"word":"publicity","structure":"public + -ity (quality, state)","meaning":"the state of being known; media attention","meaningCN":"公众注意；宣传","example":"The trial brought unwanted publicity.","exampleCN":"这场审判带来了不受欢迎的关注。"},{"word":"publicist","structure":"public + -ist (person)","meaning":"one who manages publicity","meaningCN":"宣传人员；公关","example":"Her publicist arranged three interviews.","exampleCN":"她的公关安排了三场采访。"},{"word":"republication","structure":"re- (again) + publication","meaning":"a second publishing","meaningCN":"再出版；重新发表","example":"The republication includes a new preface.","exampleCN":"这次再版增加了新序。"},{"word":"publishable","structure":"publish + -able (able to be)","meaning":"fit to be published","meaningCN":"可出版的；适合发表的","example":"The draft is not yet publishable.","exampleCN":"这份草稿还不能发表。"},{"word":"prepublication","structure":"pre- (before) + publication","meaning":"the stage before a work is published","meaningCN":"出版前（阶段）","example":"Prepublication copies went to reviewers.","exampleCN":"出版前的样书被送到了评论者手中。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"publicus","structure":"publicus (adjective)","meaning":"of the people, common","meaningCN":"属于人民的；公共的"},{"word":"publicare","structure":"publicare (verb)","meaning":"to make public","meaningCN":"使公开"}]}},{"word":"publish","ipa_uk":"/ˈpʌblɪʃ/","ipa_us":"/ˈpʌblɪʃ/","definition_zh":"出版；发表；公布；网络发布；刊登","definition_en":"to make something public — first by announcing it, then by printing and selling it, and now by posting it online","core_image":"一扇原本关着的门被推开，屋里的话、文稿和消息一下子涌到街上，所有人都能听见看见","scene":"An editor points at the screen and says: We publish the story at nine, then update it before anyone notices.","sceneCN":"这里 publish 是「网络发布」（第 4 个义项：在网站或平台上发布内容）；句意：我们九点把报道发到网上，然后在任何人发现之前更新它。画面里有新闻编辑室、时钟和一个亮着的窗口。","pos":[{"tag":"v.","zh":"出版；发表；公布；发布；刊登"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"publish a book","zh":"出版一本书"},{"phrase":"publish the results","zh":"发表结果"},{"phrase":"publish online","zh":"在网上发布"},{"phrase":"be published in","zh":"发表于（某刊物）"},{"phrase":"publish or perish","zh":"不发表就出局（学术界习语）"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"publishes"},{"label":"过去式","form":"published"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"published"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"publishing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"publisher","pos":"n.","zh":"出版者；出版商"},{"word":"publishing","pos":"n.","zh":"出版；出版业"},{"word":"publication","pos":"n.","zh":"出版；出版物；发表"},{"word":"publishable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可出版的；适合发表的"},{"word":"unpublished","pos":"adj.","zh":"未出版的；未发表的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Bringing out a book","titleCN":"出版：把一本书做出来卖掉","definition":"to prepare and issue a book, magazine, or other work for sale or distribution","definitionCN":"制作并发行书籍、杂志或其他作品以供销售或分发","example":"The press will publish her novel next spring.","exampleCN":"这家出版社将在明年春天出版她的小说。","why":"From late 14c. the verb meant 'issue (a book, etc.) to the public, cause to be printed and offered for sale'. The printed object is the first thing the word learns to push out of doors.","whyCN":"从 14 世纪后期起，这个动词意为“向公众发行（书等），使被印刷并供销售”。印刷品是这个词最早学会推出门外的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"Putting research into print","titleCN":"发表：让研究进入公共记录","definition":"to make an article, paper, or piece of writing available to the public, especially in a journal","definitionCN":"使文章、论文或文字为公众可得，尤指在期刊上","example":"They published the results in a medical journal.","exampleCN":"他们把结果发表在一份医学期刊上。","why":"The book-issuing sense narrows to the author's act: the journal issues, the author publishes. What counts is that the work enters the public record where others can cite it.","whyCN":"出书义收窄为作者的行为：期刊发行，作者发表。关键在于作品进入公共记录，别人可以引用。"},{"no":"03","title":"Making information public","titleCN":"公布：把消息放到所有人面前","definition":"to make information public, especially officially or in a formal statement","definitionCN":"使信息为公众所知，尤指官方或以正式声明的方式","example":"The company published its annual figures yesterday.","exampleCN":"公司昨天公布了年度数据。","why":"The original mid-14c. sense was 'make publicly known, reveal, divulge, announce'. No printing is needed: a spoken announcement can publish a piece of news.","whyCN":"14 世纪中的本义是“使公众知晓、揭露、泄露、宣布”。不需要印刷：一句口头宣布也能“公布”一条消息。"},{"no":"04","title":"Posting on the internet","titleCN":"网络发布：按下那个按钮","definition":"to post content on a website, platform, or social media account","definitionCN":"在网站、平台或社交媒体账号上发布内容","example":"She publishes a new video every Friday.","exampleCN":"她每周五发布一个新视频。","why":"The printing sense transfers to screens: a platform 'publishes' what it makes visible to all. The button is the modern press — one click, and the private becomes public.","whyCN":"印刷义转移到屏幕上：平台“出版”它所展示给所有人的内容。按钮就是现代的印刷机——一点，私下之物就公开了。"},{"no":"05","title":"Releasing an edition","titleCN":"发行、发售：某一版被放出去","definition":"to release a particular edition or issue for sale or distribution","definitionCN":"为销售或分发而发行某一版次或期次","example":"The dictionary was first published in 1895.","exampleCN":"这部词典于 1895 年首次出版发行。","why":"Publishing is also a dated event: a first edition appears, sells out, is reprinted. The verb names the moment the edition leaves the warehouse.","whyCN":"出版也是一个有日期的事件：初版出现、售罄、重印。这个动词命名版次离开仓库的那一刻。"},{"no":"06","title":"Spreading it abroad: the oldest sense","titleCN":"公开传播：最早的那个意思","definition":"to spread something among people; to make it known widely (the original sense)","definitionCN":"把某事在人群中传播；使广为人知（本义）","example":"The rumour was published across the town within a day.","exampleCN":"这个谣言一天之内就传遍了全镇。","why":"Old French publier meant 'make public, spread abroad, communicate', from Latin publicare. Before print and before media, publishing was simply spreading the word.","whyCN":"古法语 publier 意为“使公开、传播四方、传达”，来自拉丁语 publicare。在印刷与媒体之前，publishing 只是把话传开。"},{"no":"07","title":"Carrying it in the paper","titleCN":"刊登：报纸替你发出去","definition":"to carry an article, letter, or notice in a newspaper or magazine","definitionCN":"在报纸或杂志上刊登文章、来信或通知","example":"The paper published his letter on the front page.","exampleCN":"报纸把他的信刊登在头版。","why":"The medium becomes the agent: a paper publishes what it prints. The author may have written it, but the newspaper performs the public act.","whyCN":"媒体成了施动者：报纸刊登它所印的内容。作者也许写了它，但执行公开行为的是报纸。"},{"no":"08","title":"To expose and denounce (archaic)","titleCN":"揭发、公开谴责：把某人推到众人眼前","definition":"to disgrace or denounce someone publicly (an archaic sense)","definitionCN":"公开使某人蒙羞或谴责某人（古旧义）","example":"The pamphlet published him as a traitor.","exampleCN":"那本小册子公开指认他为叛徒。","why":"Late 14c. also recorded 'to disgrace, put to shame; denounce publicly'. Making someone public could mean exposing him to shame — publication as punishment, not information.","whyCN":"14 世纪后期还记录有“使蒙羞、羞辱；公开谴责”。把一个人公开，可以意味着让他暴露在羞耻中——公开即惩罚，而非告知。"},{"no":"09","title":"To be someone's publisher","titleCN":"为……出书：长期替一位作者出书","definition":"to be the publisher of a writer's work over time","definitionCN":"长期作为某位作者作品的出版者","example":"This house has published him for twenty years.","exampleCN":"这家出版社已经为他出书二十年了。","why":"The verb can name an ongoing relationship, not just a single act. A publisher 'publishes' an author the way a gallery represents an artist: repeatedly, as a standing commitment.","whyCN":"这个动词可以命名一种持续关系，而不只是单次行为。出版社“出版”一位作者，就像画廊代理一位艺术家：反复地、作为长期承诺。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Publish is from Latin publicare 'make public', through Old French publier. It starts as 'announce', gains 'print and sell' in the late 14c., and later picks up 'post online'. The whole history is one move: from private to public.","cn":"publish 来自拉丁语 publicare“使公开”，经古法语 publier 进入英语。它从“宣布”开始，在 14 世纪后期获得“印刷并销售”义，后来又有“网上发布”。整部历史就是一个动作：从私下到公开。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Publicare meant 'to make public', from publicus 'of the people'. Publicus was altered from Old Latin poplicus, from populus 'people'; the deeper origin of populus is uncertain and is marked source uncertain.","cn":"publicare 意为“使公开”，来自 publicus“属于人民的”。publicus 由古拉丁语 poplicus 变来，后者来自 populus“人民”；populus 更深的来源不确定，标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"Publier meant 'make public, spread abroad, communicate'. The French verb carries the word into English with the sense of spreading news among people.","cn":"publier 意为“使公开、传播四方、传达”。这个法语动词带着“在人群中传播消息”的意思进入英语。"},{"era":"EARLY 14c. ENGLISH","en":"Publicen appears in English with the sense 'make public'. It is the direct borrowing of the French verb.","cn":"publicen 以“使公开”之义出现在英语中，是对法语动词的直接借用。"},{"era":"MID-14c. ENGLISH","en":"Publishen is an alteration of publicen, probably by influence of banish and finish. It means 'make publicly known, reveal, divulge, announce'.","cn":"publishen 是 publicen 的变体，可能受 banish、finish 等词影响。它意为“使公众知晓、揭露、泄露、宣布”。"},{"era":"LATE 14c. ENGLISH","en":"The printing sense appears: 'issue (a book, etc.) to the public, cause to be printed and offered for sale'. The same period records 'to disgrace, put to shame; denounce publicly', and the odd sense 'to people, populate; to multiply'.","cn":"印刷义出现：“向公众发行（书等），使被印刷并供销售”。同一时期还记录有“使蒙羞、羞辱；公开谴责”，以及奇怪的“使人居住、繁殖”义。"},{"era":"19c.–20c. ENGLISH","en":"Publishing becomes an industry with publishers, editions and copyright; in the late 20c. the verb extends to websites and social platforms, where 'publish' means 'make visible to everyone'.","cn":"出版在 19 至 20 世纪成为拥有出版商、版次与版权的产业；20 世纪后期，这个动词扩展到网站与社交平台，publish 意为“让所有人看见”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the publ- or -ish shape but not the sense; the near group names the various acts of releasing words to the world.","cn":"形近组共享 publ- 或 -ish 的外形，但意义不同；近义组命名把文字释放给世界的各种动作。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"public","ipa":"/ˈpʌblɪk/","tag":"adjective, no -ish","definition":"open to all; of the people. It is the adjective behind publish, but has no verb ending.","definitionCN":"公共的；公众的。它是 publish 背后的形容词，但没有动词词尾。"},{"word":"punish","ipa":"/ˈpʌnɪʃ/","tag":"-ish but different root","definition":"to make someone suffer for a wrong. It rhymes with publish but comes from a different root.","definitionCN":"惩罚。它与 publish 押韵，但词根完全不同。"},{"word":"polish","ipa":"/ˈpɒlɪʃ/","tag":"one letter away","definition":"to make something smooth and shiny. It differs from publish by a single vowel.","definitionCN":"抛光；擦亮。它与 publish 只差一个元音。"},{"word":"publishable","ipa":"/ˈpʌblɪʃəbl/","tag":"publish + -able","definition":"fit to be published. It is the same verb plus the suffix -able.","definitionCN":"可出版的。它是同一个动词加上后缀 -able。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"print","ipa":"/prɪnt/","tag":"physical reproduction","definition":"to reproduce text or images on paper. It is the physical half of publishing.","definitionCN":"在纸上复制文字或图像。它是出版的物质一半。"},{"word":"issue","ipa":"/ˈɪʃuː/","tag":"release officially","definition":"to release something officially, such as stamps, shares, or an edition.","definitionCN":"正式发行某物，如邮票、股票或一个版次。"},{"word":"release","ipa":"/rɪˈliːs/","tag":"make available","definition":"to make a film, record, or statement available to the public.","definitionCN":"使电影、唱片或声明向公众可得。"},{"word":"announce","ipa":"/əˈnaʊns/","tag":"make known","definition":"to tell people about something officially. It matches publish in the 'make public' sense.","definitionCN":"正式告知人们某事。它对应 publish 的“使公开”义。"},{"word":"circulate","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkjəleɪt/","tag":"spread around","definition":"to pass something from person to person or place to place.","definitionCN":"使某物在人与人、地与时之间流传。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin publicare 'make public', Old French publier, and the modern publisher who turns a manuscript into a public object.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 publicare“使公开”、古法语 publier，以及把稿子变成公共物品的现代 publisher。"},"normal":[{"en":"publish = public + -ish: to make public, with a verb ending.","cn":"publish = public + -ish：使公开，只是多了一个动词词尾。"},{"en":"The pair gives two nouns: publication (the act or thing) and publicity (the attention).","cn":"这一对给出两个名词：publication（行为或物品）与 publicity（注意力）。"},{"en":"A publisher is the person who pushes the door open; publishing is the industry built around that push.","cn":"publisher 是推开门的人；publishing 是围绕这一推建立的产业。"},{"en":"'Publish or perish' is the academic rule: if your work is not made public, it does not count.","cn":"“publish or perish（不发表就出局）”是学术规则：作品若未公开，就不算数。"},{"en":"Press 'Publish' on a blog and the old printing metaphor happens instantly.","cn":"在博客上按下“发布”，那个古老的印刷隐喻瞬间发生。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is a door: what was inside is now outside, available to anyone.","cn":"核心是一扇门：原本在里面的，现在到了外面，任何人都能得到。"},{"en":"The word moves through three machines: voice, press, network — the same act each time.","cn":"这个词穿过三台机器：嗓音、印刷机、网络——每次都是同一个动作。"},{"en":"Publish can inform or expose; the same opening of a door can be a gift or a punishment.","cn":"publish 可以是告知，也可以是揭发；同一扇门的打开，可以是礼物，也可以是惩罚。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The journal publishes articles on climate policy every month.","cn":"这份期刊每月发表气候政策方面的文章。"},{"en":"The government published the new safety rules on its website.","cn":"政府在网站上公布了新的安全规则。"},{"en":"He published his first photograph at the age of sixteen.","cn":"他十六岁时发表了自己的第一张照片。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"public（公众）+ ish（动词）——把东西放到公众面前；谐音“帕布利什”：把稿子“扑”进印刷机，立刻（lish）公开 → publish 出版；发表","word":"publish"},"root":"源自拉丁语 publicare“使公开”，由 publicus“属于人民的”构成，经古法语 publier 进入英语；核心是“把原本关在屋里的东西推给所有人”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses, one movement outward. A voice announces, a press prints and sells, a journal carries research, a company releases figures, a website posts a video, and an old sense even exposes a person to public shame.","cn":"九个义项，一个向外的动作。嗓音宣布，印刷机印出并销售，期刊承载研究，公司发布数据，网站上传视频，还有一个古老义把一个人推到公众的羞耻里。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a closed door opened — words, writing, or news released to everyone at once.","cn":"核心意象：一扇关着的门被打开——话语、文字或消息一下子释放给所有人。"},"chain":["MAKE PUBLIC","SPREAD THE WORD","SET IT IN TYPE","OFFER IT FOR SALE","CARRY IT IN THE PAPER","POST IT ONLINE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S05","en":"THE PRINTED OBJECT: bringing out a book, and releasing a particular edition.","cn":"印刷品：把一本书做出来，以及发行某个版次。"},{"senses":"S02 · S07","en":"THE MEDIUM: research published in a journal, and a letter carried by a newspaper.","cn":"媒介：在期刊上发表研究，以及报纸刊登一封来信。"},{"senses":"S03 · S06","en":"MAKING KNOWN: official disclosure, and the oldest sense of spreading news abroad.","cn":"使人知晓：官方公布，以及最古老的“传播四方”义。"},{"senses":"S04","en":"THE NETWORK: posting content where everyone can see it.","cn":"网络：把内容发布到人人可见之处。"},{"senses":"S08 · S09","en":"THE PUBLIC GAZE: archaic public denunciation, and the publisher's long relation to an author.","cn":"公众目光：古旧的公开谴责，以及出版者与作者的长期关系。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Publish is publ- plus -ish. Its family shows Latin publicus 'of the people', the verb publicare, and the endings -er, -ing, -ation, -able and the negative prefix un-.","cn":"publish 是 publ- 加 -ish。它的词族展示拉丁语 publicus“属于人民的”、动词 publicare，以及词尾 -er、-ing、-ation、-able 和否定前缀 un-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin publicare 'make public' yields publish and publication; publicus 'of the people' gives public, publicity and publicize, while un- and re- build unpublished and republish.","cn":"拉丁语 publicare“使公开”给出 publish 与 publication；publicus“属于人民的”给出 public、publicity、publicize，而 un- 与 re- 构成 unpublished 与 republish。"},"items":[{"word":"publish","structure":"publicare (make public) + -ish (verb)","meaning":"to make public; to issue a work","meaningCN":"出版；发表；公布","example":"They publish a new edition every two years.","exampleCN":"他们每两年出版一个新版。"},{"word":"publisher","structure":"publish + -er (agent)","meaning":"one who issues books or other works","meaningCN":"出版者；出版商","example":"Her publisher sent her the first proofs.","exampleCN":"她的出版商把初校样寄给了她。"},{"word":"publishing","structure":"publish + -ing (verbal noun)","meaning":"the act or industry of issuing works","meaningCN":"出版；出版业","example":"Digital publishing changed the industry.","exampleCN":"数字出版改变了这个行业。"},{"word":"publication","structure":"publicare + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of publishing; a published work","meaningCN":"出版；出版物；发表","example":"The publication was delayed by a month.","exampleCN":"出版被推迟了一个月。"},{"word":"publishable","structure":"publish + -able (fit to be)","meaning":"suitable for publication","meaningCN":"可出版的；适合发表的","example":"The notes are interesting but not publishable.","exampleCN":"这些笔记有趣，但不适合发表。"},{"word":"unpublished","structure":"un- (not) + published","meaning":"not yet made public in print","meaningCN":"未出版的；未发表的","example":"The archive holds hundreds of unpublished letters.","exampleCN":"档案馆藏有数百封未发表的信件。"},{"word":"republish","structure":"re- (again) + publish","meaning":"to publish again","meaningCN":"再出版；重新发表","example":"The essay was republished in 1990.","exampleCN":"这篇文章于 1990 年重新发表。"},{"word":"public","structure":"publicus (of the people)","meaning":"open to all; the community","meaningCN":"公共的；公众","example":"The square is open to the public.","exampleCN":"这个广场向公众开放。"},{"word":"publicize","structure":"public + -ize (verb)","meaning":"to bring to public attention","meaningCN":"宣传；使公开","example":"They publicized the concert across campus.","exampleCN":"他们在全校宣传了这场音乐会。"},{"word":"publicity","structure":"public + -ity (state, quality)","meaning":"public attention; the state of being known","meaningCN":"公众注意；宣传","example":"The case attracted national publicity.","exampleCN":"这个案子引起了全国关注。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"publicus","structure":"publicus (adjective)","meaning":"of the people, common","meaningCN":"属于人民的；公共的"},{"word":"publicare","structure":"publicare (verb)","meaning":"to make public","meaningCN":"使公开"}]}},{"word":"purchase","ipa_uk":"/ˈpɜːtʃəs/","ipa_us":"/ˈpɝːtʃəs/","definition_zh":"购买；购置；购得之物；（以努力或牺牲）取得；紧握；抓握力；杠杆支点；（古）掠夺所得","definition_en":"to get something by paying money, or to obtain it by effort; also the firm hold by which power is applied","core_image":"一个人向前追着猎物跑，追上后死死攥住不放——先「追着取得」，很久以后才专指「用钱买下」","scene":"At a hardware store the manager taps the box and says: Keep the receipt, because this purchase over fifty dollars cannot be returned without it.","sceneCN":"这里 purchase 是「购得之物」（第 3 个义项：已经买到手的东西）；句意：留好小票，这件超过五十美元的购得之物没有它就不能退。画面里有柜台、收据和盖章的手。","pos":[{"tag":"v.","zh":"购买；购置；（以努力）取得；紧握"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"购买；购得之物；紧握（力）；杠杆支点"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"make a purchase","zh":"购买；购置"},{"phrase":"purchase price","zh":"买价；购价"},{"phrase":"purchase order","zh":"采购订单"},{"phrase":"proof of purchase","zh":"购买凭证"},{"phrase":"purchasing power","zh":"购买力"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"purchases"},{"label":"过去式","form":"purchased"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"purchased"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"purchasing"},{"label":"复数","form":"purchases"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"purchaser","pos":"n.","zh":"买主；购买者"},{"word":"purchasing","pos":"n.","zh":"采购；购买（部门或行为）"},{"word":"repurchase","pos":"v.","zh":"回购；再购买"},{"word":"purchasable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可购得的；买得到的"},{"word":"unpurchased","pos":"adj.","zh":"未购得的；没有买下的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"To buy: hand over money and take the thing","titleCN":"购买：付钱，把东西拿走","definition":"to get goods, services, or property by paying money for them","definitionCN":"用钱取得货物、服务或财产","example":"She purchased a used car for three thousand dollars.","exampleCN":"她花三千美元买了一辆二手车。","why":"The verb came from Old French porchacier, pur- 'forth' plus chacier 'to chase': to purchase was to go after something until you had it. Only in the mid-14c. did 'get by paying money' become the dominant sense.","whyCN":"动词来自古法语 porchacier，由 pur-「向前」加 chacier「追逐」构成：purchase 本是「追着去取得」。到 14 世纪中期，「付钱取得」才成为主义。"},{"no":"02","title":"Procurement: the formal act of acquiring","titleCN":"购置：有手续的正式取得","definition":"the formal or large-scale act of buying goods, equipment, or property","definitionCN":"正式或大宗地购买货物、设备或财产的行为","example":"The university approved the purchase of new laboratory equipment.","exampleCN":"校方批准了购置新的实验室设备。","why":"The noun's sense 'act of acquiring, procurement' is recorded from the late 14c. Modern institutions narrowed it to documented buying: the chase is gone, and what remains is a deliberate, recorded acquisition.","whyCN":"名词「取得、采购的行为」记录于 14 世纪后期。现代机构把它收窄为有单据的购买：追逐不见了，剩下的是有步骤、有记录的取得。"},{"no":"03","title":"The thing bought: an object with a receipt","titleCN":"购得之物：带小票的那件东西","definition":"something that has been bought","definitionCN":"已经买到手的东西","example":"Her most expensive purchase was a second-hand piano.","exampleCN":"她最贵的一件购得之物是一架二手钢琴。","why":"'That which is bought' dates from the 1580s, three centuries after the verb. The older noun meant 'acquisition, booty'; once buying became the main sense, the object bought could inherit the name.","whyCN":"「买到的东西」这一义项始于 16 世纪 80 年代，比动词晚三百年。早先名词指「获得物、战利品」；当购买成为主义，被买下的东西就继承了这个词。"},{"no":"04","title":"To win at a price: obtain by effort or loss","titleCN":"以代价取得：用努力或牺牲换来","definition":"to obtain something valuable through effort, suffering, or sacrifice rather than money","definitionCN":"通过努力、受苦或牺牲而得到有价值的东西，而非用钱","example":"They purchased their freedom with years of struggle.","exampleCN":"他们用多年的斗争换来了自由。","why":"This is the oldest English sense: c.1300 purchase meant 'acquire, obtain, procure' by any means, including merit or suffering. 'To purchase peace with blood' keeps that breadth, where money is only one possible price.","whyCN":"这是英语里最古老的义项：约 1300 年 purchase 指以任何方式「取得、获得、谋得」，包括功劳或受苦。「以鲜血换取和平」保留了这种宽度，钱只是众多代价之一。"},{"no":"05","title":"A firm grip: the hold that keeps the thing","titleCN":"紧握：攥住不放的那只手","definition":"a firm hold or grasp on something, especially one that gives control","definitionCN":"对某物的牢固抓握，尤指带来控制权的握持","example":"He got a purchase on the rope and pulled himself up.","exampleCN":"他抓住绳子，把自己拉了上去。","why":"The noun sense 'firm hold by which power may be exerted' is from 1711, extended from a nautical verb of the 1560s meaning 'to haul or draw, especially by mechanical power', as sailors purchase an anchor. Gripping and buying share the image of pulling something into your possession.","whyCN":"名词「可以施加力量的牢固把握」始于 1711 年，来自 16 世纪 60 年代一个航海动词「拉、绞（尤用机械力）」，如水手绞起锚。抓握与购买共享同一个意象：把东西拉进自己的掌控。"},{"no":"06","title":"Leverage: the point where a small force wins","titleCN":"杠杆支点：小力撬动大物的那个点","definition":"a position or hold that gives mechanical advantage, the point where a lever or force bites","definitionCN":"带来机械优势的位置或着力点，即杠杆或力量咬住的那一点","example":"Put the jack under the beam to get a better purchase.","exampleCN":"把千斤顶放到梁下，好取得更好的着力点。","why":"Mechanical 'purchase' names the hold or position that lets a small force move a great weight, the same word sailors used for hauling. The point where the lever bites is literally a place to grip.","whyCN":"机械上的 purchase 指让小力移动重物的着力点或握位，正是水手「绞拉」时用的词。杠杆咬住的那一点，字面上就是一个可以握紧的地方。"},{"no":"07","title":"Purchasing: buying turned into a department","titleCN":"采购：变成一门部门工作的购买","definition":"the institutional activity or department responsible for buying supplies and equipment","definitionCN":"负责购买物资与设备的机构性活动或部门","example":"She works in purchasing, sourcing parts for the whole factory.","exampleCN":"她在采购部工作，为整个工厂寻找零件。","why":"In business and government, purchasing became a department and a process in the 20th c.: purchase orders, purchasing agents. The act of buying is institutionalised and separated from the person who pays.","whyCN":"在商业与政府里，purchasing 在 20 世纪成为一个部门和流程：采购订单、采购员。购买行为被制度化，与掏钱的人分开了。"},{"no":"08","title":"To secure title: land and rights, not shopping","titleCN":"置产、买断：买的是产权，不是商品","definition":"to acquire property, land, or legal rights by payment, especially on a large or formal scale","definitionCN":"通过付款取得财产、土地或法律权利，尤指大宗或正式的","example":"The company purchased the land from the county in 1998.","exampleCN":"该公司于 1998 年从县政府买下了这块土地。","why":"Legal and landed use keeps the noun's weight: a purchase of land or of rights is an acquisition of title, not a shopping trip. The word still carries the old sense of getting something permanently into your holdings.","whyCN":"法律与地产用法保留了名词的分量：purchase of land or rights 是取得产权，而不是逛街购物。这个词仍带着「把某物永久纳入自己名下」的旧义。"},{"no":"09","title":"Booty: what was taken before it was bought","titleCN":"掠夺所得：还没「买」之前，是抢来的","definition":"in older usage, goods gained by pillage or robbery; spoils","definitionCN":"旧时用法：通过掠夺或抢劫得到的财物；战利品","example":"In the old chronicle, the raiders divided their purchase among the ships.","exampleCN":"在那部旧编年史里，劫掠者把抢来的财物分给了各条船。","why":"The noun's first English sense (c.1300) was 'booty, spoil, goods gained by pillage'; 'to make purchase' once meant 'to seize by robbery'. The polite buyer of today stands where a raider once stood.","whyCN":"名词最早的英语义项（约 1300 年）是「战利品、掠夺所得」；to make purchase 一度意为「抢劫夺取」。今天彬彬有礼的买主，站的是当年劫掠者的位置。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Purchase begins as a chase, not a transaction: Old French porchacier meant to go after something and get it. Money entered the word only in the 14th century, and the grip-and-lever senses came from sailors hauling anchors.","cn":"purchase 起于追逐而非交易：古法语 porchacier 意为追着去取得。金钱在 14 世纪才进入这个词，而「抓握、杠杆」义来自水手绞锚。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD FRENCH (11c.)","en":"Porchacier (later pourchasser) meant 'search for, procure; aim at, strive for, pursue eagerly'. It joins pur- 'forth' with chacier 'to run after, hunt, chase' (see chase). The exact force of pur- here, whether 'forward' or an intensive, is uncertain and is marked source uncertain.","cn":"Porchacier（后作 pourchasser）意为「寻找、谋得、力求、急切追求」，由 pur-「向前」加 chacier「追赶、打猎、追逐」（见 chase）构成。pur- 在此究竟是「向前」还是加强语气，来源不确定，故标为「来源不确定」。"},{"era":"ANGLO-FRENCH (c. 1300)","en":"The Anglo-French verb purchaser meant 'go after' and carried the legal-administrative tone of obtaining something. English took it over as purchase with a very wide meaning.","cn":"盎格鲁-法语动词 purchaser 意为「追赶、追求」，并带有取得某物的法律行政语气。英语借用为 purchase，含义非常宽。"},{"era":"c. 1300 ENGLISH","en":"The verb is first recorded as 'acquire, obtain; get, receive; procure, provide', also 'bring about, instigate, contrive'. At this stage money is not required: merit, suffering, or effort can be the price.","cn":"动词最早记录为「取得、获得、得到、领受、谋得、提供」，也有「促成、煽动、策划」义。此时并不需要金钱：功劳、受苦或努力都可以是代价。"},{"era":"MID-14c. ENGLISH","en":"The specific sense 'acquire or secure by expenditure of money or its equivalent, pay money for, buy' appears in the mid-14c. The older 'get by conquest in war, obtain as booty' survived into the 17c.","cn":"「以金钱或其等价物取得、付钱买下」这一具体义项出现于 14 世纪中期。更早的「以战争征服取得、作为战利品获得」一直用到 17 世纪。"},{"era":"1560s–1711 ENGLISH","en":"A nautical verb 'to haul or draw, especially by mechanical power' (1560s, used of hauling up anchors) produced the noun sense 'firm hold by which power may be exerted' in 1711. Meanwhile 'that which is bought' is recorded from the 1580s.","cn":"航海动词「拉、绞，尤指用机械力」（16 世纪 60 年代，用于绞起锚）在 1711 年衍生出名词「可以施加力量的牢固把握」；同时「买到的东西」记录于 16 世纪 80 年代。"},{"era":"c. 1300–20c. ENGLISH","en":"The noun's journey runs from 'booty, spoil' (c.1300) to 'act of acquiring' (late 14c.) to 'thing bought' (1580s) and finally to the 20th-century department of purchasing. Plunder, transaction, object, institution: one word, four stages.","cn":"名词的旅程从「战利品、掠夺物」（约 1300）到「取得行为」（14 世纪后期），再到「买到的东西」（16 世纪 80 年代），最后到 20 世纪的采购部门。劫掠、交易、物品、机构：一个词，四个阶段。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"pursue","ipa":"/pəˈsjuː/","tag":"sounds close, different root","definition":"to follow or chase someone, or to work toward a goal. It echoes purchase in sound but comes from Latin prosequi, not from chacier.","definitionCN":"追赶；追求。它与 purchase 读音相近，但来自拉丁语 prosequi，而非 chacier。"},{"word":"pursuit","ipa":"/pəˈsjuːt/","tag":"same sound family","definition":"the act of chasing or striving for something. Like pursue, it belongs to the sequi 'follow' family.","definitionCN":"追赶；追求。与 pursue 一样属于 sequi「跟随」词族。"},{"word":"peruse","ipa":"/pəˈruːz/","tag":"look-alike, unrelated","definition":"to read through carefully. It looks like purchase but has no etymological link.","definitionCN":"细读；浏览。它形似 purchase，但词源上毫无关联。"},{"word":"purpose","ipa":"/ˈpɜːpəs/","tag":"pur- plus poser","definition":"an aim or intention. It also begins with pur-, but the second element is poser 'to place'.","definitionCN":"目的；意图。它同样以 pur- 开头，但后半是 poser「放置」。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"buy","ipa":"/baɪ/","tag":"plain everyday word","definition":"to get something by paying money. It is the short native verb where purchase is the formal one.","definitionCN":"买。它是简短的本族动词，purchase 则是正式用词。"},{"word":"acquire","ipa":"/əˈkwaɪə/","tag":"gain possession","definition":"to come to possess something, often through effort or over time, not necessarily by payment.","definitionCN":"获得；取得。常指通过努力或随时间而拥有，不一定付钱。"},{"word":"procure","ipa":"/prəˈkjʊə/","tag":"obtain with effort","definition":"to obtain something, especially with care or difficulty. It matches the oldest sense of purchase.","definitionCN":"设法取得，尤指费心或费力地。它对应 purchase 最古老的义项。"},{"word":"obtain","ipa":"/əbˈteɪn/","tag":"formal get","definition":"to get something, especially by request or effort. Neutral in tone, wider than buy.","definitionCN":"获得。尤指通过请求或努力，语气中性，比 buy 宽。"},{"word":"grip","ipa":"/ɡrɪp/","tag":"the hold sense","definition":"a firm hold on something. It covers the physical sense of purchase as grip or leverage.","definitionCN":"紧握；抓握。它对应 purchase 表示抓握或着力点的实指义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Old French chacier 'to chase', Anglo-French purchaser, and the nautical hauling sense that gave us the grip.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：古法语 chacier「追逐」、盎格鲁-法语 purchaser，以及带来「抓握」义的航海绞拉用法。"},"normal":[{"en":"purchase = pur- 'forward' + chase: you chase something forward until it is yours.","cn":"purchase = pur-「向前」+ chase「追」：你一路往前追，直到它归你所有。"},{"en":"The same chase lives in catch and capture: to purchase is to run something down and seize it.","cn":"同一个 chase 也活在 catch 和 capture 里：purchase 就是把东西追到手并抓住。"},{"en":"Sailors purchase an anchor by hauling it up; that is why a good foothold is also called a purchase.","cn":"水手用绞拉的方式 purchase（绞起）锚；所以一个稳的落脚点也叫 purchase（着力点）。"},{"en":"A purchaser is simply the person at the end of the chase, holding the receipt.","cn":"purchaser 不过是追逐终点的那个拿着小票的人。"},{"en":"To purchase peace with blood is the word's oldest logic: the price need not be money.","cn":"以鲜血 purchase 和平，是这个词最古老的逻辑：代价不必是钱。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is possession by pursuit: first you chase, then you hold, and only later do you pay.","cn":"核心是「追而得之」：先追、再抓，最后才付钱。"},{"en":"Money is a late guest in this word, not its host.","cn":"金钱在这个词里是迟到的客人，而不是主人。"},{"en":"Purchase keeps a raider and a shopper in one body: booty, then bargain.","cn":"purchase 把劫掠者和购物者装在同一个身体里：先是战利品，后是讨价还价。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The city purchased the old railway yard and turned it into a park.","cn":"市政府买下了旧铁路场，把它改造成了公园。"},{"en":"Keep your receipt as proof of purchase in case the radio fails.","cn":"留好小票作为购买凭证，以防收音机出故障。"},{"en":"The climber finally got a purchase on the rock and pulled himself over the edge.","cn":"攀登者终于抓牢了岩壁，把自己拉上了边缘。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"pur（向前）+ chase（追）——追上去一把抓住，后来才变成「花钱买下」→ purchase 购买","word":"purchase"},"root":"源自拉丁语系：古法语 porchacier（pur-「向前」+ chacier「追逐」，同 chase）经盎格鲁-法语 purchaser 进入英语，本义「追着取得」，14 世纪中期才特化为「用钱买」；「抓握、着力点」义另出自 16 世纪水手绞锚的航海动词。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses follow one arc: chase, seize, pay, own. The verb starts as 'get by going after', narrows to 'buy', then splits into the object bought, the grip that holds it, the lever point that moves it, and the institution that orders it.","cn":"九个义项沿着一条弧线：追、抓、付、拥有。动词从「追着取得」开始，收窄为「买」，再分出「买到的东西」「攥住它的手」「撬动它的支点」以及「下订单的机构」。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: chasing something down and closing your hand around it.","cn":"核心意象：追着一样东西跑，最后把它攥进手心。"},"chain":["PUR- FORTH","CHASE AFTER","GET IT IN HAND","PAY THE PRICE","SECURE THE TITLE","HOLD AND LEVER"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S02","en":"THE TRANSACTION: ordinary buying, and the formal act of procurement.","cn":"交易：日常购买，以及正式的购置行为。"},{"senses":"S03 · S09","en":"WHAT IS TAKEN: the thing bought, and the old booty seized by force.","cn":"被取走之物：买到的东西，以及旧时武力夺来的战利品。"},{"senses":"S04 · S08","en":"GETTING BY OTHER MEANS: winning through sacrifice, and securing property by title.","cn":"以别的代价取得：用牺牲换来，以及以产权买断。"},{"senses":"S05 · S06","en":"THE GRIP: a firm hold, and the point where a lever bites.","cn":"抓握：牢固的握持，以及杠杆咬住的着力点。"},{"senses":"S07","en":"THE INSTITUTION: purchasing as a department, an order, a process.","cn":"机构：作为部门、订单与流程的采购。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Purchase is pur- plus chacier plus the English noun ending. Its family shows the prefix pur- 'forth', the root chac-/capt- 'to chase, seize', and the suffixes -er, -ing, -able, and re-.","cn":"purchase 是 pur- 加 chacier，再加英语名词词尾。它的词族展示前缀 pur-「向前」、词根 chac-/capt-「追逐、抓取」，以及后缀 -er、-ing、-able 和 re-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Behind chacier stands Vulgar Latin captiare and Latin captare 'to try to catch', from capere 'to take'. The same capere yields capture, captive and catch, so buying and seizing are cousins.","cn":"chacier 背后是通俗拉丁语 captiare 与拉丁语 captare「设法抓住」，源自 capere「拿取」。同一个 capere 还给出 capture、captive、catch，因此「买」与「抓」是表亲。"},"items":[{"word":"purchase","structure":"pur- (forth) + chacier (to chase) + noun use","meaning":"to obtain by chasing, then by paying","meaningCN":"购买（本义追着取得）","example":"They purchased the house in cash.","exampleCN":"他们用现金买下了这栋房子。"},{"word":"purchaser","structure":"purchase + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"the person who buys","meaningCN":"购买者；买主（-er 施事后缀）","example":"The purchaser must be over eighteen.","exampleCN":"购买者必须年满十八岁。"},{"word":"purchasing","structure":"purchase + -ing (noun and participle)","meaning":"the act or department of buying","meaningCN":"采购；购买（-ing 名词化）","example":"She heads the purchasing department.","exampleCN":"她主管采购部。"},{"word":"repurchase","structure":"re- (again, back) + purchase","meaning":"to buy back or buy again","meaningCN":"回购；再购买（re- 再、回）","example":"The firm repurchased two million shares.","exampleCN":"该公司回购了两百万股。"},{"word":"purchasable","structure":"purchase + -able (adjective)","meaning":"able to be bought","meaningCN":"可购得的（-able 形容词后缀）","example":"Tickets are purchasable online only.","exampleCN":"门票只能在网上购买。"},{"word":"chase","structure":"chacier (to hunt, run after)","meaning":"to run after in order to catch","meaningCN":"追逐；追赶（purchase 的后半身）","example":"The dog chased the ball across the lawn.","exampleCN":"狗追着球跑过草坪。"},{"word":"catch","structure":"Vulgar Latin captiare (to chase, seize)","meaning":"to seize something moving","meaningCN":"抓住；接住（chase 的同源双式词）","example":"He caught the falling cup just in time.","exampleCN":"他及时接住了掉下来的杯子。"},{"word":"capture","structure":"Latin capere (to take) + -ure (noun)","meaning":"to take by force; the act of taking","meaningCN":"俘获；夺取（capere 的另一支后裔）","example":"The soldiers captured the bridge at dawn.","exampleCN":"士兵们在黎明夺取了那座桥。"},{"word":"unpurchased","structure":"un- (not) + purchase + -ed (adjective)","meaning":"not yet bought","meaningCN":"未购得的（un- 否定 + -ed）","example":"The unpurchased land stayed wild for decades.","exampleCN":"那块未被买下的土地荒了几十年。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"capere","structure":"capere (verb)","meaning":"to take, seize, grasp","meaningCN":"拿取；抓住；握住"},{"word":"captare","structure":"capere + -tare (frequentative)","meaning":"to try to catch, chase","meaningCN":"设法抓住；追逐"},{"word":"captiare","structure":"Vulgar Latin frequentative of captare","meaning":"to chase, hunt","meaningCN":"追赶；打猎（chacier 的直接来源）"}]}},{"word":"pursue","ipa_uk":"/pəˈsjuː/","ipa_us":"/pərˈsuː/","definition_zh":"追求；追捕；从事；继续进行；起诉；追随；探究；（对某人）热烈追求","definition_en":"to follow someone or something closely, whether to catch it, to continue it, or to win it","core_image":"一个人紧贴着目标的后背跑，目标不停，他也不停——追捕、追梦、追案，都是同一条跑道","scene":"A detective looks down the alley and says: We will pursue this case until the last lead runs out.","sceneCN":"这里 pursue 是「继续办理、坚持追查」（第 4 个义项：把事情一路跟到底）；句意：我们会一直追查这个案子，直到最后一条线索用完。画面里有雨巷、手电和翻开的卷宗。","pos":[{"tag":"v.","zh":"追求；追捕；从事；继续；起诉；追随"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"pursue a career","zh":"从事某种职业"},{"phrase":"pursue a goal","zh":"追求一个目标"},{"phrase":"pursue legal action","zh":"提起诉讼"},{"phrase":"pursue a suspect","zh":"追捕嫌疑人"},{"phrase":"pursue one's studies","zh":"继续深造；从事学业"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"pursues"},{"label":"过去式","form":"pursued"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"pursued"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"pursuing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"pursuit","pos":"n.","zh":"追赶；追求；事务"},{"word":"pursuer","pos":"n.","zh":"追赶者；追求者"},{"word":"pursuing","pos":"adj.","zh":"追赶的；持续追求的"},{"word":"pursuant","pos":"adj.","zh":"依据……的；按照……的"},{"word":"pursuance","pos":"n.","zh":"进行；遵循；从事"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"To go after a goal: keep running toward it","titleCN":"追求目标：一直朝着它跑","definition":"to try to achieve something over time, especially a goal, dream, or interest","definitionCN":"长期努力实现某事，尤指目标、梦想或兴趣","example":"She moved to Berlin to pursue a career in music.","exampleCN":"她搬到柏林去追求音乐事业。","why":"The 'seek, seek to obtain' sense is recorded in English in the late 14c. and was already present in Latin prosequi. A goal is treated as something ahead of you that you follow until you reach it, which is why the verb suits ambitions rather than wishes.","whyCN":"「寻求、力求获得」这一义项在 14 世纪后期见于英语，拉丁语 prosequi 已有此义。目标被当成前方一个可以一路跟随、直到抵达的东西，所以这个词适合形容抱负，而不只是愿望。"},{"no":"02","title":"To chase down: follow with hostile intent","titleCN":"追捕：带着敌意紧跟不放","definition":"to follow someone in order to catch or attack them","definitionCN":"紧跟某人以抓住或攻击他","example":"Police pursued the stolen van through the narrow streets.","exampleCN":"警察在窄巷里追捕那辆被盗的面包车。","why":"This is the word's first English sense (late 13c.): 'follow with hostile intent, follow with a view of overtaking'. The Latin ancestor prosequi meant 'follow after, escort', and hostile pursuit is that following turned aggressive.","whyCN":"这是 pursue 最早的英语义项（13 世纪后期）：「带敌意跟随，意在赶上」。拉丁语祖先 prosequi 意为「跟随、护送」，敌意一起，跟随就变成了追捕。"},{"no":"03","title":"To practise: follow a trade or a subject","titleCN":"从事：把一门职业或学问一路做下去","definition":"to engage in an activity, profession, or course of study over a period","definitionCN":"在一段时间内从事某种活动、职业或学业","example":"He pursued medicine for twelve years before changing fields.","exampleCN":"他从医十二年，之后才转行。","why":"A career or a subject is something you follow along a track rather than seize once. From 'seek to obtain' the verb widened to 'carry on with', and English says pursue medicine the way it says follow a path.","whyCN":"职业或学问是沿着一条轨道跟随的东西，而不是一下子抓住的东西。动词从「力求获得」扩展到「持续进行」，所以英语说 pursue medicine，就像说 follow a path。"},{"no":"04","title":"To carry on: keep a course of action alive","titleCN":"继续：把一件正在做的事做到底","definition":"to continue with an activity, plan, or course of action","definitionCN":"继续进行某项活动、计划或行动方针","example":"The committee will pursue the investigation despite the delay.","exampleCN":"尽管有延误，委员会仍将继续这项调查。","why":"'To proceed, to follow (a path), usually figurative' is recorded from the late 14c., and the sense was already in Latin. Continuing is following without stopping: the route stays, you just keep walking it.","whyCN":"「继续进行、沿着（一条路）走，通常为比喻用法」记录于 14 世纪后期，拉丁语已有此义。继续就是不停步地跟随：路线不变，你只管一直走。"},{"no":"05","title":"To sue: follow a case into court","titleCN":"起诉：把案子一路跟进法庭","definition":"to take legal action over a claim or wrong, to follow a case through the courts","definitionCN":"就某项请求或过错采取法律行动，把案子跟到法庭","example":"The tenant pursued the landlord for the return of the deposit.","exampleCN":"房客起诉房东，要求退还押金。","why":"Legal English says pursue a claim much as it says prosecute: Latin prosequi already meant 'follow up, pursue' and gave both words. A lawsuit is a trail you follow to its end, and the court is where the trail stops.","whyCN":"法律英语说 pursue a claim，与说 prosecute 同理：拉丁语 prosequi 本有「跟进、追究」义，两个词都由此而来。诉讼就是一条跟到底的路线，法庭是这条路线的终点。"},{"no":"06","title":"To accompany: follow as an escort","titleCN":"追随、随行：作为随从跟在后头","definition":"to follow or accompany someone, especially in order to attend or escort them","definitionCN":"跟随或陪伴某人，尤指为了随侍或护送","example":"A small guard pursued the king along the road.","exampleCN":"一小队卫兵沿路跟随国王。","why":"Latin prosequi meant 'follow, accompany, attend; follow after, escort', a neutral sense of being behind someone. English kept mostly the aggressive and goal-seeking branches, but the escort sense survives in the Latin-shaped doubling with prosecute and in formal prose.","whyCN":"拉丁语 prosequi 意为「跟随、陪伴、随侍；跟随、护送」，是「跟在某人后面」的中性义。英语主要保留了攻击性与求取的两支，但「随行」义仍活在 prosecute 等拉丁形同源词和正式文体里。"},{"no":"07","title":"To dig into: follow a question to its source","titleCN":"探究：顺着问题一路挖到源头","definition":"to investigate or examine something further, following a line of inquiry","definitionCN":"进一步调查或研究某事物，沿着一条探究线索走","example":"The researchers pursued the anomaly until they found its cause.","exampleCN":"研究者一路追查这个异常现象，直到找到原因。","why":"An inquiry is a trail: each answer opens the next step. The 'follow' core makes pursue the natural verb for research, where you do not stop at the first clue but keep behind the question.","whyCN":"探究是一条线索：每个答案都打开下一步。「跟随」这个核心让 pursue 成为研究中的自然动词：你不在第一条线索处停下，而是始终坠在问题后面。"},{"no":"08","title":"To court: chase a person, not a thing","titleCN":"追求某人：追的不是事物，是人","definition":"to try persistently to win someone's romantic interest","definitionCN":"坚持不懈地争取某人的爱慕","example":"He pursued her for months before she agreed to a coffee.","exampleCN":"他追了她好几个月，她才答应喝杯咖啡。","why":"The modern romantic sense simply moves the chase from goals and suspects to people. The old hostility is gone, but the structure is identical: someone ahead, you behind, refusing to stop.","whyCN":"现代「追求某人」只是把追逐的对象从目标、嫌疑人换成了人。旧的敌意消失了，结构却一模一样：她在前，你在后，不肯停。"},{"no":"09","title":"To walk a path: follow a route or policy","titleCN":"遵循路径：沿着一条路或方针走","definition":"to follow a path, route, or policy, often figuratively","definitionCN":"沿着一条道路、路线或方针前进，常为比喻用法","example":"The country pursued a policy of neutrality for decades.","exampleCN":"这个国家奉行中立政策数十年。","why":"The literal 'follow a path' sense is old and was already figurative in Latin for a course of action. A policy is a road: pursue it and you stay on it, which is why the verb means both 'walk along' and 'carry out'.","whyCN":"「沿着一条路走」的实指义很古老，在拉丁语里已用于比喻「行动方针」。政策就是一条路：pursue 它就是走在上面，所以这个词既表「沿着走」，也表「奉行」。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Pursue is built from pro- 'forward' and sequi 'to follow'. Its history runs from Latin escorting, through French chasing, to English ambition, litigation, and research — one verb for every kind of following.","cn":"pursue 由 pro-「向前」与 sequi「跟随」构成。它的历史从拉丁语的「随行护送」，经法语的「追赶」，走到英语里的抱负、诉讼与研究——一个动词包揽了所有「跟随」。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1c BC–1c AD)","en":"Prosequi meant 'follow, accompany, attend; follow after, escort; follow up, pursue'. It is pro- 'forward' plus sequi 'to follow'. The deeper PIE root *sekw- 'to follow' is a reconstruction with no written record, so that layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"Prosequi 意为「跟随、陪伴、随侍；跟随、护送；跟进、追究」，由 pro-「向前」加 sequi「跟随」构成。更深的印欧语词根 *sekw-「跟随」是重构形式、没有书面记录，因此那一层标为「来源不确定」。"},{"era":"VULGAR LATIN (date uncertain)","en":"Spoken Latin reshaped the verb into *prosequare, the form behind the French family. The exact date and region of this reshaping are not recorded, so the timing is source uncertain.","cn":"口语拉丁语把这个动词改造成 *prosequare，法语词族即由此而来。这一改造的确切年代与地区没有记录，因此时间标为「来源不确定」。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.)","en":"Poursuir, with the variant porsivre, meant 'to chase, pursue, follow; continue, carry on'. The two strands English later separated — chasing and continuing — were already together in French.","cn":"Poursuir（变体 porsivre）意为「追赶、追求、跟随；继续、进行」。英语后来分开的两条线——追捕与继续——在法语里已经并存。"},{"era":"ANGLO-FRENCH (late 13c.)","en":"Anglo-French pursuer and the English verb appear as 'follow with hostile intent, follow with a view of overtaking'. This is the hunting sense that still dominates police reports.","cn":"盎格鲁-法语 pursuer 与英语动词出现时意为「带敌意跟随，意在赶上」。这就是至今主导警情报道的追捕义。"},{"era":"LATE 14c. ENGLISH","en":"Two quieter senses join: 'to proceed, to follow (a path)', usually figurative for a course of action, and 'to seek, seek to obtain'. Both were already Latin, so English did not invent them; it simply kept more of the parent verb.","cn":"两个更安静的义项加入：「继续进行、沿着（一条路）走」（通常比喻行动方针）与「寻求、力求获得」。两者拉丁语已有，英语并非自创，只是保留了母词更多的义项。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Legal 'pursue a claim' follows the same 'follow it to the end' image, and the 20c. romantic 'pursue someone' moves the chase to people. No new source is involved: both are the old following verb applied to new objects.","cn":"法律用语 pursue a claim 沿用的是同一个「一路跟到底」的意象；20 世纪「追求某人」把追逐对象换成了人。两者都没有新词源，只是那个古老的「跟随」动词用在了新对象上。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"pursuit","ipa":"/pəˈsjuːt/","tag":"same family, noun","definition":"the act of chasing or striving. It is the noun built on pursue, so the resemblance is real.","definitionCN":"追赶；追求。它是 pursue 衍生出的名词，形似是真的。"},{"word":"pursuant","ipa":"/pəˈsjuːənt/","tag":"same family, adjective","definition":"done in accordance with something, as in pursuant to the rules. It keeps the French participle shape.","definitionCN":"依据……的；按照……的（pursuant to the rules）。它保留了法语分词形态。"},{"word":"peruse","ipa":"/pəˈruːz/","tag":"look-alike, unrelated","definition":"to read through carefully. It resembles pursue but comes from a different root.","definitionCN":"细读。它形似 pursue，但词源不同。"},{"word":"purse","ipa":"/pɜːs/","tag":"four letters only","definition":"a small bag for money. It shares the opening pur- and nothing else.","definitionCN":"钱包。它只与 pursue 共享开头的 pur-，别无关联。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"chase","ipa":"/tʃeɪs/","tag":"physical pursuit","definition":"to run after someone or something in order to catch it. It is the plain, physical word.","definitionCN":"追赶；追逐。它是最朴素、最实指的对应词。"},{"word":"follow","ipa":"/ˈfɒləʊ/","tag":"neutral tracking","definition":"to go or come after someone. It lacks the urgency and hostility of pursue.","definitionCN":"跟随。它没有 pursue 那种急迫与敌意。"},{"word":"seek","ipa":"/siːk/","tag":"look for","definition":"to try to find or obtain something. It matches the goal sense but not the chasing.","definitionCN":"寻找；寻求。它对应目标义，但不含追赶。"},{"word":"prosecute","ipa":"/ˈprɒsɪkjuːt/","tag":"legal twin","definition":"to conduct a legal case against someone. It is the Latin-shaped twin of pursue in law.","definitionCN":"起诉；检控。它是 pursue 在法律领域的拉丁形姐妹词。"},{"word":"hunt","ipa":"/hʌnt/","tag":"search with intent","definition":"to chase game or search for something persistently. It stresses effort and prey.","definitionCN":"打猎；搜寻。它强调用力与猎物。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin sequi 'to follow', prosequi 'follow after', and the English family pursuit, pursuant, prosecute.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 sequi「跟随」、prosequi「跟随、追究」，以及英语词族 pursuit、pursuant、prosecute。"},"normal":[{"en":"pursue = pro- 'forward' + sequi 'follow': follow forward, and keep following.","cn":"pursue = pro-「向前」+ sequi「跟随」：向前跟，而且跟到底。"},{"en":"The same sequi gives sequence and consecutive: all of them are about one thing after another.","cn":"同一个 sequi 给出 sequence、consecutive：它们讲的都是一个接一个。"},{"en":"Pursue and prosecute are twins: the same Latin verb, one French-shaped, one Latin-shaped.","cn":"pursue 与 prosecute 是双胞胎：同一个拉丁动词，一个走法语形，一个走拉丁形。"},{"en":"A pursuer is literally 'the one behind you', which is why the word works for detectives and suitors alike.","cn":"pursuer 字面上就是「你身后那个人」，所以它同时适用于侦探和求爱者。"},{"en":"pursuant to the rules means following the rules, with the old participle still visible.","cn":"pursuant to the rules 意为「依据规则」，古老的现在分词仍看得见。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is relative position: the target ahead, the pursuer behind, the gap closing or held.","cn":"核心是相对位置：目标在前，追者在后，距离在缩短或保持。"},{"en":"Every sense keeps the same geometry; only the object changes: a deer, a degree, a lawsuit, a person.","cn":"每个义项都保持同一种几何关系，只换对象：一头鹿、一个学位、一场官司、一个人。"},{"en":"To pursue is never to arrive instantly: the word lives in the interval.","cn":"pursue 从来不是立刻抵达：这个词活在「还没追上」的那段时间里。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She decided to pursue a doctorate in linguistics.","cn":"她决定攻读语言学博士学位。"},{"en":"The guards pursued the escaped prisoner across the field.","cn":"看守们穿过田野追捕那名逃犯。"},{"en":"The company may pursue legal action if the payments stop.","cn":"如果付款停止，公司可能会提起诉讼。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"per（一直）+ sue（告）——一直跟着、一直告下去 → pursue 追赶、追求、起诉","word":"pursue"},"root":"源自拉丁语 prosequi「跟随、随行、追究」，由 pro-「向前」+ sequi「跟随」构成；经法语 porsivre/poursuir 进入英语，核心始终是「跟在后面、一路不停」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses, one geometry: something is ahead of you and you keep after it. Whether it is a suspect, a career, an investigation, a policy, or a person, the verb never changes direction — only what is being followed.","cn":"九个义项，一种几何关系：一样东西在你前面，你一路跟着。无论那是嫌疑人、职业、调查、政策还是一个人，这个动词的方向从不改变，变的只是被跟随的对象。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: staying behind a moving target and refusing to let the gap open.","cn":"核心意象：始终坠在一个移动的目标后面，不让距离拉开。"},"chain":["PRO- FORWARD","SEQUI FOLLOW","CLOSE THE GAP","KEEP IT GOING","SEEK TO WIN","FOLLOW UP IN COURT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S07","en":"THE GOAL AHEAD: ambition, and the inquiry that follows a question to its source.","cn":"前方的目标：抱负，以及顺着问题追到源头的探究。"},{"senses":"S02 · S08","en":"THE LIVING QUARRY: hunting a suspect, and courting a person.","cn":"活的猎物：追捕嫌疑人，以及追求一个人。"},{"senses":"S03 · S04","en":"CARRYING ON: practising a profession, and continuing a course of action.","cn":"持续进行：从事一门职业，以及继续一项行动。"},{"senses":"S05","en":"THE CASE: following a claim all the way into court.","cn":"案子：把一项请求一路跟进法庭。"},{"senses":"S06 · S09","en":"THE PATH: escorting someone, and walking a route or policy.","cn":"路径：随行护送某人，以及沿一条路线或方针前行。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Pursue is pro- plus sequ- plus the French verb ending. Its family shows the prefix pro- 'forward', the root sequ- 'follow', and the suffixes -er, -ant, -ance, and -ing.","cn":"pursue 是 pro- 加 sequ- 再加法语动词词尾。它的词族展示前缀 pro-「向前」、词根 sequ-「跟随」，以及后缀 -er、-ant、-ance、-ing。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin sequi 'to follow' is the base of prosequi 'follow after' and of the English words sequence, consecutive and prosecute. The French branch softened -sequ- into -su-.","cn":"拉丁语 sequi「跟随」是 prosequi「跟随、追究」的基础，也是英语 sequence、consecutive、prosecute 的基础。法语一支把 -sequ- 软化成了 -su-。"},"items":[{"word":"pursue","structure":"pro- (forward) + sequi (to follow) via French","meaning":"to follow after, whether to catch or to continue","meaningCN":"追求；追捕；继续进行（向前跟随）","example":"He pursued the goal for ten years.","exampleCN":"他为这个目标追求了十年。"},{"word":"pursuit","structure":"pursue + -it (French noun ending)","meaning":"the act of chasing or striving","meaningCN":"追赶；追求（名词）","example":"The pursuit lasted three hours.","exampleCN":"追捕持续了三个小时。"},{"word":"pursuer","structure":"pursue + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"one who follows or chases","meaningCN":"追赶者；追求者（-er 施事后缀）","example":"The pursuer lost the trail in the rain.","exampleCN":"追赶者在雨里失去了踪迹。"},{"word":"pursuant","structure":"pursue + -ant (present participle)","meaning":"following from; in accordance with","meaningCN":"依据……的；按照……的（-ant 分词后缀）","example":"Pursuant to the contract, notice must be written.","exampleCN":"依据合同，通知必须以书面形式发出。"},{"word":"pursuance","structure":"pursue + -ance (noun)","meaning":"the carrying out of a plan or duty","meaningCN":"进行；履行（-ance 名词后缀）","example":"He acted in pursuance of his instructions.","exampleCN":"他按照指示行事。"},{"word":"prosecute","structure":"pro- + sequi + -ate (Latin-shaped twin)","meaning":"to follow up a case in court","meaningCN":"起诉；检控（pursue 的拉丁形姐妹词）","example":"The state prosecuted him for fraud.","exampleCN":"州政府以欺诈罪起诉他。"},{"word":"sue","structure":"Old French suer, from Latin sequi","meaning":"to take legal action; to follow in court","meaningCN":"起诉；诉讼（sequi 的又一后裔）","example":"She sued the company for damages.","exampleCN":"她起诉该公司要求赔偿。"},{"word":"suit","structure":"Old French suite, from sequi (a following)","meaning":"a set that follows; a legal case","meaningCN":"一套；诉讼（「跟随而来的一组」）","example":"He filed a suit against his former partner.","exampleCN":"他对前合伙人提起了诉讼。"},{"word":"sequence","structure":"sequi + -ence (noun)","meaning":"a series of things following one another","meaningCN":"顺序；序列（一个接一个跟随）","example":"Arrange the events in the correct sequence.","exampleCN":"按正确顺序排列这些事件。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"sequi","structure":"sequi (deponent verb)","meaning":"to follow","meaningCN":"跟随"},{"word":"prosequi","structure":"pro- + sequi","meaning":"to follow after, escort, pursue","meaningCN":"跟随；护送；追究"},{"word":"*prosequare","structure":"Vulgar Latin reshaping of prosequi","meaning":"to follow, chase (source of French poursuir)","meaningCN":"跟随、追赶（法语 poursuir 的来源，形式为重构）"}]}},{"word":"qualitative","ipa_uk":"/ˈkwɒlɪtətɪv/","ipa_us":"/ˈkwɑːləteɪtɪv/","definition_zh":"定性的；性质上的；质的；描述性的；非量化的；品质层面的；（化学）定性分析的","definition_en":"relating to qualities or to the kind of thing something is, rather than to how much of it there is","core_image":"不去数篮子里有几个苹果，而是拿起每一个看颜色、尝味道、摸质地——只问「什么样」，不问「多少」","scene":"A researcher closes the spreadsheet and says: The interviews are qualitative data, so we describe themes instead of counting answers.","sceneCN":"这里 qualitative 是「描述性的、非量化的」（第 4 个义项：用文字描述而不计量）；句意：访谈属于定性数据，所以我们描述主题，而不是统计答案。画面里有录音笔、被高亮的文本和合上的表格。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"定性的；性质（上）的；质的；描述性的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"qualitative research","zh":"定性研究"},{"phrase":"qualitative analysis","zh":"定性分析"},{"phrase":"qualitative data","zh":"定性数据"},{"phrase":"a qualitative difference","zh":"质的差别"},{"phrase":"qualitative change","zh":"质变"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more qualitative"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most qualitative"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"qualitatively","pos":"adv.","zh":"定性地；从性质上"},{"word":"quality","pos":"n.","zh":"质量；品质；特性"},{"word":"qualify","pos":"v.","zh":"使具有资格；限定"},{"word":"qualification","pos":"n.","zh":"资格；限定条件"},{"word":"qualified","pos":"adj.","zh":"有资格的；有限定的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Qualitative research: study by description","titleCN":"定性研究：靠描述做学问","definition":"using observation, interviews, or written accounts rather than measurement to study something","definitionCN":"用观察、访谈或文字记述来研究，而不是用测量","example":"The team ran a qualitative study of how nurses talk to patients.","exampleCN":"团队开展了一项定性研究，考察护士如何与病人交谈。","why":"The word was coined in early 15c. as 'that produces a quality'; only around 1600 did it mean 'concerned with quality without reference to quantity'. Research methods took that second sense and made it a name for work that records kinds and meanings instead of numbers.","whyCN":"这个词在 15 世纪初造出时意为「产生某种性质的」；直到约 1600 年才表示「只关性质、不涉数量」。研究方法取了这个义项，用它命名记录种类与意义、而非数字的工作。"},{"no":"02","title":"Of a quality: belonging to what something is","titleCN":"性质上的：属于「它是什么」的那一面","definition":"relating to a quality or qualities that something possesses","definitionCN":"关于某物所具有的性质或属性的","example":"Heat and cold are qualitative states of the air, not amounts of it.","exampleCN":"冷与热是空气的性质状态，而不是空气的量。","why":"Medieval Latin qualitativus meant 'relating to quality', built on qualitas. The adjective simply points at the property itself: not how much, but what sort.","whyCN":"中世纪拉丁语 qualitativus 意为「关于性质的」，由 qualitas 构成。这个形容词只是指向性质本身：不是多少，而是何种。"},{"no":"03","title":"Qualitative difference: a difference in kind","titleCN":"质的差别：种类上的不同","definition":"describing a difference in kind, character, or nature rather than in degree or amount","definitionCN":"指种类、性质或本性上的差别，而非程度或数量上的","example":"There is a qualitative difference between being tired and being ill.","exampleCN":"「累」和「病」之间有质的差别。","why":"Once the adjective means 'concerned with quality alone', two things can differ in quality rather than quantity. This is the sense that lets English oppose qualitative to quantitative as two kinds of difference.","whyCN":"一旦这个形容词表示「只关乎性质」，两样东西就可以在性质上而非数量上不同。正是这个义项让英语把 qualitative 与 quantitative 对立成两种差别。"},{"no":"04","title":"Qualitative data: words, not figures","titleCN":"定性数据：是文字，不是数字","definition":"consisting of descriptions, words, images, or observations rather than numerical measurements","definitionCN":"由描述、文字、图像或观察构成，而不是数值测量","example":"The report mixes qualitative field notes with a few simple counts.","exampleCN":"这份报告把定性的田野笔记与少量简单计数混在一起。","why":"Data can be sorted by what it is: numbers measure amount, words record kind. The adjective's 'without reference to quantity' sense gives the label for the second pile.","whyCN":"数据可以按「是什么」分类：数字测量数量，文字记录种类。这个形容词「不涉数量」的义项正好为第二堆数据提供了名称。"},{"no":"05","title":"Quality-level: better in kind, not bigger","titleCN":"品质层面：好在质地，而非更大","definition":"relating to the standard or excellence of something rather than its size or amount","definitionCN":"关于某物的水准或优良程度，而非大小或数量","example":"The reform brought a qualitative improvement in care, not more beds.","exampleCN":"这项改革带来的是护理品质的提升，而不是更多床位。","why":"From 'relating to quality' comes the evaluative use: a qualitative gain is a gain in how good something is. English keeps quality for both 'property' and 'excellence', and the adjective follows both.","whyCN":"从「关于性质」引申出评价用法：qualitative 的提升就是「好在哪」的提升。英语的 quality 兼指「属性」与「优良」，这个形容词两条都跟着走。"},{"no":"06","title":"Qualitative analysis: find out what is there","titleCN":"定性分析：先查明「有什么」","definition":"in chemistry, identifying the substances present in a sample without measuring how much of each there is","definitionCN":"化学中鉴定样品里存在哪些物质，而不测定各有多少","example":"Qualitative analysis showed the powder contained lead.","exampleCN":"定性分析显示这种粉末含铅。","why":"Chemistry splits the question in two: what is it, and how much. The first question asks for kind, so it takes the adjective of quality; quantitative takes the question of amount.","whyCN":"化学把问题一分为二：这是什么，有多少。第一个问的是种类，于是用「性质」的形容词；第二个问数量，才用 quantitative。"},{"no":"07","title":"Qualitative change: a leap into another state","titleCN":"质变：跃入另一种状态","definition":"in philosophy, a change in the essential nature of something, as opposed to a change only in amount","definitionCN":"哲学上指事物根本本性的变化，与仅数量上的变化相对","example":"The textbook describes water turning to steam as a qualitative change.","exampleCN":"这本教材把水变成蒸汽描述为一种质变。","why":"Aristotelian philosophy used qualitas for one of its categories; English inherited that seriousness. If a thing changes in kind and not merely in degree, the change is qualitative — a new state, not a larger old one.","whyCN":"亚里士多德哲学把 qualitas 当作范畴之一，英语继承了这份严肃。当事物在种类上而非仅在程度上改变，这变化就是 qualitative 的——是新状态，而不是旧状态的加量。"},{"no":"08","title":"Qualitative judgement: the feel of a thing","titleCN":"定性判断：凭手感下的结论","definition":"based on impressions, experience, or observed character rather than on exact measurement","definitionCN":"基于印象、经验或观察到的特性，而非精确测量","example":"The chef made a qualitative judgement about the sauce by tasting it.","exampleCN":"厨师尝了一口，对酱汁作出了定性判断。","why":"Where numbers are unavailable, judgement still works by noticing qualities: colour, texture, tone. The adjective names that kind of knowing — real but not countable.","whyCN":"没有数字可用时，判断仍可靠察觉性质来运作：颜色、质地、味道。这个形容词命名的就是这种「真实但数不清」的认识方式。"},{"no":"09","title":"A qualitative adjective: naming a quality","titleCN":"性质形容词：直接命名一种性质","definition":"in grammar, an adjective that describes a quality of a noun, such as wooden, kind, or heavy","definitionCN":"语法上指描述名词性质的形容词，如 wooden、kind、heavy","example":"Wooden is a qualitative adjective, while this in this table is not.","exampleCN":"wooden 是性质形容词，而 this table 里的 this 不是。","why":"Grammarians needed a word for adjectives that assign a quality rather than point, count, or relate. They borrowed the adjective of quality itself: a qualitative adjective is one that says what kind.","whyCN":"语法学家需要一个词来指「赋予性质」而非指认、计数或关联的形容词，于是借用了「性质」这个形容词本身：qualitative adjective 就是说明「何种」的那类形容词。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Qualitative descends from the Latin question qualis, 'of what kind?' Cicero coined qualitas to render Greek poiotēs, and Medieval Latin added the adjective. English first used it for 'producing a quality' and only around 1600 for 'concerned with quality, not quantity'.","cn":"qualitative 源自拉丁语的提问词 qualis「何种？」。西塞罗造出 qualitas 来翻译希腊语 poiotēs，中世纪拉丁语又加上形容词形式。英语先用它表「产生某种性质的」，到约 1600 年才表「只关性质、不涉数量」。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1c BC)","en":"Qualis was the correlative question word 'of what kind? what sort of?'. Its deeper PIE root *kwo-, the stem of relative and interrogative pronouns, is a reconstruction with no written record, so that layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"Qualis 是关联疑问词「何种的？哪一类的？」。它更深的印欧语词根 *kwo-（关系代词与疑问代词词干）是重构形式，没有书面记录，因此那一层标为「来源不确定」。"},{"era":"LATIN (1c BC)","en":"Qualitas 'a quality, property; nature, state, condition' is said to have been coined by Cicero to translate Greek poiotēs. The word therefore begins as a philosopher's loan-translation, not a folk term.","cn":"Qualitas「性质、属性；本性、状态、状况」据说由西塞罗造出，用来翻译希腊语 poiotēs。因此这个词一开始就是哲学家的仿译词，而非民间口语。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN (14c.)","en":"Qualitativus 'relating to quality' supplied the adjective. The suffix -ivus marks 'belonging to or having the nature of', the same ending that gives English -ive.","cn":"Qualitativus「关于性质的」提供了形容词形式。后缀 -ivus 表示「属于……或有……性质的」，正是英语 -ive 的来源。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH → early 15c. ENGLISH","en":"English first records qualitative as qualitatif in the early 15c., meaning 'that produces a (physical) quality'. The word described causes, not methods: a quality-producing agent.","cn":"英语最早记录为 15 世纪初的 qualitatif，意为「产生（物理）性质的」。这个词当时描述的是原因而非方法：一个产生性质的动因。"},{"era":"c. 1600 ENGLISH","en":"The modern sense 'concerned with quality, relating to the possession of qualities without reference to quantities' appears about 1600, from French qualitatif or Medieval Latin qualitativus. Quantity drops out, and kind stands alone.","cn":"现代义「关于性质的、只涉及是否具有性质而不涉数量」约在 1600 年出现，来自法语 qualitatif 或中世纪拉丁语 qualitativus。数量退场，只剩下种类。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The adjective became the standard partner and opposite of quantitative in research writing. This pairing is a modern intellectual arrangement, not a separate etymology: the same Latin word simply had its 'not quantity' sense put to work.","cn":"这个形容词在现代研究写作中成为 quantitative 的标准搭档与对立面。这种配对是近代的思想安排，而非另一套词源：同一个拉丁词只是让它的「非数量」义发挥了作用。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"quantitative","ipa":"/ˈkwɒntɪtətɪv/","tag":"the mirror opposite","definition":"relating to quantity or amount. It differs from qualitative by two letters and by the whole question it asks.","definitionCN":"关于数量或数额的。它与 qualitative 只差几个字母，但问的是完全不同的问题。"},{"word":"quality","ipa":"/ˈkwɒləti/","tag":"the parent noun","definition":"the property or standard of something. Qualitative is the adjective built on it.","definitionCN":"性质；质量。qualitative 正是由它构成的形容词。"},{"word":"qualified","ipa":"/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪd/","tag":"same qual- stem","definition":"having the necessary training or a stated limitation. It belongs to qualify, not to quality.","definitionCN":"有资格的；有限定的。它属于 qualify，而不是 quality。"},{"word":"qualifier","ipa":"/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪə/","tag":"same qual- stem","definition":"a word or person that limits or qualifies. Another branch of the qual- family.","definitionCN":"限定词；取得资格者。qual- 词族的另一支。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"descriptive","ipa":"/dɪˈskrɪptɪv/","tag":"says what, not how much","definition":"giving an account of what something is like rather than measuring it.","definitionCN":"描述某物是什么样子，而非测量它。"},{"word":"subjective","ipa":"/səbˈdʒektɪv/","tag":"based on the observer","definition":"resting on personal feeling or judgement rather than external measurement.","definitionCN":"基于个人感受或判断，而非外部测量。"},{"word":"impressionistic","ipa":"/ɪmˌpreʃəˈnɪstɪk/","tag":"overall feel","definition":"based on broad impressions rather than exact detail or figures.","definitionCN":"基于整体印象，而非精确细节或数据。"},{"word":"interpretive","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɜːprətɪv/","tag":"reads for meaning","definition":"concerned with explaining meaning, as qualitative research does with interviews and texts.","definitionCN":"着力解释意义的，正如定性研究处理访谈与文本那样。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin qualis 'of what kind', qualitas 'quality', and the English family quality, qualify, qualitative.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 qualis「何种」、qualitas「性质」，以及英语词族 quality、qualify、qualitative。"},"normal":[{"en":"qualitative = quality + -ative: it is the adjective of quality, just as quantitative is the adjective of quantity.","cn":"qualitative = quality + -ative：它是 quality 的形容词，正如 quantitative 是 quantity 的形容词。"},{"en":"Qualis asks 'of what kind?', which is exactly what qualitative research tries to answer.","cn":"qualis 问的是「何种？」，这正是定性研究想回答的问题。"},{"en":"One letter cluster separates the twins: qual- asks what kind, quant- asks how much.","cn":"一对孪生词只差一簇字母：qual- 问「何种」，quant- 问「多少」。"},{"en":"Cicero made qualitas to translate Greek poiotēs, so the word has a philosopher's fingerprint on it.","cn":"西塞罗造 qualitas 来翻译希腊语 poiotēs，所以这个词上留着哲学家的指纹。"},{"en":"A qualitative adjective such as wooden tells you what kind, not how many.","cn":"像 wooden 这样的性质形容词告诉你「何种」，而不是「几个」。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is a question, not a measurement: what is it like?","cn":"核心是一个提问，而不是一次测量：它是什么样子的？"},{"en":"Quality describes the inside of a thing; quantity describes its outside size.","cn":"性质描述一个东西的内部，数量描述它的外部大小。"},{"en":"Everything qualitative can be said in words but not always put on a scale.","cn":"定性的东西都能用话讲清楚，却不一定能放上秤。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The study combines qualitative interviews with a large survey.","cn":"这项研究把定性访谈与大规模问卷调查结合起来。"},{"en":"There is a qualitative difference between solving a puzzle and understanding it.","cn":"解出一道谜题与真正理解它之间存在质的差别。"},{"en":"Qualitative analysis identified the metal but did not measure its amount.","cn":"定性分析查明了那种金属，但没有测定它的含量。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"quality（质量）+ -ative（……的）——不问多少，只问「什么质地」→ qualitative 定性的","word":"qualitative"},"root":"源自拉丁语 qualis「何种的」，西塞罗据以造出 qualitas「性质」，中世纪拉丁语 qualitativus「关于性质的」经法语进入英语；核心是「问种类、问质地，而不问数量」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses, all variations of one question: what kind is it? The word starts as 'producing a quality', becomes 'about quality rather than quantity', and then serves research methods, chemistry, philosophy, and grammar.","cn":"九个义项都是同一个提问的变奏：它属于何种？这个词从「产生性质」开始，变成「关于性质而非数量」，随后服务于研究方法、化学、哲学与语法。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: looking at what a thing is like instead of weighing how much of it there is.","cn":"核心意象：去看一个东西是什么样子，而不是去称它有多少。"},"chain":["QUALIS: WHAT KIND","QUALITAS: THE PROPERTY","QUALITY IN ENGLISH","-ATIVE: RELATING TO","QUANTITY SET ASIDE","DESCRIBE THE KIND"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S04","en":"METHOD AND DATA: study by description, and words rather than figures.","cn":"方法与数据：以描述做研究，用文字而非数字。"},{"senses":"S02 · S03","en":"PROPERTY AND KIND: what a thing possesses, and differences in kind.","cn":"属性与种类：事物具有的性质，以及种类上的差别。"},{"senses":"S05 · S07","en":"STANDARD AND STATE: improvement in excellence, and change into another state.","cn":"水准与状态：品质上的提升，以及跃入另一种状态的变化。"},{"senses":"S06","en":"WHAT IS PRESENT: chemical identification without measurement.","cn":"有什么：不作测量的化学鉴定。"},{"senses":"S08 · S09","en":"JUDGEMENT AND GRAMMAR: the feel of a thing, and the adjective that names a quality.","cn":"判断与语法：凭手感下的结论，以及命名性质的形容词。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Qualitative is qual- plus -itative. Its family shows the question stem qual- 'what kind', the noun suffix -ity, the verb suffix -ify, and the adjective endings -ed, -ative and -ly.","cn":"qualitative 是 qual- 加 -itative。它的词族展示疑问词干 qual-「何种」、名词后缀 -ity、动词后缀 -ify，以及形容词词尾 -ed、-ative 和 -ly。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin qualis 'of what kind' gives qualitas 'quality', then Medieval Latin qualitativus. The same stem, through qualificare, gives qualify and qualification.","cn":"拉丁语 qualis「何种」给出 qualitas「性质」，再给出中世纪拉丁语 qualitativus。同一个词干经 qualificare 又给出 qualify 与 qualification。"},"items":[{"word":"qualitative","structure":"qualitas (quality) + -ative (adjective)","meaning":"relating to quality, not quantity","meaningCN":"定性的；性质上的（-ative 形容词后缀）","example":"They chose a qualitative approach for the interviews.","exampleCN":"他们对访谈采用了定性方法。"},{"word":"quality","structure":"Latin qualitas, from qualis (of what kind)","meaning":"property, character, or degree of excellence","meaningCN":"性质；品质；质量","example":"The quality of the paper is excellent.","exampleCN":"纸张的质量非常好。"},{"word":"qualify","structure":"qualis + -ificare (to make)","meaning":"to make fit; to limit or modify","meaningCN":"使有资格；限定（qualis + 使……）","example":"This course qualifies you to teach music.","exampleCN":"这门课程使你具备教音乐的资格。"},{"word":"qualification","structure":"qualify + -ication (noun)","meaning":"a certificate, condition, or limiting statement","meaningCN":"资格；限定条件（-ication 名词后缀）","example":"She has the qualifications for the post.","exampleCN":"她具备担任该职位的资格。"},{"word":"qualified","structure":"qualify + -ed (adjective)","meaning":"having met the required standard","meaningCN":"合格的；有资格的（-ed 形容词后缀）","example":"He is a qualified electrician.","exampleCN":"他是一名合格的电工。"},{"word":"qualifier","structure":"qualify + -er (agent or noun)","meaning":"one who qualifies, or a word that limits","meaningCN":"取得资格者；限定词（-er 后缀）","example":"Very is a qualifier in very cold.","exampleCN":"very 在 very cold 中是限定词。"},{"word":"disqualify","structure":"dis- (away, not) + qualify","meaning":"to make unfit or declare ineligible","meaningCN":"取消资格（dis- 否定 + qualify）","example":"The runner was disqualified for a false start.","exampleCN":"那名跑者因抢跑被取消资格。"},{"word":"unqualified","structure":"un- (not) + qualified","meaning":"lacking qualifications; complete and absolute","meaningCN":"无资格的；彻底的、无保留的（un- 否定）","example":"She gave the plan unqualified support.","exampleCN":"她毫无保留地支持这项计划。"},{"word":"qualitatively","structure":"qualitative + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in terms of quality, not amount","meaningCN":"定性地；从性质上（-ly 副词后缀）","example":"The two systems differ qualitatively.","exampleCN":"这两个系统在性质上不同。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"qualis","structure":"qualis (interrogative and relative adjective)","meaning":"of what kind? what sort of?","meaningCN":"何种的？哪一类的？"},{"word":"qualitas","structure":"qualis + -itas (noun)","meaning":"quality, property, nature","meaningCN":"性质；属性；本性"},{"word":"qualitativus","structure":"qualitas + -ivus (adjective)","meaning":"relating to quality","meaningCN":"关于性质的"}]}},{"word":"quality","ipa_uk":"/ˈkwɒləti/","ipa_us":"/ˈkwɑːləti/","definition_zh":"质量；品质；品性；特性；优质；（声音的）音色；身份地位；（哲学的）性质；严肃报刊的高品位","definition_en":"the character or nature of a thing, its degree of goodness, or a particular property that belongs to it","core_image":"同一块布，手指一捻就知道它的织法与手感——先问「它是什么质地」，再判断「它好不好」","scene":"At a concert the violinist draws the bow and whispers: Listen to the quality of that tone.","sceneCN":"这里 quality 是「音色、音质」（第 5 个义项：声音的质地）；句意：听听那个音的音色。画面里有琴弓、谱架和微微颤动的琴弦。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"质量；品质；特性；优质；音色；身份"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"high quality","zh":"高质量；高品质"},{"phrase":"quality of life","zh":"生活质量"},{"phrase":"quality control","zh":"质量控制"},{"phrase":"quality time","zh":"（与家人等的）宝贵相处时间"},{"phrase":"of good quality","zh":"质量好的"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"qualities"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"qualitative","pos":"adj.","zh":"定性的；性质上的"},{"word":"qualify","pos":"v.","zh":"使有资格；限定"},{"word":"qualification","pos":"n.","zh":"资格；限定条件"},{"word":"qualified","pos":"adj.","zh":"有资格的；合格"},{"word":"qualifier","pos":"n.","zh":"限定词；取得资格者"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Quality: how good or bad a thing is","titleCN":"质量：一样东西好到什么程度","definition":"the standard of something when it is compared with other things of the same kind","definitionCN":"某物与同类事物相比较时所达到的水准","example":"The quality of the soil decides what will grow there.","exampleCN":"土壤的质量决定那里能种什么。","why":"'Degree of goodness or excellence' is recorded from the late 14c., beside the older 'inherent attribute'. Once you know what a thing is like, you can rank it: the property becomes a standard of goodness.","whyCN":"「优良程度」记录于 14 世纪后期，与更早的「固有属性」并存。一旦知道一个东西是什么样子，就能给它排序：属性于是变成了衡量好坏的标准。"},{"no":"02","title":"Character: the temper inside a person","titleCN":"品性：一个人内里的性情","definition":"the nature, character, or disposition of a person or thing","definitionCN":"人或事物的本性、性格或性情","example":"She has a quality of calm that steadies everyone around her.","exampleCN":"她有一种沉静的品性，能让身边的人都安定下来。","why":"The word's first English sense (c.1300) was 'temperament, character, disposition', borrowed from Old French calite. A person's quality was not a rating but the kind of person they were.","whyCN":"这个词最早的英语义项（约 1300 年）是「性情、性格、禀性」，借自古法语 calite。一个人的 quality 不是评分，而是他属于哪一种人。"},{"no":"03","title":"An attribute: a property that belongs to it","titleCN":"特性：附着在它身上的属性","definition":"a particular property or feature that belongs to a person or thing","definitionCN":"属于某人或某物的特定属性或特点","example":"Patience is one of the qualities a good teacher needs.","exampleCN":"耐心是好老师所需要的品质之一。","why":"From the late 14c. quality also named 'an inherent attribute', a single property considered on its own. This is the countable sense: a thing can have many qualities, and you can list them.","whyCN":"从 14 世纪后期起，quality 也指「固有属性」，即单独看待的某一项性质。这是可数的义项：一样东西可以有许多 qualities，你可以一条条列出来。"},{"no":"04","title":"Quality goods: the label of excellence","titleCN":"优质：把「好」直接贴成标签","definition":"used before a noun to mean of high grade or superior excellence","definitionCN":"用在名词前，表示高档、优良","example":"The shop sells quality leather at fair prices.","exampleCN":"这家店以公道价格出售优质皮革。","why":"'A distinguished and characteristic excellence' is recorded from the 1580s. English then did what it often does: it put the noun in front of another noun, so quality leather means leather marked by that excellence.","whyCN":"「突出的、标志性的优良」记录于 16 世纪 80 年代。英语随后做了它常做的事：把名词放到另一个名词前，于是 quality leather 就是被这种优良标记的皮革。"},{"no":"05","title":"Timbre: the quality of a sound","titleCN":"音色：声音的质地","definition":"the character of a sound or tone, especially its timbre as distinct from pitch or loudness","definitionCN":"声音或音调的特性，尤指区别于音高与响度的音色","example":"The old piano has a warm quality that new ones lack.","exampleCN":"这架旧钢琴有一种新琴所没有的温暖音色。","why":"Sounds also have qualities: a violin's tone is recognised by its kind, not its volume. Musicians simply applied the general word for 'what it is like' to hearing, and quality became timbre in that context.","whyCN":"声音也有性质：小提琴的音靠「何种」而被辨认，而不是靠音量。音乐家只是把泛指「它是什么样」的词用到了听觉上，quality 在语境里就成了音色。"},{"no":"06","title":"Rank: quality as social standing","titleCN":"身份：作为社会等级的品质","definition":"high social position or rank, especially in the phrase the quality meaning people of rank","definitionCN":"高的社会地位或等级，尤用于 the quality 指有身份的人","example":"In the old novel, the quality sat apart from the servants.","exampleCN":"在那部旧小说里，有身份的人与仆人分开坐。","why":"'Social rank, position' is recorded from c.1400, hence 'nobility, gentry'. A person's kind and birth were once read as the same fact, so quality could name the class itself: the quality were the people of good quality.","whyCN":"「社会等级、地位」记录于约 1400 年，因而有「贵族、士绅」义。从前一个人的种类与出身被看作同一件事，所以 quality 可以指这个阶层本身：the quality 就是「有好品质的人」。"},{"no":"07","title":"A category: quality in philosophy","titleCN":"性质：哲学里的一大范畴","definition":"in philosophy, that by which a thing is said to be of a certain sort, one of the basic categories of Aristotle","definitionCN":"哲学上指使事物成为某种样子的东西，亚里士多德的基本范畴之一","example":"The lecture asked whether colour is a quality or a relation.","exampleCN":"讲座讨论颜色究竟是一种性质还是一种关系。","why":"Cicero coined Latin qualitas to translate Greek poiotēs 'of what sort', and the word entered English still carrying Aristotelian philosophy. This is the technical sense behind every later 'property of a thing'.","whyCN":"西塞罗造拉丁语 qualitas 来译希腊语 poiotēs「何种」，这个词进入英语时仍带着亚里士多德哲学。它就是后来一切「事物的属性」背后的技术义。"},{"no":"08","title":"Quality of a proposition: yes or no","titleCN":"命题的质：肯定还是否定","definition":"in logic, the affirmative or negative character of a proposition","definitionCN":"逻辑学中一个命题是肯定还是否定的性质","example":"The two statements share a subject but differ in quality.","exampleCN":"这两个陈述主语相同，但「质」不同。","why":"Logicians inherited the Aristotelian category and asked whether a proposition affirms or denies. That yes-or-no character is its quality, as opposed to its quantity (all, some). The Chinese term for quality keeps the same metaphor.","whyCN":"逻辑学家继承了亚里士多德的范畴，追问一个命题是肯定还是否定。这个「是/否」的性格就是它的 quality，区别于 quantity（全称、特称）。中文译作「质」，保留同一个隐喻。"},{"no":"09","title":"The quality press: seriousness as a label","titleCN":"严肃报刊：把「有品」贴在报纸上","definition":"in British journalism, newspapers of serious content and high standard, as in quality papers or the quality press","definitionCN":"英国新闻界指内容严肃、水准较高的报纸，如 quality papers 或 the quality press","example":"The story ran in the quality press before the tabloids picked it up.","exampleCN":"这条报道先出现在严肃报刊上，后来小报才跟进。","why":"The attributive use of quality did not stay with goods. Journalism borrowed it to grade readers and tone: quality papers are the ones marked by seriousness, the opposite of the tabloids. The old label-making sense simply moved from leather to newsprint.","whyCN":"quality 作定语并不限于货物。新闻业借它来给读者与格调分级：quality papers 就是以严肃为标志的报纸，与小报相对。那个古老的「贴标签」义，只是从皮革搬到了新闻纸。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Quality begins with a Latin question word, qualis, 'of what kind?'. Cicero turned it into a noun for a philosophical category, and English broadened that noun into character, attribute, goodness, rank, timbre, and finally the tone of a newspaper.","cn":"quality 起于拉丁疑问词 qualis「何种？」。西塞罗把它变成指哲学范畴的名词，英语又把这个名词一路扩展为性情、属性、优良、身份、音色，最后甚至指报纸的格调。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1c BC)","en":"Qualis was the interrogative and relative adjective 'of what kind? what sort of?'. Its PIE root *kwo-, the stem of pronouns like who and what, is a reconstruction without written record, so that layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"Qualis 是疑问与关系形容词「何种的？哪一类的？」。它的印欧语词根 *kwo-（who、what 等代词的词干）是重构形式，没有书面记录，因此那一层标为「来源不确定」。"},{"era":"LATIN (1c BC)","en":"Qualitas 'a quality, property; nature, state, condition' is said to have been coined by Cicero to translate Greek poiotēs. It entered philosophy as a category term before it ever described a person or a product.","cn":"Qualitas「性质、属性；本性、状态、状况」据说由西塞罗造出以译希腊语 poiotēs。它先作为哲学范畴词进入语言，之后才用来形容人或产品。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.)","en":"Old French calite, qualite meant 'quality, nature, characteristic' (Modern French qualité). The French form explains why English first spelled the word with a c.","cn":"古法语 calite、qualite 意为「性质、本性、特征」（现代法语 qualité）。法语形式解释了英语早期为何把这个词拼作 c 开头。"},{"era":"c. 1300 ENGLISH","en":"The noun is first recorded as 'temperament, character, disposition', used with awareness of its place in Aristotelian philosophy. A person's quality was the sort of person they were, not a score.","cn":"名词最早记录为「性情、性格、禀性」，使用时仍意识到它在亚里士多德哲学中的位置。一个人的 quality 是他属于哪种人，而不是分数。"},{"era":"LATE 14c.–c. 1400 ENGLISH","en":"New senses multiply: 'an inherent attribute' and 'degree of goodness or excellence' from the late 14c., 'social rank, position' c.1400, hence 'nobility, gentry'. The same noun now covers what a thing has, how good it is, and who a person is.","cn":"新义项接连出现：14 世纪后期的「固有属性」与「优良程度」，约 1400 年的「社会等级、地位」，进而指「贵族、士绅」。同一个名词此时兼管：事物有什么、有多好、人是什么身份。"},{"era":"1580s–1977 ENGLISH","en":"'A distinguished and characteristic excellence' is from the 1580s, which made quality usable before nouns (quality goods). Modern compounds follow: quality control (1935), quality of life (1943), quality time (1977).","cn":"「突出的、标志性的优良」始于 16 世纪 80 年代，使 quality 可以放在名词前（quality goods）。现代复合词随后出现：quality control（1935）、quality of life（1943）、quality time（1977）。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"qualitative","ipa":"/ˈkwɒlɪtətɪv/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"relating to quality rather than quantity. It is the adjective built directly on quality.","definitionCN":"定性的；性质上的。它是直接由 quality 构成的形容词。"},{"word":"qualify","ipa":"/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪ/","tag":"same stem, verb","definition":"to make fit or to limit. It shares the qual- stem but adds -ify 'to make'.","definitionCN":"使有资格；限定。它共享 qual- 词干，但加了 -ify「使……」。"},{"word":"quantity","ipa":"/ˈkwɑːntəti/","tag":"the mirror twin","definition":"amount or number. It looks and sounds close but answers a different question.","definitionCN":"数量。它形音都相近，回答的却是另一个问题。"},{"word":"qualifier","ipa":"/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪə/","tag":"same qual- family","definition":"a word or person that limits or qualifies something.","definitionCN":"限定词；取得资格者。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"property","ipa":"/ˈprɒpəti/","tag":"what belongs to a thing","definition":"a characteristic or attribute that a thing possesses. It is close to quality in the 'attribute' sense.","definitionCN":"事物所具有的特性或属性。它与 quality 的「属性」义接近。"},{"word":"attribute","ipa":"/əˈtrɪbjuːt/","tag":"single feature","definition":"a quality or feature regarded as belonging to someone or something.","definitionCN":"被视为属于某人或某物的性质或特征。"},{"word":"characteristic","ipa":"/ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk/","tag":"identifying feature","definition":"a feature that identifies a person or thing and is typical of it.","definitionCN":"能标识并代表某人或某物的典型特征。"},{"word":"grade","ipa":"/ɡreɪd/","tag":"level of goodness","definition":"a level of rank or quality, especially in goods or results.","definitionCN":"等级；品级。尤用于货物或成绩。"},{"word":"excellence","ipa":"/ɪkˈseləns/","tag":"high quality as a standard","definition":"the state of being extremely good. It names quality at its top end.","definitionCN":"卓越；优秀。它指 quality 的最高一档。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin qualis 'of what kind', qualitas 'property', and the English family qualify, qualitative, quantity.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 qualis「何种」、qualitas「属性」，以及英语词族 qualify、qualitative、quantity。"},"normal":[{"en":"quality answers the question qualis, 'what kind?'; quantity answers quantus, 'how much?'","cn":"quality 回答 qualis「何种」；quantity 回答 quantus「多少」。"},{"en":"the quality once meant the nobility: people whose kind was supposed to be better.","cn":"the quality 一度指贵族：人们认为他们那一类人更好。"},{"en":"Quality control is a modern factory phrase, but the logic is old: check what kind came out.","cn":"quality control 是现代工厂用语，但逻辑很古老：检查出来的是哪一种成色。"},{"en":"Quality time is time judged by its kind, not its length.","cn":"quality time 是按「质地」而非长度衡量的时间。"},{"en":"A violin's quality is its timbre: the sound's kind, not its volume.","cn":"小提琴的 quality 是音色：声音的种类，而不是音量。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is kind before degree: you must know what sort a thing is before you can say how good it is.","cn":"核心是先有种类，后有程度：先知道它是哪一类，才谈得上多好。"},{"en":"Quality travels inward: from a category in philosophy to a person's temper to the feel of cloth.","cn":"quality 一路向内走：从哲学范畴，到人的性情，再到布的手感。"},{"en":"One noun holds both 'what it is' and 'how good it is'; English never fully separated them.","cn":"一个名词同时装着「它是什么」和「它有多好」，英语从未把它们彻底分开。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Customers are willing to pay more for quality.","cn":"顾客愿意为质量多付钱。"},{"en":"Honesty is the quality I value most in a friend.","cn":"诚实是我在朋友身上最看重的品质。"},{"en":"The recording captures the warm quality of her voice.","cn":"这段录音捕捉到了她嗓音里温暖的音色。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"qual（＝quality，质地）+ ity（名词）——先摸质地，再评好坏 → quality 质量、品质","word":"quality"},"root":"源自拉丁语 qualis「何种的」，西塞罗造 qualitas「性质、属性」以译希腊语 poiotēs，经古法语 calite/qualite 于约 1300 年进入英语；核心是「问种类、论质地」，再引申出好坏与身份。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses fan out from one question: what kind is it? Character, attribute, goodness, high grade, timbre, rank, philosophical category, logical polarity, and the tone of a newspaper are all ways of answering that question.","cn":"九个义项从一个提问展开：它属于何种？性情、属性、优良、高档、音色、身份、哲学范畴、逻辑的肯定否定、报纸的格调，都是回答这个问题的不同方式。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: fingering a thing to learn its kind before judging its worth.","cn":"核心意象：先用手捻一捻，知道它是什么质地，再判断它值多少。"},"chain":["QUALIS: WHAT KIND","QUALITAS: PROPERTY","CHARACTER OF A PERSON","GOODNESS OF A THING","RANK IN SOCIETY","A LABEL OF EXCELLENCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S04","en":"HOW GOOD: the standard of a thing, and the attributive label quality goods.","cn":"有多好：事物的水准，以及作定语的 quality goods（优质货）。"},{"senses":"S02 · S03","en":"WHAT IT IS: a person's temper, and a single property that belongs to it.","cn":"是什么：人的性情，以及附着其上的单项属性。"},{"senses":"S05 · S08","en":"THE CHARACTER OF A THING: the timbre of a sound, and the yes-or-no of a proposition.","cn":"事物的性格：声音的音色，以及命题的肯定或否定。"},{"senses":"S06 · S09","en":"A MARK OF STANDING: social rank, and the seriousness of the quality press.","cn":"身份的标记：社会等级，以及严肃报刊的格调。"},{"senses":"S07","en":"THE PHILOSOPHICAL CATEGORY: quality as what makes a thing of a certain sort.","cn":"哲学范畴：使一物成为某种样子的「性质」。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Quality is qual- plus -ity. Its family shows the question stem qual- 'what kind', the noun suffix -ity, the verb suffix -ify, and the adjective endings -ative, -ed and -ly.","cn":"quality 是 qual- 加 -ity。它的词族展示疑问词干 qual-「何种」、名词后缀 -ity、动词后缀 -ify，以及形容词词尾 -ative、-ed、-ly。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin qualis 'of what kind' yields qualitas 'quality'; with facere 'to make' it yields qualificare, the source of qualify. The abstract noun qualitas also produced qualitativus, hence qualitative.","cn":"拉丁语 qualis「何种」给出 qualitas「性质」；与 facere「做」结合给出 qualificare，即 qualify 的来源。抽象名词 qualitas 又生出 qualitativus，即 qualitative。"},"items":[{"word":"quality","structure":"qualis (of what kind) + -itas (noun)","meaning":"kind, property, or degree of goodness","meaningCN":"质量；品质；性质（-itas 名词后缀）","example":"The quality of the light changed at dusk.","exampleCN":"黄昏时光线的质感变了。"},{"word":"qualitative","structure":"qualitas + -ative (adjective)","meaning":"concerned with quality, not quantity","meaningCN":"定性的；性质上的","example":"The survey adds qualitative depth to the numbers.","exampleCN":"这项调查为数字增加了定性的深度。"},{"word":"qualify","structure":"qualis + -ificare (to make)","meaning":"to make fit; to limit","meaningCN":"使有资格；限定","example":"Two years of training qualify her for the job.","exampleCN":"两年训练使她胜任这份工作。"},{"word":"qualification","structure":"qualify + -ication (noun)","meaning":"a certificate, condition, or restriction","meaningCN":"资格；限定条件","example":"He left school without qualifications.","exampleCN":"他离校时没有任何学历资格。"},{"word":"qualified","structure":"qualify + -ed (adjective)","meaning":"having the required standard","meaningCN":"合格的；有资格的","example":"Only qualified staff may use the machine.","exampleCN":"只有合格员工才能使用这台机器。"},{"word":"qualifier","structure":"qualify + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"a person or word that qualifies","meaningCN":"取得资格者；限定词","example":"Quite is a qualifier in quite good.","exampleCN":"quite 在 quite good 中是限定词。"},{"word":"disqualify","structure":"dis- (not, away) + qualify","meaning":"to declare unfit or ineligible","meaningCN":"取消资格","example":"A failed drug test disqualified the athlete.","exampleCN":"药检未通过使这名运动员被取消资格。"},{"word":"unqualified","structure":"un- (not) + qualified","meaning":"not qualified; also complete, absolute","meaningCN":"不合格的；彻底的","example":"The plan won unqualified approval.","exampleCN":"这项计划获得了无条件批准。"},{"word":"qualitatively","structure":"qualitative + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in terms of quality","meaningCN":"定性地；在性质上","example":"The two experiences differ qualitatively.","exampleCN":"这两次体验在性质上不同。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"qualis","structure":"qualis (interrogative adjective)","meaning":"of what kind","meaningCN":"何种的"},{"word":"qualitas","structure":"qualis + -itas","meaning":"quality, property, nature","meaningCN":"性质；属性；本性"},{"word":"qualitativus","structure":"qualitas + -ivus","meaning":"relating to quality","meaningCN":"关于性质的"}]}},{"word":"quantity","ipa_uk":"/ˈkwɒntəti/","ipa_us":"/ˈkwɑːntəti/","definition_zh":"数量；量；大量；数额；总量；（物理）量；数学量；（诗律）音节长短；（逻辑）命题的量","definition_en":"how much of something there is, or a particular amount measured in units","core_image":"一把谷子倒进斗里，斗沿上的刻度一格一格往上爬——所有问题都归到一句：有多少","scene":"A lab assistant points at a beaker and says: Record the quantity of the solution, not just its colour.","sceneCN":"这里 quantity 是「数量、用量」（第 1 个义项：有多少）；句意：记录溶液的用量，而不只是颜色。画面里有量筒、刻度线和记录本。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"数量；量；大量；数额；总量"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a large quantity of","zh":"大量的……"},{"phrase":"in quantity","zh":"大量地；成批地"},{"phrase":"a small quantity of","zh":"少量的……"},{"phrase":"quantity discount","zh":"批量折扣"},{"phrase":"an unknown quantity","zh":"未知量；未知因素"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"quantities"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"quantify","pos":"v.","zh":"量化；用数量表示"},{"word":"quantitative","pos":"adj.","zh":"定量的；数量的"},{"word":"quantification","pos":"n.","zh":"量化；定量"},{"word":"quantifier","pos":"n.","zh":"量词；数量限定词"},{"word":"quantum","pos":"n.","zh":"量子；定量"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"How much: the answer to a count or a measure","titleCN":"数量：数出来或量出来的答案","definition":"the amount or number of something, especially when it can be measured","definitionCN":"某物的数量或数目，尤指可以测量的","example":"The quantity of water in the tank is lower than yesterday.","exampleCN":"水箱里的水量比昨天少了。","why":"The noun is recorded in early 14c. as 'amount, magnitude, the being so much in measure or extent', from Latin quantitas. It answers the Latin question quantus, 'how much?', and that question is still its core.","whyCN":"名词在 14 世纪初记录为「数量、大小，在度量或范围上达到多少」，来自拉丁语 quantitas。它回答拉丁语提问词 quantus「多少？」，这个提问至今仍是它的核心。"},{"no":"02","title":"In quantity: a lot of it at once","titleCN":"大量：一次就是一大批","definition":"a large amount or number, especially in the phrases in quantity and quantities of","definitionCN":"大量或大批，尤用于 in quantity 与 quantities of","example":"It is cheaper to buy rice in quantity.","exampleCN":"大批买米要便宜些。","why":"Once quantity means 'amount', the plural quantities can mean 'large amounts', and in quantity means 'in bulk'. English often turns a neutral measure word into a word for abundance simply by putting it in the plural or in a buying phrase.","whyCN":"一旦 quantity 表示「数量」，复数 quantities 就能表示「大量」，in quantity 就是「成批」。英语常把中性的度量词通过复数或购买短语变成「丰足」的意思。"},{"no":"03","title":"A sum: the total on the page","titleCN":"数额、总量：纸上那个合计","definition":"a particular amount of something, especially money or goods, considered as a total","definitionCN":"某物的特定数额，尤指钱或货物，被视为一个总量","example":"A large quantity of money was moved offshore.","exampleCN":"一大笔钱被转移到了海外。","why":"From late 14c. quantity also meant 'that which has quantity, a concrete quantity'. An amount you can point to and total is a thing in its own right, which is why the word can name a sum of money.","whyCN":"从 14 世纪后期起，quantity 也指「具有数量的东西、具体数量」。一个可以指认并合计的数额本身就成了一样东西，所以这个词能指一笔钱。"},{"no":"04","title":"A measured portion: this much, no more","titleCN":"份量：就这么多，不能再多","definition":"a portion of something measured out for a particular use","definitionCN":"为特定用途量出的一份东西","example":"Add a small quantity of salt to the boiling water.","exampleCN":"往沸水里加少量盐。","why":"Measuring out is the practical face of quantity: you take from the whole an amount you have fixed. The word moves easily from 'how much there is' to 'how much you are giving', because both are the same number seen from different sides.","whyCN":"量出是 quantity 的实用面孔：你从整体里取出一个定好的量。这个词很容易从「一共有多少」滑到「给你多少」，因为两者只是同一个数字的两面。"},{"no":"05","title":"A physical quantity: number plus unit","titleCN":"物理量：数字后面必须带单位","definition":"in physics, a property that can be measured and expressed as a number with a unit, such as mass or length","definitionCN":"物理学中可测量并用数值加单位表示的属性，如质量或长度","example":"Force is a physical quantity measured in newtons.","exampleCN":"力是一种物理量，以牛顿为单位。","why":"Latin quantitas already meant 'how much in measure or extent'. Physics modernised that: anything that can carry a unit and be compared on a scale is a quantity, so the word became a technical label for measurable properties.","whyCN":"拉丁语 quantitas 本已表示「在度量或范围上多少」。物理学把它现代化：凡能带单位、能在标尺上比较的，都是 quantity，于是这个词成了可测属性的技术标签。"},{"no":"06","title":"An unknown quantity: the x in the equation","titleCN":"未知量：方程里那个 x","definition":"in mathematics, a value or expression that can be added, multiplied, or solved for, often an unknown","definitionCN":"数学中可相加、相乘或求解的值或表达式，常指未知数","example":"Let x be the unknown quantity in the equation.","exampleCN":"设 x 为方程中的未知量。","why":"Algebra treats amounts as letters you can operate on before you know their value. Such a value is a quantity even while unknown, which is why 'an unknown quantity' later escaped mathematics into ordinary speech about uncertain people and plans.","whyCN":"代数把数量当作字母，在知道数值之前就能运算。这样的值即使未知也是一种 quantity，所以 an unknown quantity 后来从数学逃进日常语，指不确定的人或计划。"},{"no":"07","title":"Metrical quantity: how long a syllable lasts","titleCN":"诗律的音量：一个音节占多长时间","definition":"in prosody, the relative time taken to utter a vowel or syllable, making it long or short","definitionCN":"诗律学中念出一个元音或音节所需的相对时间，决定其长短","example":"Latin verse depends on the quantity of each syllable.","exampleCN":"拉丁诗歌取决于每个音节的长短。","why":"In quantitative verse, rhythm is built from time, not stress: a long syllable is literally a larger quantity of sound-time. The word is recorded in this metrical sense by the 1560s, when Latin verse was still the model for English poets.","whyCN":"在按长短写成的诗里，节奏由时间而非重音构成：长音节字面上就是更多的一份「声音时间」。这个诗律义在 16 世纪 60 年代已有记录，当时拉丁诗仍是英国诗人的范本。"},{"no":"08","title":"Logical quantity: all, or some","titleCN":"逻辑的量：全部，还是有些","definition":"in logic, the extent to which a proposition refers to its subject, whether universal (all) or particular (some)","definitionCN":"逻辑学中命题对其主词的指涉范围，分为全称（全部）与特称（有些）","example":"Changing the quantity turns an all-statement into a some-statement.","exampleCN":"改变命题的量，就把「全部」的陈述变成了「有些」的陈述。","why":"Logicians pair quantity with quality: quality says whether a proposition affirms or denies, quantity says how much of the class it covers. The English pair is a direct inheritance from the Latin vocabulary of the Aristotelian categories.","whyCN":"逻辑学家把 quantity 与 quality 配对：quality 说命题是肯定还是否定，quantity 说它覆盖了这个类别的多少。英语的这一对词直接继承自亚里士多德范畴的拉丁词汇。"},{"no":"09","title":"Quantity as a category: the 'how much' of things","titleCN":"量：哲学里与「质」相对的那一范畴","definition":"in philosophy, the category of how much or how many, opposed to quality, the category of what kind","definitionCN":"哲学中「多少、几何」的范畴，与表示「何种」的「质」相对","example":"The dialectic describes quantity turning into quality at a threshold.","exampleCN":"这一辩证法描述量在某个临界点上转化为质。","why":"Latin quantitas was coined as a loan-translation of Greek posotes, the category of 'how much', just as qualitas rendered 'of what sort'. Quantity and quality are therefore a matched pair made by translators, which is why the phrase 'quantity into quality' works in philosophy.","whyCN":"拉丁语 quantitas 是作为希腊语 posotes「多少」这一范畴的仿译词造出的，正如 qualitas 译「何种」。因此 quantity 与 quality 是译者造出的一对配套词，这也是「量转化为质」在哲学中说得通的原因。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Quantity comes from the Latin question quantus, 'how much?'. It was coined as a noun to render Greek posotes, the philosophical category of amount, and English has used it ever since for anything countable, weighable, unit-bearing, or merely uncertain.","cn":"quantity 来自拉丁疑问词 quantus「多少？」。它作为名词被造出来翻译希腊语 posotes，即「量」这一哲学范畴；英语此后用它指一切可数、可称、带单位，甚至只是「不确定」的东西。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1c BC)","en":"Quantus was the correlative adjective 'of what size? how much? how great? what amount?'. Its PIE root *kwo-, the stem of interrogative and relative pronouns, is a reconstruction with no written record, so that layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"Quantus 是关联形容词「多大？多少？多强？几何？」。它的印欧语词根 *kwo-（疑问与关系代词的词干）是重构形式，没有书面记录，因此那一层标为「来源不确定」。"},{"era":"LATIN (1c BC)","en":"Quantitas 'relative greatness or extent' was coined as a loan-translation of Greek posotes, from posos 'how great? how much?'. The coiner and the exact date of this coinage are not recorded, so that detail is marked source uncertain.","cn":"Quantitas「相对大小或范围」是作为希腊语 posotes 的仿译词造出的，posotes 来自 posos「多大？多少？」。造词者与确切年代没有记录，因此这一细节标为「来源不确定」。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.)","en":"Old French quantite, cantite meant 'amount, quantity' (Modern French quantité). The French form is why English first wrote the word as quantite.","cn":"古法语 quantite、cantite 意为「数量、量」（现代法语 quantité）。法语形式正是英语早期拼作 quantite 的原因。"},{"era":"EARLY 14c. ENGLISH","en":"The noun is first recorded as 'amount, magnitude, the being so much in measure or extent'. It still answers the original Latin question, and it can describe anything you can put on a scale.","cn":"名词最早记录为「数量、大小，在度量或范围上达到多少」。它仍在回答那个拉丁提问，也可描述一切能放上标尺的东西。"},{"era":"LATE 14c.–1610s ENGLISH","en":"Three branches appear: 'that which has quantity, a concrete quantity' (late 14c.), the prosodic sense 'relative time of a vowel or syllable' (by the 1560s), and 'an object regarded as more or less' (1610s). Amount becomes a thing, a beat, and a counted object.","cn":"三条分支出现：「具有数量的东西、具体数量」（14 世纪后期）；诗律义「元音或音节的相对时长」（16 世纪 60 年代前）；「被视为多或少的一个对象」（17 世纪 10 年代）。数量变成了一样东西、一个节拍、一个被计数的对象。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Science added the sharp technical uses: a physical quantity is a measurable property with a unit; an unknown quantity is a symbol in algebra; the quantity of a proposition is universal or particular. The old 'how much' simply learned new grammars.","cn":"科学又添了精确的技术义：物理量是带单位的可测属性；未知量是代数里的符号；命题的量分全称与特称。那个古老的「多少」只是学会了新的语法。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"quality","ipa":"/ˈkwɒləti/","tag":"the mirror twin","definition":"the character or standard of something. It differs by a few letters and by asking 'what kind' instead of 'how much'.","definitionCN":"性质；质量。它与 quantity 只差几个字母，问的却是「何种」而非「多少」。"},{"word":"quantitative","ipa":"/ˈkwɒntɪtətɪv/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"relating to amount or number. It is the adjective built on quantity.","definitionCN":"定量的；数量的。它是 quantity 的形容词。"},{"word":"quantify","ipa":"/ˈkwɒntɪfaɪ/","tag":"same stem, verb","definition":"to express something as a number or amount.","definitionCN":"量化；用数量表示。"},{"word":"quantum","ipa":"/ˈkwɒntəm/","tag":"Latin singular of quanta","definition":"a fixed minimum amount of energy; also Latin for 'how much'.","definitionCN":"量子；固定最小份额。它也是拉丁语「多少」的单数形式。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"amount","ipa":"/əˈmaʊnt/","tag":"plain total","definition":"how much there is of something, especially money or a substance.","definitionCN":"数量；总额。尤指钱或某物质的量。"},{"word":"number","ipa":"/ˈnʌmbə/","tag":"countable items","definition":"a count of separate things. It suits things you can count one by one, where quantity suits what you measure.","definitionCN":"数目；数量。它适合能一个个数的事物，而 quantity 适合被测量的东西。"},{"word":"volume","ipa":"/ˈvɒljuːm/","tag":"space or bulk","definition":"the amount of space something fills, or a large amount of something.","definitionCN":"体积；容量；大量。"},{"word":"sum","ipa":"/sʌm/","tag":"added total","definition":"the total reached by adding amounts together.","definitionCN":"总数；总和。"},{"word":"magnitude","ipa":"/ˈmæɡnɪtjuːd/","tag":"size on a scale","definition":"the great size or importance of something, often measured on a scale.","definitionCN":"巨大；量级。常指在某一标尺上的大小。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin quantus 'how much', quantitas, and the English family quantify, quantitative, quantum.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 quantus「多少」、quantitas，以及英语词族 quantify、quantitative、quantum。"},"normal":[{"en":"quantity answers quantus, 'how much?'; quality answers qualis, 'what kind?' — two Latin question words, two English nouns.","cn":"quantity 回答 quantus「多少」；quality 回答 qualis「何种」——两个拉丁疑问词，两个英语名词。"},{"en":"quantify is simply 'to give a quantity to' something that had none.","cn":"quantify 就是给原本没有数量的东西「安上一个数量」。"},{"en":"quantum is Latin for 'how much', which is why a quantum is a fixed lump of something.","cn":"quantum 是拉丁语「多少」，所以量子是某样东西的一个固定份额。"},{"en":"An unknown quantity is literally the x you have not solved yet, and then any person you cannot predict.","cn":"an unknown quantity 字面上是你还没解出的 x，后来指任何你摸不透的人。"},{"en":"Buying in quantity means buying a big how-much at once.","cn":"buying in quantity 就是一次买下一个很大的「多少」。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is one question, asked of everything: how much of it is there?","cn":"核心是一个问题，对一切事物发问：它有多少？"},{"en":"Quantity can be counted, weighed, timed, or merely unknown; the word does not care which.","cn":"数量可以被数、被称、被计时，也可以只是未知；这个词不在乎是哪一种。"},{"en":"Quality asks what it is; quantity asks how much it is — and philosophy made them a pair.","cn":"quality 问它是什么，quantity 问它有多少——哲学把它们做成了一对。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The recipe lists the quantity of each ingredient in grams.","cn":"食谱以克为单位列出了每种配料的用量。"},{"en":"Factories buy paper in large quantities to cut costs.","cn":"工厂大批购买纸张以降低成本。"},{"en":"In physics, time is a quantity that can be measured precisely.","cn":"在物理学中，时间是一种可以精确测量的量。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"quant（＝how much，多少）+ ity（名词）——只回答一个问题：有多少 → quantity 数量","word":"quantity"},"root":"源自拉丁语 quantus「多少、多大」，其名词 quantitas 为希腊语 posotes「量」的仿译，经古法语 quantite 于 14 世纪初进入英语；核心是「以度量回答多少」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses, one question with many grammars: how much? It begins as a measure of extent, grows into 'a large amount' and 'a sum', then becomes a physical quantity, an algebraic unknown, a syllable's length, a proposition's scope, and a philosophical category.","cn":"九个义项，一个提问，多套语法：多少？它从「范围的大小」开始，长出「大量」与「数额」，再成为物理量、代数未知量、音节的长短、命题的范围，最后成为哲学范畴。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: tipping grain into a measure and watching the marks rise.","cn":"核心意象：把谷子倒进量斗，看刻度一格格往上升。"},"chain":["QUANTUS: HOW MUCH","QUANTITAS: MEASURE","COUNT AND WEIGH","A LARGE AMOUNT","NUMBER WITH A UNIT","SCOPE IN LOGIC"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S03","en":"HOW MUCH: a measured amount, and a sum considered as a total.","cn":"多少：测得的数量，以及被视为总量的数额。"},{"senses":"S02 · S04","en":"ABUNDANCE AND PORTION: buying in bulk, and a measured share for use.","cn":"丰足与份量：成批购买，以及为使用量出的一份。"},{"senses":"S05 · S06","en":"TECHNICAL AMOUNTS: the physical quantity with units, and the unknown in algebra.","cn":"技术性的量：带单位的物理量，以及代数里的未知量。"},{"senses":"S07 · S08","en":"MEASURED SCOPE: a syllable's length in verse, and a proposition's all-or-some.","cn":"被量出的范围：诗句中音节的长短，以及命题的全称或特称。"},{"senses":"S09","en":"THE CATEGORY: quantity as the philosophical opposite of quality.","cn":"范畴：作为 quality 哲学对立面的「量」。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Quantity is quant- plus -ity. Its family shows the question stem quant- 'how much', the noun suffix -ity, the verb suffix -ify, and the adjective endings -ative, -able and -ly.","cn":"quantity 是 quant- 加 -ity。它的词族展示疑问词干 quant-「多少」、名词后缀 -ity、动词后缀 -ify，以及形容词词尾 -ative、-able、-ly。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin quantus 'how much' gives quantitas 'amount'. With facere 'to make' it yields quantificare, the source of quantify, and the neuter quantum survives as the name of a minimum lump of energy.","cn":"拉丁语 quantus「多少」给出 quantitas「数量」。与 facere「做」结合给出 quantificare，即 quantify 的来源；中性形式 quantum 则活下来，指一份最小的能量。"},"items":[{"word":"quantity","structure":"quantus (how much) + -itas (noun)","meaning":"amount; how much there is","meaningCN":"数量；量（-itas 名词后缀）","example":"The quantity of rain this year was unusual.","exampleCN":"今年的降雨量很不寻常。"},{"word":"quantify","structure":"quantus + -ificare (to make)","meaning":"to measure or express as an amount","meaningCN":"量化；以数量表示","example":"It is hard to quantify the damage.","exampleCN":"很难量化损失。"},{"word":"quantitative","structure":"quantitas + -ative (adjective)","meaning":"relating to amount or number","meaningCN":"定量的；数量的","example":"They collected quantitative data on rainfall.","exampleCN":"他们收集了关于降雨的定量数据。"},{"word":"quantification","structure":"quantify + -ication (noun)","meaning":"the act of measuring or expressing as amount","meaningCN":"量化；定量（-ication 名词后缀）","example":"The quantification of risk is an inexact science.","exampleCN":"风险的量化是一门不精确的学问。"},{"word":"quantifier","structure":"quantify + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"a word such as all or some that states quantity","meaningCN":"量词；数量限定词（如 all、some）","example":"Every is a quantifier in every student.","exampleCN":"every 在 every student 中是量词。"},{"word":"quantum","structure":"quantus (how much), neuter singular","meaning":"a fixed minimum amount, especially of energy","meaningCN":"量子；固定最小份额","example":"A photon is a quantum of light.","exampleCN":"光子是光的一个量子。"},{"word":"quantifiable","structure":"quantify + -able (adjective)","meaning":"able to be measured or counted","meaningCN":"可量化的（-able 形容词后缀）","example":"The benefits are real but not easily quantifiable.","exampleCN":"益处是真实的，但不容易量化。"},{"word":"quantitatively","structure":"quantitative + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in terms of amount or number","meaningCN":"定量地；从数量上","example":"The two groups differ quantitatively but not qualitatively.","exampleCN":"这两组在数量上不同，但在性质上并无差别。"},{"word":"quantitation","structure":"quantity + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of determining how much","meaningCN":"定量测定（-ation 动作名词后缀）","example":"Quantitation of the drug in blood takes two hours.","exampleCN":"血液中药物含量的定量测定需要两小时。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"quantus","structure":"quantus (correlative adjective)","meaning":"how much, how great, of what size","meaningCN":"多少；多大；几何"},{"word":"quantitas","structure":"quantus + -itas (noun)","meaning":"amount, relative greatness or extent","meaningCN":"数量；相对大小或范围"},{"word":"posotes","structure":"Greek posotes, from posos (how much)","meaning":"quantity, the category of amount","meaningCN":"量（希腊语，quantitas 所仿译者）"}]}},{"word":"quote","ipa_uk":"/kwəʊt/","ipa_us":"/kwoʊt/","definition_zh":"引用；引述；引文；引语；报价；估价；引号；上市挂牌；（旧）按编号标注","definition_en":"to repeat words that someone else has said or written, or to name the price you will charge for something","core_image":"书页边上用数字标出的一段话，被人一字不差地抄进另一篇文章，两侧再添上一对弯钩似的引号","scene":"A reporter flips her notebook shut and says: Don't quote me on this, but the dealer asked twice the market rate.","sceneCN":"这里 quote 是「引述某人说」（第 10 个义项：在新闻报道中转述某人的话）；句意：别把我的话写进报道，但那家店要价比市场价高一倍。画面里有笔记本、录音笔和一张写满数字的纸。","pos":[{"tag":"v.","zh":"引用；引述；援引；报价；上市挂牌"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"引文；引语；报价；引号"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"quote from","zh":"引自……；从……中引用"},{"phrase":"quote sb as saying","zh":"引述某人说"},{"phrase":"quote a price","zh":"报价；开价"},{"phrase":"be quoted at","zh":"报价为……；以……价格挂牌"},{"phrase":"quote unquote","zh":"（口语）所谓；带引号地（含讽刺）"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"quotes"},{"label":"过去式","form":"quoted"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"quoted"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"quoting"},{"label":"复数","form":"quotes"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"quotation","pos":"n.","zh":"引文；引语；报价单"},{"word":"quotable","pos":"adj.","zh":"值得引用的；可引用的"},{"word":"misquote","pos":"v.","zh":"误引；错误引用"},{"word":"unquote","pos":"v.","zh":"结束引文（口语中标出引号结束）"},{"word":"quota","pos":"n.","zh":"配额；定额（同出 quot“多少”）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Repeat the exact words","titleCN":"引用原话：把别人的字句一字不差地搬来","definition":"to repeat or copy out words that someone else has said or written","definitionCN":"重复或抄录别人说过或写下的原话","example":"She quoted a line from the report to open her speech.","exampleCN":"她引用报告里的一句话来开场。","why":"The word starts as a scribe's act: Medieval Latin quotare meant 'mark a book off into chapters and verses by numbers'. From pointing at a numbered passage grew 'to give as a reference', and by the 1670s 'to copy out exact words'.","whyCN":"这个词起于抄写员的动作：中世纪拉丁语 quotare 意为“用数字把书分成章与节”。从“指向某个编号段落”长出“作为依据列出”，到 17 世纪 70 年代成了“一字不差地抄出原话”。"},{"no":"02","title":"The borrowed line itself","titleCN":"引文、引语：被搬来的那一行字","definition":"a sentence or phrase taken from a book, speech, or other source and repeated by someone else","definitionCN":"从书、演讲或其他来源摘出并被他人重复的句子或短语","example":"The essay opens with a quote from Darwin.","exampleCN":"这篇文章以一句达尔文的引文开篇。","why":"English made the verb into a noun only in 1885, calling the borrowed passage 'a quotation' and later clipping it to quote. Before that, a quote (c. 1600) meant a marginal reference, the little pointing mark rather than the words.","whyCN":"英语直到 1885 年才把动词变成名词，称被搬来的段落为 quotation，后来缩成 quote。更早（约 1600 年）的 quote 指页边的参照标记，是那个“指向”的记号，而不是文字本身。"},{"no":"03","title":"Cite as an authority","titleCN":"援引：把某句话请出来作证人","definition":"to mention a person or text as support for an argument or as an authority","definitionCN":"提及某人或某文本，作为论点的依据或权威","example":"The lawyer quoted the 1954 ruling in her closing argument.","exampleCN":"律师在结案陈词中援引了 1954 年的那项裁决。","why":"This is the 1570s bridge between numbering and verbatim copying: a quoted passage is summoned into court as a witness. The passage is still a pointer, but now it carries authority.","whyCN":"这是 16 世纪 70 年代在“编号”与“照抄”之间的桥：被引用的段落像证人一样被传上法庭。它仍是一个指向，只是如今带上了权威。"},{"no":"04","title":"Name your price","titleCN":"报价：把价钱说成一个数","definition":"to tell a customer or client the price you will charge for goods or work","definitionCN":"告诉客户或委托人你将收取的货物或工作价格","example":"The builder quoted £4,000 for the whole roof.","exampleCN":"施工方为整个屋顶报价四千英镑。","why":"The 1866 business sense deliberately revives the oldest layer: quotare was to mark something with a number. A quotation is a number put on a job, exactly as a scribe numbered verses.","whyCN":"1866 年出现的商业义是有意复活最古老的一层：quotare 就是给某物标上一个数字。报价就是给一件活计标上数字，正像抄写员给诗篇编号。"},{"no":"05","title":"The estimate on paper","titleCN":"报价单：写在纸上的那个估价","definition":"a written statement of how much something will cost, or the sum stated","definitionCN":"写明某物要花多少钱的书面说明，或其中写明的金额","example":"We accepted the cheaper of the two quotes.","exampleCN":"我们接受了两个报价中较便宜的那个。","why":"Once the verb means 'state a price', the product of that act takes the same name. A quote is a frozen act of quoting, just as a quote in an essay is a frozen act of speaking.","whyCN":"一旦动词意为“说出价格”，这个动作的产物就取同一个名字。报价单是被冻结的“报价”动作，正如文章里的引文是被冻结的“说话”动作。"},{"no":"06","title":"The two little hooks","titleCN":"引号：把借来的话圈起来的那对钩","definition":"quotation marks, the pair of marks placed around words that are quoted","definitionCN":"放在被引用文字两端的引号","example":"Put the title in quotes, not in italics.","exampleCN":"把标题放进引号里，不要用斜体。","why":"Quotes as a short form of quotation marks is recorded from 1869. The mark does visibly what the verb does: it fences off words that belong to someone else.","whyCN":"quotes 作为 quotation marks 的缩写记录于 1869 年。这个符号把动词所做的事看得见地做了一遍：把属于别人的话圈起来。"},{"no":"07","title":"Quoted on the exchange","titleCN":"上市挂牌：把公司的名字报到市场上","definition":"to have a company's shares listed and priced on a stock exchange","definitionCN":"使公司股票在证券交易所挂牌并标价交易","example":"The firm was quoted on the London exchange last spring.","exampleCN":"这家公司去年春天在伦敦交易所挂牌上市。","why":"A listed share is literally a priced item on a public list, so the pricing sense extends to the exchange. The listing usage is not dated in the standard etymology, so its exact origin is marked source uncertain.","whyCN":"挂牌股票字面上就是公共清单上标了价的一项，因此“标价”义延伸到交易所。通行词源没有给出“上市挂牌”这一用法的年代，故其确切来源标为“来源不确定”。"},{"no":"08","title":"Number the margins","titleCN":"按编号标注：抄写员在页边写下数字","definition":"to mark a book with chapter numbers or marginal references, an obsolete sense","definitionCN":"用章节编号或页边参照标注书籍，现已废弃的义项","example":"Monks quoted the psalter so that readers could find each verse.","exampleCN":"修士们给诗篇标上编号，好让读者找到每一节。","why":"This is the word's birthplace in English, late 14c. coten, from Medieval Latin quotare 'distinguish by numbers'. Every later sense is a descendant of a number written beside a passage.","whyCN":"这是这个词在英语里的出生地：14 世纪后期的 coten，来自中世纪拉丁语 quotare“用数字区分”。后来所有义项，都是“写在段落旁的那个数字”的后代。"},{"no":"09","title":"Quote unquote: saying the marks aloud","titleCN":"口头引号：把引号念出来，还带点讽刺","definition":"a spoken formula marking the beginning and end of a quoted word, often used ironically","definitionCN":"口头标出所引词语起止的说法，常带讽刺意味","example":"He's a quote unquote expert who has never published anything.","exampleCN":"他是个所谓的专家，却从没发表过任何东西。","why":"In 1912 telegraph messages had to spell out punctuation, so quote and unquote replaced the marks. By 1920 the pair was spoken together, and the audible hooks became a way of raising an eyebrow.","whyCN":"1912 年电报必须把标点念出来，于是 quote 与 unquote 代替了引号。到 1920 年这两个词被连读，听得见的“引号”成了挑一挑眉毛的表达方式。"},{"no":"10","title":"Quoted as saying","titleCN":"引述某人说：新闻里的转述格式","definition":"to report someone's statement in a news story, usually with quote sb as saying","definitionCN":"在新闻报道中转述某人的话，通常用 quote sb as saying","example":"The minister was quoted as saying that no new taxes would be introduced.","exampleCN":"报道引述部长的话说，不会开征新税。","why":"Journalism turns the verb into a frame: the reporter does not repeat every word, but certifies that the words came from a named mouth. The quotation mark of print becomes a byline in a newspaper.","whyCN":"新闻业把这个动词变成一个框架：记者不必复述每个字，只需证明这些话出自某张有名字的嘴。印刷品里的引号，在报纸里变成了一个消息来源的署名。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Quote descends from a number in a margin. Latin quot 'how many' produced quotare 'mark by numbers', which became 'point to a passage', then 'cite it', then 'repeat it exactly', and finally 'put a price on it'.","cn":"quote 的祖先是页边的一个数字。拉丁语 quot“多少”生出 quotare“用数字标记”，再变成“指向某段”，继而“援引它”“一字不差地重复它”，最后“给它标上价钱”。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE (reconstructed)","en":"The pronominal root *kwo- 'who, how many' is reconstructed from forms in Latin and other branches. There is no written record of it, so this layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"代词性词根 *kwo-“谁、多少”是从拉丁语及其他语支的形式重构出来的。它没有书面记录，因此这一层标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"LATIN (before 1C BC)","en":"Quot meant 'how many', quotus 'which in order, of what number'. From them came quotare 'to distinguish by numbers, mark off into chapters'. Quota (pars) 'how large a part' belongs to the same family.","cn":"quot 意为“多少”，quotus 意为“第几、什么编号”。由它们生出 quotare“用数字区分、分成章节”。quota (pars)“多大的一份”属于同一家族。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN & OLD FRENCH (13c.–14c.)","en":"Medieval Latin quotare specialized to 'mark a book with chapter and verse numbers'. Old French coter carried the same scribal duty and supplied the English form.","cn":"中世纪拉丁语 quotare 专门指“用章节与诗篇编号标注书籍”。古法语 coter 承担同样的抄写职责，并提供了英语的形式。"},{"era":"LATE 14c. ENGLISH","en":"The verb appears as coten, 'to mark or annotate a book with chapter numbers or marginal references'. The qu- spelling is attested from the early 15c.; Middle English also used it for 'to compute, reckon'.","cn":"动词以 coten 形式出现，意为“用章节编号或页边参照标注书籍”。qu- 拼写自 15 世纪初有记录；中古英语还用它表示“计算、估算”。"},{"era":"1570s–1670s ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'to give as a reference, cite as an authority' is from the 1570s. 'To copy out or repeat exact words' follows in the 1670s, together with the printing sense 'enclose in quotation marks'.","cn":"“作为参照列出、援引作权威”的义项始于 16 世纪 70 年代。“抄出或重复原话”紧随其后，出现于 17 世纪 70 年代，同时还有印刷上的“加引号”。"},{"era":"1866–1885 ENGLISH","en":"The commercial sense 'to state the price of a commodity' (1866) revives the old notion of marking an item with a number. The noun 'a quotation' is from 1885, and quotes for quotation marks from 1869. The stock-exchange listing sense has no dated entry in the standard etymology and is marked source uncertain.","cn":"商业义“说明商品价格”（1866）复活了“给某物标一个数字”的旧观念。名词“引文”始于 1885 年，quotes 指引号始于 1869 年。证券“上市挂牌”义在通行词源中没有年代记录，标为“来源不确定”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares the letters quot-, whether or not it shares the root; the second group shares the act of passing words or prices between people.","cn":"第一组共享 quot- 这几个字母，未必共享词根；第二组共享“把人说的话或价钱在人与人之间传递”这一动作。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"quota","ipa":"/ˈkwəʊtə/","tag":"same root, different noun","definition":"a fixed share or amount assigned to each person. It is Latin quota pars, 'how large a part', from the same quot.","definitionCN":"配额；定额。它来自拉丁语 quota pars“多大的一份”，与 quote 同出 quot。"},{"word":"quoth","ipa":"/kwəʊθ/","tag":"archaic 'said'","definition":"an old past tense meaning 'said', always placed before its subject. It is not related to quote.","definitionCN":"古语“说”，总放在主语之前。它与 quote 并无词源关系。"},{"word":"quotient","ipa":"/ˈkwəʊʃnt/","tag":"same root, mathematics","definition":"the result of a division. Latin quotiens 'how many times' asks the same 'how many' question as quot.","definitionCN":"商；除法结果。拉丁语 quotiens“多少次”问的正是与 quot 相同的“多少”。"},{"word":"quotidian","ipa":"/kwəˈtɪdiən/","tag":"same root, daily","definition":"ordinary, happening every day. Latin quotidie 'daily' is built on quotus 'of what number', hence 'every numbered day'.","definitionCN":"日常的；每日发生的。拉丁语 quotidie“每日”建在 quotus“第几”之上，即“每一个被数到的日子”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"cite","ipa":"/saɪt/","tag":"name as authority","definition":"to mention a source in support of an argument. It is the formal act behind quoting.","definitionCN":"引用；援引（作为依据）。它是 quote 背后那个正式的动作。"},{"word":"excerpt","ipa":"/ˈeksɜːpt/","tag":"a cut-out passage","definition":"a short piece taken from a longer work. It is the passage itself, not the act of repeating it.","definitionCN":"摘录；节选。它指那段文字本身，而不是重复它的动作。"},{"word":"paraphrase","ipa":"/ˈpærəfreɪz/","tag":"same idea, new words","definition":"to express someone's meaning in different words. It is the opposite of quoting exactly.","definitionCN":"释义；改述。它正是“一字不差地引用”的反面。"},{"word":"bid","ipa":"/bɪd/","tag":"price offered","definition":"a price offered for goods or at an auction. It competes with quote in the market sense.","definitionCN":"出价；投标价。在市场义上与 quote 竞争。"},{"word":"quotation","ipa":"/kwəʊˈteɪʃn/","tag":"the full noun","definition":"the uncut noun for both a quoted passage and a written price. Quote is its shortened form.","definitionCN":"引文；报价单。它是引文与书面报价的完整名词形式，quote 是其缩略。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"The links are all in the quot- family: quota, quotient and quotidian ask 'how many', while quotation and quotation marks carry the borrowed words.","cn":"这些联想都在 quot- 家族里：quota、quotient、quotidian 都在问“多少”，而 quotation 与 quotation marks 则承载着借来的话。"},"normal":[{"en":"quote and quota both come from quot 'how many': one numbers a passage, the other numbers a share.","cn":"quote 与 quota 都来自 quot“多少”：一个给段落编号，一个给份额编号。"},{"en":"A quote is a numbered margin note that escaped the book and became speech.","cn":"引文就是一条逃出书本的页边编号注，后来变成了人说的话。"},{"en":"Quotation marks are little hooks: they hook someone else's words and hold them apart.","cn":"引号是一对小钩子：钩住别人的话，把它单独拎出来。"},{"en":"The builder's quote is a price tag written on a job, the same act as numbering a verse.","cn":"施工方的报价就是贴在活计上的价签，与给诗篇编号是同一个动作。"},{"en":"Quote unquote spells the punctuation out loud, so you can hear the scare quotes.","cn":"quote unquote 把标点念出声，让你听见那对“可疑的引号”。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"One gesture under all ten senses: point at something, then take it into your own mouth.","cn":"十个义项下只有一个手势：先指向某物，再把它拿进自己嘴里。"},{"en":"Number, word, price: a quote is always a value attached to something by an outside hand.","cn":"编号、字句、价钱：quote 永远是由外部之手贴在某物上的一个值。"},{"en":"The quotation mark and the price tag are the same invention: a label saying 'this is not mine'.","cn":"引号与价签是同一项发明：一个标签，写着“这不属于我”。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"He quoted three lines from the poem without naming the author.","cn":"他引用了诗中的三行，却没提作者的名字。"},{"en":"The garage quoted us £600 to replace the brakes.","cn":"修车行给我们换刹车的报价是六百英镑。"},{"en":"Her shares are quoted on three different exchanges.","cn":"她的股票在三个不同的交易所挂牌。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"quo（= quota 份额、编号）+ te —— 给这段话编上号，照着号码一字不改搬过来 → quote 引用；报价","word":"quote"},"root":"源自拉丁语 quot“多少”、quotus“第几”，派生 quotare“用数字标记、分章编号”，经中世纪拉丁语与古法语 coter 进入英语；核心是“在段落旁写下一个数字，再照它把话搬走”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Ten senses, one motion: a number in the margin turns into a borrowed voice, and the same 'marking with a value' becomes a price tag, a pair of quotation marks, and a listing on an exchange.","cn":"十个义项，一个动作：页边的数字变成借来的声音；同一个“标上一个值”的动作，又变成价签、一对引号，以及交易所里的挂牌。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a passage marked with a number is lifted, intact, into another mouth.","cn":"核心意象：一段被数字标出的文字，被原封不动地搬进另一张嘴。"},"chain":["MARK BY NUMBER","POINT TO A PASSAGE","CITE AS AUTHORITY","REPEAT EXACT WORDS","FENCE IT WITH MARKS","PUT A PRICE ON IT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S08 · S03","en":"FROM NUMBER TO WITNESS: the scribe's margin note becomes a citation in an argument.","cn":"从编号到证人：抄写员的页边注，变成论证中的一条援引。"},{"senses":"S01 · S02","en":"THE BORROWED VOICE: repeating exact words, and the passage that results.","cn":"借来的声音：一字不差地重复，以及由此得到的引文。"},{"senses":"S06 · S09","en":"THE VISIBLE HOOK: printed quotation marks, and the same marks spoken aloud.","cn":"看得见的钩：印刷的引号，以及把同一对引号念出声。"},{"senses":"S04 · S05","en":"THE NUMBER ON THE JOB: quoting a price, and the written estimate it produces.","cn":"贴在活计上的数字：报价，以及由此产生的书面估价。"},{"senses":"S07 · S10","en":"THE PUBLIC RECORD: shares listed and priced, and speech attributed in a news story.","cn":"公开的记录：股票的挂牌标价，以及新闻报道中被归到某人名下的言论。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Quote is a bare Latin stem with no prefix: quot- 'how many' plus the verb ending -are. Its family shows the noun suffixes -ation, -able, -ient, and the negative prefixes mis- and un-.","cn":"quote 是一个不带前缀的拉丁词干：quot-“多少”加动词词尾 -are。它的词族展示名词后缀 -ation、-able、-ient，以及否定前缀 mis-、un-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin quot 'how many' yields quotus 'of what number', quotare 'to number', quota pars 'how large a part', and quotiens 'how many times'.","cn":"拉丁语 quot“多少”生出 quotus“第几”、quotare“编号”、quota pars“多大一份”，以及 quotiens“多少次”。"},"items":[{"word":"quote","structure":"quot- (how many) + -are (verb)","meaning":"to number, then to cite and repeat words","meaningCN":"编号；引用；引述","example":"Please quote the exact sentence from the contract.","exampleCN":"请引用合同里的原句。"},{"word":"quotation","structure":"quote + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of quoting; a quoted passage or price","meaningCN":"引用；引文；报价单","example":"The quotation at the top of the page is from Confucius.","exampleCN":"页面顶端的那句引文出自孔子。"},{"word":"quotable","structure":"quote + -able (capable of)","meaning":"short and sharp enough to be quoted","meaningCN":"值得引用的；可引用的","example":"He gave a quotable line about patience.","exampleCN":"他说了一句关于耐心的、很适合引用的话。"},{"word":"misquote","structure":"mis- (wrongly) + quote","meaning":"to quote someone inaccurately","meaningCN":"误引；错误引用","example":"The paper misquoted her, and she demanded a correction.","exampleCN":"报纸误引了她的话，她要求更正。"},{"word":"unquote","structure":"un- (reverse) + quote","meaning":"to mark the end of a quotation","meaningCN":"结束引文（标出引号结束）","example":"He said, quote, we are close to a deal, unquote.","exampleCN":"他说，引号，我们接近达成协议了，引号结束。"},{"word":"quota","structure":"quot- (how many) + -a (Latin feminine)","meaning":"a fixed share assigned to each","meaningCN":"配额；定额","example":"Each country has a strict import quota.","exampleCN":"每个国家都有严格的进口配额。"},{"word":"quotient","structure":"quotiens (how many times) + -ent (noun)","meaning":"the number of times one quantity contains another","meaningCN":"商；商数","example":"Divide 20 by 4 and the quotient is 5.","exampleCN":"20 除以 4，商是 5。"},{"word":"quotidian","structure":"quotidie (daily) + -an (adjective)","meaning":"belonging to every day; ordinary","meaningCN":"每日的；日常的；平凡的","example":"The diary records the quotidian details of farm life.","exampleCN":"这本日记记录了农场上日常的琐碎细节。"},{"word":"quotation mark","structure":"quotation + mark (compound noun)","meaning":"either of a pair of marks placed around quoted words","meaningCN":"引号","example":"Single quotation marks are used inside a quotation.","exampleCN":"引文之中的引文用单引号。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"quot","structure":"quot (interrogative pronoun)","meaning":"how many","meaningCN":"多少"},{"word":"quotare","structure":"quotus + -are (verb)","meaning":"to number, mark off into chapters","meaningCN":"编号；分章标注"},{"word":"quota (pars)","structure":"quota, feminine of quotus + pars","meaning":"how large a part; a fixed share","meaningCN":"多大的一份；定额"}]}},{"word":"radical","ipa_uk":"/ˈrædɪkl/","ipa_us":"/ˈrædɪkl/","definition_zh":"根本的；彻底的；激进的；激进分子；根；词根；根号；自由基；（俚）极酷的","definition_en":"relating to the root of something, and therefore either fundamental or extreme; also a root, a root sign, or a root in a word","core_image":"一株植物被连根拔起，泥土里那团盘绕的根须露出来，整株植物的生死都系在它身上","scene":"A chemistry teacher taps the board and says: A radical is a molecule with an unpaired electron, so it reacts very fast.","sceneCN":"这里 radical 是「自由基」（第 8 个义项：带未成对电子、极易反应的原子或原子团）；句意：自由基是带未成对电子的分子，反应极快。画面里有分子结构图和一支粉笔。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"根本的；彻底的；激进的；极端的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"激进分子；根；词根；根号；自由基"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"radical change","zh":"根本性的变革；彻底的改变"},{"phrase":"radical reform","zh":"激进改革；彻底改革"},{"phrase":"radical idea","zh":"激进的想法；离经叛道的想法"},{"phrase":"radical difference","zh":"根本的差异"},{"phrase":"free radical","zh":"自由基"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more radical"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most radical"},{"label":"复数","form":"radicals"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"radically","pos":"adv.","zh":"根本上；彻底地；激进地"},{"word":"radicalism","pos":"n.","zh":"激进主义"},{"word":"radicalize","pos":"v.","zh":"使激进化"},{"word":"radicalization","pos":"n.","zh":"激进化"},{"word":"radish","pos":"n.","zh":"萝卜（拉丁 radix“根”的另一支）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Of the root: fundamental","titleCN":"根本的：长在根上的那部分","definition":"relating to the basic nature of something, not to its surface","definitionCN":"涉及某物基本性质的，而非表面的","example":"The report calls for radical changes in how the city treats its water.","exampleCN":"这份报告呼吁从根本上改变这座城市对待水的方式。","why":"Latin radicalis meant 'of or having roots', from radix 'root'. The figurative sense 'going to the origin, essential' appears in the 1650s: what is at the root is by definition what everything else stands on.","whyCN":"拉丁语 radicalis 意为“有根的”，来自 radix“根”。比喻义“直达本源、本质”出现于 17 世纪 50 年代：凡是长在根上的东西，按定义就是其余一切所立足的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"Down to the root: thoroughgoing","titleCN":"彻底的：一直挖到根，不留旧土","definition":"thorough and complete, affecting the whole of something rather than a part","definitionCN":"彻底而完全的，影响整体而非局部","example":"The system needs radical surgery, not another patch.","exampleCN":"这套制度需要彻底的手术，而不是再打一个补丁。","why":"If a change reaches the root, no part of the plant is left untouched. English speakers turned this spatial image into a degree word: radical means changing something all the way down, not merely trimming it.","whyCN":"如果一次改变触及根部，植物就没有哪一部分还能保持原样。英语使用者把这一空间意象变成一个程度词：radical 指把某物一直改到底层，不只是修剪枝叶。"},{"no":"03","title":"Pulling up the roots: politically extreme","titleCN":"激进的：要把旧制度连根拔起","definition":"wanting deep and rapid change in politics or society","definitionCN":"主张在政治或社会上作深刻而迅速变革的","example":"The party's radical wing wants to abolish the old tax system entirely.","exampleCN":"该党的激进派想彻底废除旧税制。","why":"The political label dates from 1817 for the extreme section of the British Liberal party. 'Radical reform' had been a slogan since 1786, and the metaphor was literal: change from the roots up.","whyCN":"这一政治标签始于 1817 年，指英国自由党的极端一派。自 1786 年起“radical reform”就是口号，其隐喻是字面的：从根往上改。"},{"no":"04","title":"A rooter: the person, not the idea","titleCN":"激进分子：愿意连根拔的人","definition":"a person who holds extreme political views and works for thorough change","definitionCN":"持极端政治观点并为彻底变革奔走的人","example":"In 1802 the newspapers began calling him a radical.","exampleCN":"1802 年，报纸开始称他为激进分子。","why":"The noun appears in 1802 for 'one who pursues a theory to its furthest limit'. It is a person described by the direction of their pull: toward the root, away from compromise.","whyCN":"名词出现于 1802 年，指“把一种理论推到极致的人”。它描述的是一种拉力方向：朝根部去，离开妥协。"},{"no":"05","title":"Basal: growing straight from the root","titleCN":"基生的：直接从根部长出来的","definition":"of leaves or buds, growing from or close to the root of a plant rather than on the stem","definitionCN":"（叶或芽）从植物根部或贴近根部处长出，而不是长在茎上","example":"Dandelions form a radical rosette of leaves close to the ground.","exampleCN":"蒲公英贴地长出一圈基生叶莲座。","why":"Latin radicalis meant 'of or having roots'. Botanists keep the adjective literal: a leaf springing from the root rather than the stem is called radical.","whyCN":"拉丁语 radicalis 意为“属于根、有根的”。植物学家把形容词用在本义上：从根部而非茎上长出的叶，就称为 radical（基生的）。"},{"no":"06","title":"Root of a word","titleCN":"词根：单词扎在语言土里的那一截","definition":"the basic part of a word to which prefixes and suffixes are added","definitionCN":"单词中可加前缀、后缀的基本部分","example":"The radical of 'international' is 'nat', from Latin for birth.","exampleCN":"international 的词根是 nat，来自拉丁语“出生”。","why":"The noun entered English in the 1630s in philology, meaning 'primitive verbal element serving as the root of inflected or derivative words'. Grammarians borrowed the botanist's image: words grow from a stem.","whyCN":"这个名词于 17 世纪 30 年代以语文学术语进入英语，意为“作为屈折词或派生词之根的原始语文要素”。语法学家借用了植物学家的意象：词从一根茎上长出来。"},{"no":"07","title":"The root sign","titleCN":"根号：把“根”画成一个符号","definition":"the mathematical sign placed before a quantity to show that its root is to be taken","definitionCN":"数学中放在某量之前、表示要开方的符号","example":"Write the answer under the radical, not beside it.","exampleCN":"把答案写在根号下面，不要写在旁边。","why":"The radical sign dates from the 1680s, and the mark itself is a modified letter r, the first letter of radix. The symbol still carries the word's root in its shape.","whyCN":"根号始于 17 世纪 80 年代，这个符号本身是字母 r 的变形，也就是 radix 的首字母。符号的形状里仍藏着这个词的“根”。"},{"no":"08","title":"A chemical root: the free radical","titleCN":"自由基：化学里四处抓电子的那截基团","definition":"an atom or group of atoms with an unpaired electron, which reacts very readily","definitionCN":"带未成对电子、极易发生反应的原子或原子团","example":"Free radicals in the body can damage cells.","exampleCN":"体内的自由基会损伤细胞。","why":"Chemists adopted radical in 1816 for a group of atoms that acts as a unit, the 'root' of a compound. Later it named the unpaired-electron fragment that is chemically hungry, still a root detached from its molecule.","whyCN":"化学家于 1816 年借 radical 指作为一个整体起作用的一组成员原子，即化合物的“根”。后来它指那种带未成对电子、化学上很“饿”的碎片，仍是从分子上脱落的根。"},{"no":"09","title":"Rad: cool, in surfer slang","titleCN":"rad：冲浪少年口中的“极酷”","definition":"excellent, exciting, or impressive, in old surfing and youth slang","definitionCN":"极好的、刺激的、了不起的，用于旧时的冲浪与青年俚语","example":"That wave was totally rad, dude.","exampleCN":"那道浪太酷了，哥们儿。","why":"Surfer slang of the 1970s used radical for 'at the limits of control', and clipped it to rad. By 1983 U.S. youth slang had flipped the political word into praise: extreme became excellent.","whyCN":"20 世纪 70 年代的冲浪俚语用 radical 表示“到了失控的边缘”，并缩成 rad。到 1983 年，美国青年俚语把这个政治词翻成了赞美：极端变成了极好。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Radical is the Latin word for 'root' turned into an adjective, then into a political weapon. Every sense, from algebra to chemistry to slang, keeps the image of something at the base of a plant or of an argument.","cn":"radical 是拉丁语“根”一词变成的形容词，后来又变成政治武器。从代数到化学再到俚语，每个义项都保留着“位于植物或论证底部”的意象。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE (reconstructed)","en":"The root *wrād- 'branch, root' is a reconstruction, though de Vaan, after hesitation, finds it justified. There is no written record, so this layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"词根 *wrād-“枝、根”是重构形式；德·瓦恩在犹豫之后认为它成立。它没有书面记录，因此这一层标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"LATIN (before 1C BC)","en":"Radix (genitive radicis) meant 'root', both of a plant and figuratively of a thing's origin. Radicalis meant 'of or having roots'. The related ramus 'branch' grows from the same image.","cn":"radix（属格 radicis）意为“根”，既指植物的根，也比喻事物的起源。radicalis 意为“有根的”。同源的 ramus“枝”出自同一意象。"},{"era":"LATE 14c. ENGLISH","en":"The adjective appears meaning 'originating in the root or ground', and for body parts or fluids 'vital to life'. The bare physical sense of a plant root came along with it.","cn":"形容词出现，意为“源于根部或土地的”，并用于“维持生命所必需”的身体部位或体液。植物根的实指义也随之而来。"},{"era":"1630s–1680s ENGLISH","en":"The noun is recorded in the 1630s in philology as 'root part of a word'. The figurative adjective 'going to the origin, essential' is from the 1650s, and the radical sign in mathematics from the 1680s.","cn":"名词于 17 世纪 30 年代以语文学术语“单词的词根部分”被记录。比喻形容词“直达本源、本质”始于 17 世纪 50 年代，数学根号始于 17 世纪 80 年代。"},{"era":"1802–1817 ENGLISH","en":"The political noun 'extremist' appears in 1802; the adjective 'reformist' in 1817, for the extreme section of the British Liberal party. 'Radical reform' had been current since 1786.","cn":"政治名词“极端分子”出现于 1802 年；形容词“改革派的”出现于 1817 年，指英国自由党的极端一派。“radical reform”自 1786 年起通行。"},{"era":"1816–1983 ENGLISH","en":"The chemical sense is from 1816. 'Unconventional' is from 1921, and the praising slang rad from 1983, built on 1970s surfer use meaning 'at the limits of control'.","cn":"化学义始于 1816 年。“不落俗套的”始于 1921 年；表示赞美的俚语 rad 始于 1983 年，建立在 20 世纪 70 年代冲浪俚语“到了失控边缘”的用法上。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares the Latin root radix and its letters; the second group shares the idea of going to the bottom or to the limit.","cn":"第一组共享拉丁词根 radix 及其字母；第二组共享“到底部或到极限”的观念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"radicle","ipa":"/ˈrædɪkl/","tag":"same root, tiny root","definition":"the part of a plant embryo that becomes the root. It is almost homophone of radical and shares radix.","definitionCN":"胚根；植物胚胎发育成根的部分。它与 radical 几乎同音，并共享 radix。"},{"word":"eradicate","ipa":"/ɪˈrædɪkeɪt/","tag":"e- out + radix","definition":"to destroy something completely, literally to pull it out by the roots.","definitionCN":"根除；消灭。字面就是“连根拔出”。"},{"word":"radish","ipa":"/ˈrædɪʃ/","tag":"same root, a root vegetable","definition":"a small red or white root vegetable. Latin radix became radish through French.","definitionCN":"小萝卜；红色或白色的根茎蔬菜。拉丁语 radix 经法语变成 radish。"},{"word":"radix","ipa":"/ˈreɪdɪks/","tag":"the Latin source","definition":"the base of a number system, or a root in mathematics. English borrowed the Latin word itself in the 17c.","definitionCN":"基数；记数制的底；数学中的根。英语在 17 世纪直接借用了这个拉丁词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"fundamental","ipa":"/ˌfʌndəˈmentl/","tag":"at the base","definition":"forming the base or necessary part of something. It matches radical in the 'essential' sense without the politics.","definitionCN":"根本的；基础的。它对应 radical 的“本质”义，但不带政治色彩。"},{"word":"extreme","ipa":"/ɪkˈstriːm/","tag":"at the far end","definition":"very great, or far from the centre. It describes the position radical politics reaches.","definitionCN":"极端的；极度的。它描述激进政治所抵达的位置。"},{"word":"revolutionary","ipa":"/ˌrevəˈluːʃənəri/","tag":"turning over a system","definition":"causing or wanting a complete change of government or system. It goes further than radical reform.","definitionCN":"革命的；鼓吹革命的。它比 radical reform 走得更远。"},{"word":"root","ipa":"/ruːt/","tag":"the literal base","definition":"the underground part of a plant, or the origin of a thing. It is the plain noun behind radical.","definitionCN":"根；根源。它就是 radical 背后那个朴素的名词。"},{"word":"thorough","ipa":"/ˈθʌrə/","tag":"to the end","definition":"complete, with no part neglected. It matches the 'thoroughgoing' sense of radical.","definitionCN":"彻底的；周全的。它对应 radical 的“彻底”义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"The family is botanical: radix, radish and eradicate all picture a root being pulled out of the ground.","cn":"这个词族是植物学的：radix、radish、eradicate 都画着一条根被从土里拔出来。"},"normal":[{"en":"radical and radish are cousins: both come from Latin radix, 'root'; a radish is literally 'the root thing'.","cn":"radical 与 radish 是表亲：都来自拉丁语 radix“根”；radish 字面就是“根的东西”。"},{"en":"eradicate is e- 'out' plus radix: to eradicate is to pull a weed out by its root.","cn":"eradicate 是 e-“出”加 radix：根除就是把杂草连根拔出。"},{"en":"The radical sign √ is the letter r for radix stretched into a roof.","cn":"根号 √ 就是代表 radix 的字母 r 拉长成一个屋顶。"},{"en":"A radical politician wants change from the root; a radical change goes to the root.","cn":"激进的政治家要“从根上”改变；一次 radical 的变革则“改到了根上”。"},{"en":"Free radicals are roots torn off a molecule, still hungry for an electron.","cn":"自由基就是从分子上被扯下来的根，仍然饿着一个电子。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Ten senses, one direction: down. Radical always means toward the bottom of a thing.","cn":"十个义项，一个方向：向下。radical 永远指朝向某物的底部。"},{"en":"The same root is a botanical fact, a political threat, a maths sign and a chemical danger.","cn":"同一个“根”，可以是植物学事实、政治威胁、数学符号，也可以是化学危险。"},{"en":"To be radical is to refuse the surface: the word will not look at leaves while the root is untouched.","cn":"激进就是拒绝表面：根还没动，这个词就不肯去看叶子。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The discovery forced a radical rethink of how the disease spreads.","cn":"这一发现迫使人们从根本上重新思考这种疾病的传播方式。"},{"en":"Only a radical would accept such a break with tradition.","cn":"只有激进分子才会接受这样与传统的决裂。"},{"en":"Antioxidants help neutralise free radicals in the body.","cn":"抗氧化剂有助于中和体内的自由基。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"radi（radio 无线电）+ cal —— 无线电波一路钻到最深的根子里 → radical 根本的；激进的（要改到根上）","word":"radical"},"root":"源自拉丁语 radix（属格 radicis）“根”及其形容词 radicalis“有根的”；核心是“位于最底部、供养整株植物的那一段”，由此引申为“根本、彻底、从根上改”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses, all pointing down to the same root: the plant's root, the word's root, the root sign, the chemical root, and the person who wants to pull the old system up by its roots.","cn":"九个义项都指向同一个根：植物的根、词的根、根号、化学的基团，以及那个想把旧制度连根拔起的人。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: the root under the soil, which holds the whole plant and can pull it down.","cn":"核心意象：土下那条根，它托着整株植物，也能把整株植物掀翻。"},"chain":["ROOT","OF THE ROOT","AT THE ROOT","CHANGE FROM THE ROOT","ROOT OF A WORD OR NUMBER","A ROOT TORN FREE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S05 · S01","en":"BASAL GROWTH: leaves springing straight from the root, and anything essential that grows out of it.","cn":"从根部长出：直接从根部生出的叶，以及由根生发的本质之物。"},{"senses":"S02 · S03","en":"DOWN TO THE ROOT: thoroughgoing change, and the politics that demands it.","cn":"一直改到根：彻底的改变，以及要求这种改变的政治。"},{"senses":"S04","en":"THE ROOTER: the person who pulls rather than prunes.","cn":"拔根的人：只肯拔、不肯修剪的那个人。"},{"senses":"S06 · S07","en":"THE WRITTEN ROOT: a word's root, and the r-shaped sign for a number's root.","cn":"写下来的根：单词的词根，以及表示数字之根的 r 形符号。"},{"senses":"S08 · S09","en":"THE DETACHED ROOT: the hungry free radical, and the slang that praises the extreme.","cn":"脱落的根：饥渴的自由基，以及赞美极端的俚语。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Radical is radic- 'root' plus -al, an adjective ending. Its family shows the prefixes e-/ex- and the suffixes -ly, -ism, -ize, -ation, and the same stem in radish and radicle.","cn":"radical 是 radic-“根”加形容词后缀 -al。它的词族展示前缀 e-/ex-，后缀 -ly、-ism、-ize、-ation，以及 radish、radicle 中相同的词干。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin radix (radic-) 'root' gives radicalis 'of roots', radicula 'small root', and the verb eradicare 'to root out'.","cn":"拉丁语 radix（radic-）“根”给出 radicalis“根的”、radicula“小根”，以及动词 eradicare“连根拔出”。"},"items":[{"word":"radical","structure":"radic- (root) + -al (adjective)","meaning":"of the root; fundamental or extreme","meaningCN":"根的；根本的；激进的","example":"They demanded radical reform of the court system.","exampleCN":"他们要求对法院制度进行彻底改革。"},{"word":"radically","structure":"radical + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a fundamental or extreme way","meaningCN":"根本上；彻底地；激进地","example":"The environment has changed radically since 1990.","exampleCN":"自 1990 年以来，环境已发生根本性变化。"},{"word":"radicalism","structure":"radical + -ism (doctrine)","meaning":"the belief in thorough political change","meaningCN":"激进主义","example":"His early radicalism softened with age.","exampleCN":"他早年的激进主义随着年龄增长而缓和了。"},{"word":"radicalize","structure":"radical + -ize (make)","meaning":"to make a person or group more extreme","meaningCN":"使激进化","example":"Poverty can radicalize young men.","exampleCN":"贫困会使年轻人变得激进。"},{"word":"radicalization","structure":"radicalize + -ation (process noun)","meaning":"the process of becoming extreme","meaningCN":"激进化（过程）","example":"The study traces the radicalization of the group.","exampleCN":"这项研究追踪了该团体的激进化过程。"},{"word":"eradicate","structure":"e- (out) + radic- (root) + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to pull out by the root, hence to destroy completely","meaningCN":"根除；消灭","example":"The campaign aims to eradicate the disease by 2030.","exampleCN":"这项运动的目标是到 2030 年根除这种疾病。"},{"word":"eradication","structure":"eradicate + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the complete removal of something rooted","meaningCN":"根除；铲除","example":"The eradication of smallpox took two centuries.","exampleCN":"天花的根除用了两个世纪。"},{"word":"radish","structure":"radix (root) + -ish (Old French noun ending)","meaning":"a root vegetable","meaningCN":"萝卜（一种根菜）","example":"She sliced a radish into the salad.","exampleCN":"她切了一个萝卜放进沙拉。"},{"word":"radicle","structure":"radic- (root) + -ule (diminutive)","meaning":"the tiny embryonic root of a seed","meaningCN":"胚根","example":"The radicle emerges first when the seed sprouts.","exampleCN":"种子发芽时，胚根最先伸出。"},{"word":"radix","structure":"radix (Latin noun, root)","meaning":"the base of a number system; a root","meaningCN":"基数；根","example":"In base ten, the radix is ten.","exampleCN":"在十进制中，基数是十。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"radix","structure":"radix, radicis (noun)","meaning":"root; origin, foundation","meaningCN":"根；起源；基础"},{"word":"radicalis","structure":"radic- + -alis (adjective)","meaning":"of or having roots","meaningCN":"根的；有根的"},{"word":"eradicare","structure":"e- (out) + radic- + -are","meaning":"to root out, remove entirely","meaningCN":"连根拔出；彻底清除"}]}},{"word":"random","ipa_uk":"/ˈrændəm/","ipa_us":"/ˈrændəm/","definition_zh":"随机的；随意的；无目的的；无规律的；偶然的；随机存取；随机数；胡乱地","definition_en":"happening or chosen without a plan, purpose, or pattern, so that no one can predict which one comes next","core_image":"一匹脱缰的马不辨方向地狂奔，马蹄落处扬起的尘土没有一条直线，谁也不知道它下一步踩向哪里","scene":"A programmer rolls a die across the desk and says: We pick the sample at random, so no single case can skew the result.","sceneCN":"这里 random 先出现在 at random「随机地、胡乱地」（第 2 个义项：16 世纪短语“以极大的速度”引申为“不择方向”），再作「随机抽样的」（第 4 个义项）；句意：我们随机抽取样本，这样任何单个案例都无法让结果偏斜。画面里有骰子、屏幕上的数据表和一支笔。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"随机的；随意的；无规律的；偶然的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（计算机）随机；随意挑选的东西"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"at random","zh":"随机地；胡乱地；任意地"},{"phrase":"random sample","zh":"随机样本；随机抽样"},{"phrase":"random access","zh":"随机存取"},{"phrase":"random number","zh":"随机数"},{"phrase":"a random selection","zh":"随机选取；随便挑出的组合"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more random"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most random"},{"label":"名词（不可数）","form":"random"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"randomly","pos":"adv.","zh":"随机地；任意地"},{"word":"randomness","pos":"n.","zh":"随机性；无序"},{"word":"randomize","pos":"v.","zh":"使随机化；随机排列"},{"word":"randomization","pos":"n.","zh":"随机化"},{"word":"randomizer","pos":"n.","zh":"随机生成器；随机分配器"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"No aim, no target","titleCN":"无目的的：箭射出去，不瞄准任何靶子","definition":"made or done without a definite aim, purpose, or plan","definitionCN":"没有明确目标、目的或计划而做出或进行的","example":"He made a random guess and happened to be right.","exampleCN":"他随便猜了一下，碰巧猜对了。","why":"The adjective is first recorded in the 1650s as 'having no definite aim or purpose, haphazard, not sent in a special direction'. It borrows the image of a rider who has stopped steering.","whyCN":"这个形容词最早记录于 17 世纪 50 年代，意为“没有确定目标或目的、偶然、未被送往特定方向”。它借用了骑手放开缰绳的意象。"},{"no":"02","title":"At random: at full gallop","titleCN":"胡乱地：原意是“以极大的速度”","definition":"in a way that has no plan or order, as in the phrase at random","definitionCN":"毫无计划或秩序地，如短语 at random","example":"Books were piled at random on the floor.","exampleCN":"书胡乱地堆在地板上。","why":"The phrase at random is from the 1560s and first meant 'at great speed', from the old noun randon 'impetuosity, speed'. A horse running full tilt goes wherever momentum takes it, and speed turned into carelessness.","whyCN":"短语 at random 始于 16 世纪 60 年代，原意是“以极大的速度”，来自古名词 randon“冲势、猛劲”。一匹全速奔跑的马跑到哪里全凭惯性，速度就变成了漫不经心。"},{"no":"03","title":"Random access: jump anywhere","titleCN":"随机存取：不必从头读到尾","definition":"a way of reading computer memory in which any location can be reached directly, without passing through the ones before it","definitionCN":"一种读取计算机存储器的方式，可直接到达任一位置，无需先经过前面的位置","example":"RAM stands for random access memory.","exampleCN":"RAM 即随机存取存储器。","why":"Random access is recorded from 1953 for memory that need not be read sequentially. Here random does not mean 'by chance' but 'without a fixed order': the head may jump to any address at will.","whyCN":"random access 记录于 1953 年，指无需顺序读取的存储器。这里 random 不是“碰运气”，而是“没有固定次序”：磁头可以随意跳到任一地址。"},{"no":"04","title":"Random sample: every case has a chance","titleCN":"随机抽样：每个个体都有同等机会被抽中","definition":"a group chosen so that every member of a population has an equal chance of being selected","definitionCN":"这样选出的一组样本：总体中每个成员被选中的机会相等","example":"Researchers took a random sample of 500 households.","exampleCN":"研究者随机抽取了 500 户家庭作为样本。","why":"Statistics needs a procedure in which no case is favoured. The word's old sense of 'not directed toward a particular target' becomes a technical guarantee: nobody's hand steers the selection.","whyCN":"统计学需要一种不偏袒任何个体的程序。这个词“不被送往特定目标”的旧义变成一项技术保证：没有哪只手在引导选择。"},{"no":"05","title":"No pattern at all","titleCN":"无规律的：看不出可复现的花样","definition":"lacking any recognizable pattern, order, or regular arrangement","definitionCN":"缺乏可辨认的图案、次序或规则排列的","example":"The cracks formed a random pattern across the wall.","exampleCN":"裂缝在墙上形成毫无规律的图案。","why":"Once 'no aim' is applied to shapes rather than actions, random means 'no pattern'. The mind looks for a rule and finds none, which is exactly what the word reports.","whyCN":"一旦“无目的”从动作转用到形状，random 就表示“无规律”。头脑去找规则却找不到，这正是这个词所报告的状态。"},{"no":"06","title":"By chance encounter","titleCN":"偶然的：两条路线碰巧交叉","definition":"happening by chance rather than by arrangement","definitionCN":"出于偶然而非事先安排而发生的","example":"A random meeting in the airport changed her career.","exampleCN":"机场里的一次偶然相遇改变了她的职业道路。","why":"The 1650s sense already contained 'haphazard'. Two independent courses crossing without a plan is the everyday picture of chance, so random slides from 'unaimed' to 'unplanned'. ","whyCN":"17 世纪 50 年代的义项已含“偶然”。两条互不相干的路线在没有计划的情况下交叉，正是偶然的日常画面，于是 random 从“无瞄准”滑向“无安排”。"},{"no":"07","title":"That random person","titleCN":"不相干的：不知从哪儿冒出来的那个人","definition":"not known or not connected to the people involved; arbitrary or irrelevant, in informal use","definitionCN":"不认识或与当事人无关的；任意、不相干的（非正式用法）","example":"Some random guy kept texting her all night.","exampleCN":"一个不知从哪儿冒出来的家伙整晚给她发消息。","why":"Colloquial English extended 'no connection' to people: a random stranger is one with no link to your life. The 1980s college slang sense 'person who does not belong on our floor' pushed the word toward 'outsider'.","whyCN":"口语英语把“没有关联”扩展到人：a random stranger 就是与你生活毫无联系的人。20 世纪 80 年代的大学俚语义“不属于我们这层楼的人”，把这个词推向“局外人”。"},{"no":"08","title":"Random numbers, random choices","titleCN":"随机数与随机化：把偶然做成工具","definition":"a number or selection produced by a process that has no predictable order, used in computing and research","definitionCN":"由无可预测次序的过程产生的数字或选择，用于计算与研究","example":"The app generates a random number between one and ten.","exampleCN":"这个应用生成一到十之间的随机数。","why":"To use chance, people built machines and algorithms that imitate it: random number, randomize, randomizer. The adjective becomes a noun modifier for the output of an artificial process.","whyCN":"为了利用偶然，人们造出模仿偶然的机器与算法：random number、randomize、randomizer。这个形容词变成名词修饰语，指一个人工过程的产物。"},{"no":"09","title":"Random: the odd one out","titleCN":"俚语里的“怪人”：不属于这里的那一个","definition":"in 1980s U.S. college slang, an inferior or undesirable person, especially one who does not belong","definitionCN":"20 世纪 80 年代美国大学俚语中指次等或不受欢迎的人，尤指不属于此处的人","example":"Don't bring a random to the party.","exampleCN":"别把不相干的怪人带到派对上。","why":"By the 1980s U.S. campus slang had turned the adjective into a noun of contempt for someone outside the group. The 'no connection' sense hardened into social exclusion.","whyCN":"到 20 世纪 80 年代，美国校园俚语把这个形容词变成指称群体之外者的轻蔑名词。“没有关联”的义项硬化成了社会排斥。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Random begins as a word for speed: a horse at full gallop has no aim. 'At great speed' became 'carelessly', then 'without plan', and finally the technical 'without fixed order' of computing.","cn":"random 起初是一个表示速度的词：全速奔驰的马没有目标。“极快”变成“漫不经心”，再变成“没有计划”，最后成为计算机术语里“没有固定次序”。"},"items":[{"era":"GERMANIC (reconstructed)","en":"Frankish *rant 'a running' and Proto-Germanic *randa are reconstructed from the Old French and Germanic verbs for running. No written form survives, so this layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"法兰克语 *rant“奔跑”与原始日耳曼语 *randa 是从古法语及日耳曼语各语言的“跑”动词重构出来的。没有书面形式留存，因此这一层标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.–13c.)","en":"Randon meant 'rush, disorder, force, impetuosity', and randir 'to run fast'. The word pictures a charge rather than a stroll.","cn":"randon 意为“冲势、混乱、力量、猛劲”，randir 意为“快跑”。这个词画的是冲锋，而不是散步。"},{"era":"MIDDLE ENGLISH (c. 1300)","en":"The noun randon, randoun is recorded meaning 'impetuosity, speed'. The -n to -m spelling shift parallels seldom and ransom.","cn":"名词 randon、randoun 记录于约 1300 年，意为“冲势、速度”。-n 变 -m 的拼写变化与 seldom、ransom 平行。"},{"era":"1560s ENGLISH","en":"The phrase at random appears, first meaning 'at great speed', hence 'carelessly, haphazardly'. Speed and lack of aim are fused in one idiom.","cn":"短语 at random 出现，最初意为“以极大的速度”，因此引申为“漫不经心、胡乱地”。速度与无目标在一个习语里熔合了。"},{"era":"1650s ENGLISH","en":"The adjective random is recorded, 'having no definite aim or purpose, haphazard, not sent in a special direction'. The modern statistical sense grows out of this.","cn":"形容词 random 被记录，意为“没有确定目标或目的、偶然、未被送往特定方向”。现代统计学义即由此生长出来。"},{"era":"1953–1980s ENGLISH","en":"Random access is recorded in 1953 for computer memory that need not be read sequentially. By the 1980s college slang had added 'inferior, undesirable, out of place'.","cn":"random access 记录于 1953 年，指无需顺序读取的计算机存储器。到 20 世纪 80 年代，大学俚语又添上“次等的、不受欢迎的、格格不入的”一义。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares the ran-/rand- sound and, in two cases, the actual etymology; the second group shares the idea of choosing without a rule.","cn":"第一组共享 ran-/rand- 的读音，其中两个词还真有词源关系；第二组共享“不按规则地选择”这一观念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"ransom","ipa":"/ˈrænsəm/","tag":"same -n to -m shift","definition":"money paid to free a captive. It is unrelated in meaning but shares the odd -m spelling change with random.","definitionCN":"赎金。意义无关，但与 random 共享那个奇特的 -n 变 -m 拼写变化。"},{"word":"randon","ipa":"/ˈrændən/","tag":"the lost source noun","definition":"the Middle English noun for 'rush, impetuosity' from which at random was shortened.","definitionCN":"中古英语名词，意为“冲势、猛劲”，at random 即由它缩来。"},{"word":"rand","ipa":"/rænd/","tag":"edge of the old root","definition":"a unit of currency, or a random value in computing. It looks like a clipped random but is a separate word.","definitionCN":"货币单位，或计算中的随机值。它看起来像 random 的缩写，其实是另一个词。"},{"word":"randomly","ipa":"/ˈrændəmli/","tag":"look-alike derivative","definition":"in a random manner. The adverb looks like the adjective with a tail.","definitionCN":"随机地。这个副词看起来就像形容词多了一条尾巴。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"arbitrary","ipa":"/ˈɑːbɪtrəri/","tag":"chosen by will, not rule","definition":"decided by personal choice or impulse rather than reason. It stresses the chooser's freedom, while random stresses the absence of pattern.","definitionCN":"任意的；专断的。它强调选择者的自由，而 random 强调图案的缺失。"},{"word":"haphazard","ipa":"/ˌhæpˈhæzəd/","tag":"by mere chance","definition":"with no plan or order, happening as it may. It is close to random but more judgemental.","definitionCN":"偶然的；杂乱的。它接近 random，但更带贬义。"},{"word":"chance","ipa":"/tʃɑːns/","tag":"unplanned event","definition":"an event that happens without design. It names the cause, while random names the lack of pattern.","definitionCN":"偶然；机会。它命名原因，而 random 命名缺乏规律。"},{"word":"casual","ipa":"/ˈkæʒuəl/","tag":"without deliberation","definition":"done without care or intention. It suits a casual remark, not a random sample.","definitionCN":"随便的；漫不经心的。它适合一句随口的话，不适合随机样本。"},{"word":"indiscriminate","ipa":"/ˌɪndɪsˈkrɪmɪnət/","tag":"no selection at all","definition":"done without choosing carefully, affecting everyone or everything alike.","definitionCN":"不加区别的；滥施的。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"The real links are speed and horses: Old French randon 'rush', the phrase at random, and ransom's matching -m spelling.","cn":"真实的联想是速度与马：古法语 randon“冲势”、短语 at random，以及 ransom 那同样的 -m 拼写。"},"normal":[{"en":"random and randon: the old noun meant 'rush, impetuosity', so at random first meant 'at full speed'.","cn":"random 与 randon：这个古名词意为“冲势、猛劲”，所以 at random 最初意为“全速地”。"},{"en":"Think of a horse with no rider: it runs fast and goes nowhere in particular.","cn":"想象一匹没有骑手的马：跑得飞快，却哪里也不去。"},{"en":"random access memory does not read in order; it jumps, like a shopper who knows every aisle.","cn":"随机存取存储器不按顺序读；它直接跳，像一个熟悉每条货架的购物者。"},{"en":"Random and ransom share the -m: both changed from -n, and neither tells you why.","cn":"random 与 ransom 共享那个 -m：两者都由 -n 变来，谁也说不出原因。"},{"en":"A random sample is chance made fair: everyone gets the same lottery ticket.","cn":"随机样本是把偶然变得公平：每个人都拿到同样的彩票。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is released control: no hand on the reins, no target in sight.","cn":"核心是放开的控制：缰绳上没有手，视野里没有靶。"},{"en":"Speed, chance, pattern, order: random denies a different thing in each field.","cn":"速度、偶然、图案、次序：random 在每个领域否认的东西都不一样。"},{"en":"A statistical word built from a galloping horse is the best proof that metaphor becomes method.","cn":"一个由奔马构成的统计词，正是“隐喻变成方法”的最好证据。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The names were chosen at random from a hat.","cn":"名字是从帽子里随机抽出来的。"},{"en":"A random error in the data can ruin the whole model.","cn":"数据中的一个随机误差就能毁掉整个模型。"},{"en":"She met a random stranger who turned out to be her new boss.","cn":"她偶然遇到一个陌生人，结果竟是她的新上司。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"ran（跑）+ dom（= dumb 哑的）—— 一匹又跑又哑的马，没有方向地乱冲 → random 随机的；胡乱的","word":"random"},"root":"源自古法语 randon“冲势、猛劲”、randir“快跑”，上溯法兰克语 *rant 与原始日耳曼语 *randa“奔跑”，与 run 同族；核心是“一匹全速奔跑却不辨方向的马”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses follow one horse: it gallops without a target, so nothing is aimed, nothing repeats, nothing is in order — and in computing the same word means 'without a fixed sequence'.","cn":"九个义项跟着同一匹马：它没有目标地狂奔，于是没有瞄准、没有重复、没有次序；在计算机里，同一个词就表示“没有固定顺序”。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a horse galloping with no rider and no destination.","cn":"核心意象：一匹没有骑手、也没有目的地的奔马。"},"chain":["RUN FAST","AT GREAT SPEED","WITH NO AIM","BY CHANCE","WITH NO PATTERN","WITH NO FIXED ORDER"],"branches":[{"senses":"S02 · S06","en":"THE GALLOP: the old phrase 'at speed' and the chance encounter it became.","cn":"奔驰：古老的“全速”短语，以及由此变成的偶然相遇。"},{"senses":"S01 · S05","en":"NO TARGET, NO PATTERN: unaimed action and irregular shape.","cn":"无靶、无纹：没有瞄准的动作，与没有规律的形状。"},{"senses":"S03 · S08","en":"NO FIXED ORDER: memory that jumps, and numbers made by an imitation of chance.","cn":"无固定次序：会跳的存储器，以及模仿偶然造出的数字。"},{"senses":"S04","en":"FAIR CHANCE: the sample in which every case has the same ticket.","cn":"公平的偶然：每个个体都拿到同样一张票的样本。"},{"senses":"S07 · S09","en":"THE OUTSIDER: the stranger with no link, and the slang name for someone who does not belong.","cn":"局外人：毫无联系的陌生人，以及指称“不属于这里的人”的俚语。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Random has no living prefix or suffix in English; it is a whole French noun that became an adjective. Its family shows -ly, -ness, -ize, -ization and the compound random-access.","cn":"random 在英语里没有活的前缀或后缀；它是一个整体借来的法语名词，后来变成形容词。它的词族展示 -ly、-ness、-ize、-ization 以及复合词 random-access。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"There is no Latin ancestor: the line runs from Frankish *rant through Old French randon and randir to English. Latin is absent from this word's family tree.","cn":"它没有拉丁祖先：这条线从法兰克语 *rant 经古法语 randon、randir 到英语。这个词的家谱里没有拉丁语。"},"items":[{"word":"random","structure":"Old French randon (rush) + English adjective use","meaning":"without aim or pattern","meaningCN":"随机的；无目的的","example":"The survey used a random sample of readers.","exampleCN":"这项调查使用了随机读者样本。"},{"word":"randomly","structure":"random + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a random way","meaningCN":"随机地；任意地","example":"The files were randomly assigned to each group.","exampleCN":"文件被随机分配给每一组。"},{"word":"randomness","structure":"random + -ness (quality noun)","meaning":"the quality of having no pattern","meaningCN":"随机性；无序性","example":"True randomness is hard to produce by machine.","exampleCN":"真正的随机性很难由机器产生。"},{"word":"randomize","structure":"random + -ize (make)","meaning":"to arrange in a random order","meaningCN":"使随机化；随机排列","example":"The software randomizes the order of the questions.","exampleCN":"这个软件会随机打乱题目的顺序。"},{"word":"randomization","structure":"randomize + -ation (process noun)","meaning":"the act of making something random","meaningCN":"随机化","example":"Randomization reduces bias in clinical trials.","exampleCN":"随机化可减少临床试验中的偏倚。"},{"word":"randomizer","structure":"randomize + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"a device or program that produces random choices","meaningCN":"随机生成器","example":"The teacher used an online randomizer to call on students.","exampleCN":"老师用在线随机器点名。"},{"word":"random access","structure":"random (without fixed order) + access","meaning":"direct reading of any memory location","meaningCN":"随机存取","example":"Solid-state drives offer fast random access.","exampleCN":"固态硬盘提供快速的随机存取。"},{"word":"random number","structure":"random + number (compound noun)","meaning":"a number with no predictable order","meaningCN":"随机数","example":"The password generator starts with a random number.","exampleCN":"密码生成器以一个随机数开始。"},{"word":"at random","structure":"at + random (fixed phrase)","meaning":"without a plan or order","meaningCN":"随机地；胡乱地","example":"She opened the book at random and began to read.","exampleCN":"她随手翻开书，开始读起来。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"range","ipa_uk":"/reɪndʒ/","ipa_us":"/reɪndʒ/","definition_zh":"范围；幅度；系列；射程；靶场；山脉；炉灶；牧场；排列；漫游；（在一定范围内）变动","definition_en":"the spread of things between two limits, a line of mountains, or the distance something can reach; as a verb, to vary between limits or to roam over an area","core_image":"旷野上一排木桩从眼前一直排到山脚，桩线之间圈出一大片地，人可以在圈内走、猎、放牧，也可以量出箭能飞多远","scene":"A hiking guide points at the ridge and says: This range runs forty miles north, with trails from easy to severe.","sceneCN":"这里 range 是「山脉」（第 5 个义项：连成一线的一列山峰或丘陵）；句意：这条山脉向北延伸四十英里，步道难度从容易到险峻不等。画面里有山脊、路标和一条被踩出的土路。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"范围；幅度；系列；射程；靶场；山脉；炉灶；牧场"},{"tag":"v.","zh":"排列；漫游；（在一定范围内）变动"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a wide range of","zh":"范围广泛的；各种各样的"},{"phrase":"range from … to …","zh":"从……到……不等"},{"phrase":"within range","zh":"在射程内；在可及范围内"},{"phrase":"mountain range","zh":"山脉"},{"phrase":"shooting range","zh":"射击场；靶场"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"ranges"},{"label":"三单","form":"ranges"},{"label":"过去式","form":"ranged"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"ranged"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"ranging"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"ranger","pos":"n.","zh":"护林员；巡逻骑警；漫游者"},{"word":"rangy","pos":"adj.","zh":"身材瘦长的；适于漫游的"},{"word":"arrange","pos":"v.","zh":"安排；排列（a- 向 + range 排成行）"},{"word":"arrangement","pos":"n.","zh":"安排；排列；布置"},{"word":"range-finder","pos":"n.","zh":"测距仪"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The spread between limits","titleCN":"范围：从这头到那头之间的整片","definition":"the limits within which something varies, or the whole set of values between them","definitionCN":"某物变化的界限，或界限之间的全部取值","example":"The price range is between £20 and £60.","exampleCN":"价格范围在二十到六十英镑之间。","why":"The 'scope, extent' sense is recorded from the late 15c. It grows straight out of a row: a row of posts marks off the ground between its first and last post, and that span becomes the range.","whyCN":"“范围、幅度”义记录于 15 世纪后期。它直接从“一排”长出：一排木桩标出第一根到最后一根之间的地，这段跨度就成了 range。"},{"no":"02","title":"A row of choices","titleCN":"系列：一排摆开的同类东西","definition":"a set of similar things of different kinds, especially goods for sale","definitionCN":"不同种类的同类事物，尤指待售商品","example":"The shop stocks a wide range of teas.","exampleCN":"这家店备有各种各样的茶。","why":"A row is a line of items side by side. When the items are products rather than posts, the row becomes a 'line of goods', and English shops speak of their range.","whyCN":"一排就是一列并排的东西。当这些条目是商品而不是木桩时，这一排就成了“一系列货品”，英国商家便说自家有 a range。"},{"no":"03","title":"How far a shot reaches","titleCN":"射程：箭或子弹能飞到的距离","definition":"the distance over which a gun, bow, or instrument can send or receive something","definitionCN":"枪、弓或仪器能送出或接收某物的距离","example":"The missile has a range of 1,500 kilometres.","exampleCN":"这枚导弹射程一千五百公里。","why":"This sense is recorded from the 1590s. A row of targets measured out from the shooter gives a length; that measured length becomes the range. Later it covers an instrument's reach as well.","whyCN":"这一义项记录于 16 世纪 90 年代。从射手处量出的一排靶标给出一个长度；这个被量出的长度就是射程。后来也扩展到仪器的量程。"},{"no":"04","title":"The ground laid out for shooting","titleCN":"靶场：划出界线供人练枪的那片地","definition":"a place with targets where people practise shooting","definitionCN":"设有靶子、供人练习射击的场地","example":"Police officers qualify at the shooting range twice a year.","exampleCN":"警官每年在射击场参加两次资格考核。","why":"The 'place used for shooting practice' sense is from 1862. The measured distance became a measured ground: a range is both the length of the shot and the field where that length is tested.","whyCN":"“练枪场地”义始于 1862 年。被量出的距离变成了一块被量出的地：range 既是射击的长度，也是检验这个长度的那片场。"},{"no":"05","title":"A row of mountains","titleCN":"山脉：一座接一座排到天边","definition":"a line of connected mountains or hills","definitionCN":"连成一线的一列山峰或丘陵","example":"A snow-capped range rises behind the village.","exampleCN":"村庄背后耸起一道雪顶山脉。","why":"The sense 'row of mountains' is recorded from 1705. Mountains that stand in a line are literally a row, the oldest meaning of the word applied to the largest possible objects.","whyCN":"“山脉”义记录于 1705 年。连成一线的山字面上就是一排，词的最古老含义被用到了最大的物体上。"},{"no":"06","title":"The kitchen range","titleCN":"炉灶：一排灶眼连成的那个铁家伙","definition":"a large stove with several burners or ovens, used for cooking","definitionCN":"带多个灶眼或烤箱的大型炉具","example":"She left the stew simmering on the back of the range.","exampleCN":"她把炖菜留在炉灶后侧小火慢煨。","why":"The cooking appliance has been called a range since the mid-15c., for reasons that the standard etymology calls unknown; it was originally a stove built into a fireplace with openings on top. The exact motivation is marked source uncertain.","whyCN":"这种烹饪炉具自 15 世纪中叶起被称作 range，通行词源称其原因不明；它原先是砌在壁炉里、顶部带多个开口的炉子。确切动因标为“来源不确定”。"},{"no":"07","title":"The ground animals roam","titleCN":"牧场：牲畜走食的那一片","definition":"a large open area of land where animals graze or roam","definitionCN":"牲畜吃草或漫游的大片开阔地","example":"Cattle grazed on the open range all summer.","exampleCN":"整个夏天，牛群在开阔牧场上吃草。","why":"The sense 'area over which animals seek food' is from the 1620s and comes from the verb, not the noun. The land is defined by the ranging: wherever the herd wanders becomes its range.","whyCN":"“动物觅食的区域”义始于 17 世纪 20 年代，来自动词而非名词。这片地由“走动”来定义：牛群游到哪里，哪里就成了它们的牧场。"},{"no":"08","title":"Set in a row","titleCN":"排列：把东西一根一根摆成行","definition":"to place things in a row or in a particular order","definitionCN":"把东西排成一行或按某种次序摆放","example":"The books were ranged along the top shelf by height.","exampleCN":"书按高度排列在最上层书架上。","why":"The verb 'arrange in rows' is recorded from c. 1300. This is the family's trunk sense; the noun range and the verb arrange both come from the same Old French row.","whyCN":"动词“排成行”记录于约 1300 年。这是整个家族的树干义；名词 range 与动词 arrange 都来自同一个古法语的“排”。"},{"no":"09","title":"Roam over open country","titleCN":"漫游：没有固定路线地走遍一片地","definition":"to move freely over a large area, often while searching or hunting","definitionCN":"在大片区域内自由移动，常为搜寻或狩猎","example":"Wolves ranged across the valley at night.","exampleCN":"夜里狼群在山谷中四处游走。","why":"The verb is recorded c. 1200 as 'to move over or through a large area, roam with the purpose of searching or hunting'. A line of hunters spreading over ground is a row in motion.","whyCN":"动词记录于约 1200 年，意为“在大片区域内移动，为搜寻或狩猎而漫游”。散开在地面上的猎手队列，就是一排正在移动的“行”。"},{"no":"10","title":"Vary between two points","titleCN":"变动：在两端之间来回取值","definition":"to vary between two limits, as in range from one figure to another","definitionCN":"在两个界限之间变化，如 range from…to…","example":"Tickets range from free to fifty dollars.","exampleCN":"票价从免费到五十美元不等。","why":"When a set is thought of as a row of values, the verb can say that the values occupy that row. Range from … to … is the noun's span turned into motion between its two ends.","whyCN":"当一组数被想成一排取值时，动词就能说这些值占据了这一排。range from…to… 就是名词的跨度变成在两端之间的移动。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Range starts as a row of soldiers or hunters. The row becomes a measured line, the line becomes a span of values, and the same word ends up as mountains, a stove, a pasture and a verb of roaming.","cn":"range 起于一排士兵或猎手。这一排变成一条被量出的线，线变成一段取值，同一个词最后又成了山脉、炉灶、牧场，以及表示漫游的动词。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE (reconstructed)","en":"The root *sker- 'to turn, bend' is the reconstructed source of Proto-Germanic *hringaz 'circle, ring'. No written record exists, so this layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"词根 *sker-“转、弯”是原始日耳曼语 *hringaz“圆圈、环”的重构来源。没有书面记录，因此这一层标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"FRANKISH & OLD FRENCH (before 12c.)","en":"Frankish *hring 'ring, something curved' gave Old French reng, renge 'a row, line, rank'. A ring of people or posts seen from the side is a line, and the word shifted to the row itself.","cn":"法兰克语 *hring“环、弯曲之物”给出古法语 reng、renge“一排、一线、一列”。一圈人或木桩从侧面看就是一条线，词义便移到了这一排本身。"},{"era":"c. 1200 ENGLISH","en":"The noun renge is recorded as 'row or line of persons', especially hunters or soldiers; the verb rengen as 'to move over or through a large area, roam in search of game'. Row and roam arrive together.","cn":"名词 renge 记录为“一排或一列人”，尤指猎手或士兵；动词 rengen 记录为“在大片区域移动、为寻猎而漫游”。排列与漫游同时到来。"},{"era":"c. 1300–late 15c. ENGLISH","en":"'Arrange in rows' is recorded from c. 1300, the general 'line, row' from the early 14c., and 'scope, extent' from the late 15c. The cooking appliance also appears in the mid-15c., for unknown reasons.","cn":"“排成行”记录于约 1300 年，泛指的“线、排”记录于 14 世纪初，“范围、幅度”记录于 15 世纪后期。烹饪炉具也出现于 15 世纪中叶，原因不明。"},{"era":"1590s–1785 ENGLISH","en":"'Distance a gun can send a bullet' is from the 1590s; 'area over which animals seek food' from the 1620s; 'row of mountains' from 1705; the U.S. township sense from 1785.","cn":"“枪能把子弹送出的距离”始于 16 世纪 90 年代；“动物觅食区域”始于 17 世纪 20 年代；“山脉”始于 1705 年；美国六英里宽乡镇的义项始于 1785 年。"},{"era":"1862–1872 ENGLISH","en":"'Place used for shooting practice' is from 1862, when measured distance became measured ground. Range-finder, an instrument for measuring distance, is attested from 1872.","cn":"“练枪场地”始于 1862 年，被量出的距离由此变成了被量出的场地。测距仪 range-finder 记录于 1872 年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares the -rang- shape and, in two cases, the actual row-root; the second group shares the idea of an extent or a stretch.","cn":"第一组共享 -rang- 的词形，其中两个还真有“排”的词根；第二组共享“延伸的范围或跨度”这一观念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"rank","ipa":"/ræŋk/","tag":"same row, one letter shorter","definition":"a position in an order, or a line of soldiers. It is the same 'row' word without the -ge.","definitionCN":"等级；行列。它就是同一个“排”字，只是少了 -ge。"},{"word":"ranch","ipa":"/rɑːntʃ/","tag":"one letter swapped","definition":"a large farm for cattle or horses. It looks like range but comes from Spanish rancho, a group of huts.","definitionCN":"大牧场。它形似 range，却来自西班牙语 rancho“一排棚屋”。"},{"word":"ranger","ipa":"/ˈreɪndʒə/","tag":"agent noun of range","definition":"a forest or park officer, or an old mounted trooper. Literally 'one who ranges'.","definitionCN":"护林员；旧时骑警。字面就是“漫游的人”。"},{"word":"arrange","ipa":"/əˈreɪndʒ/","tag":"a- to + range","definition":"to put things in order. The prefix ad- 'to' plus rangier 'set in a row' gives the row verb.","definitionCN":"安排；排列。前缀 ad-“向”加 rangier“排成行”构成这个“排”动词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"scope","ipa":"/skəʊp/","tag":"room to act","definition":"the area a subject or activity covers. It matches range as 'extent' but is more abstract.","definitionCN":"范围；余地。它对应 range 的“幅度”义，但更抽象。"},{"word":"span","ipa":"/spæn/","tag":"end to end","definition":"the distance or time from one end to the other. It is the measured length inside a range.","definitionCN":"跨度；持续时间。它就是 range 内部那段被量出的长度。"},{"word":"extent","ipa":"/ɪkˈstent/","tag":"how far it goes","definition":"the size or degree to which something extends.","definitionCN":"程度；广度；范围。"},{"word":"spectrum","ipa":"/ˈspektrəm/","tag":"a spread of values","definition":"a continuous series of values or qualities. It overlaps range in science and in politics.","definitionCN":"谱；连续系列。它在科学与政治上与 range 重叠。"},{"word":"vary","ipa":"/ˈveəri/","tag":"change across limits","definition":"to change within limits. It is the verbal action behind range from … to ….","definitionCN":"变化；不同。它是 range from…to… 背后的动词动作。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"The family is a row: reng, rank, arrange and ranger all line things up or walk along a line.","cn":"这个词族就是一排：reng、rank、arrange、ranger 都把东西排成线，或沿一条线行走。"},"normal":[{"en":"range and arrange share the Old French row: arrange is 'put into a range'.","cn":"range 与 arrange 共享古法语那个“排”：arrange 就是“排进一列”。"},{"en":"rank is the same row word: soldiers stand in rank, mountains stand in range.","cn":"rank 是同一个“排”字：士兵站成 rank，山峰连成 range。"},{"en":"A ranger is literally a person who ranges: he walks the line of a forest.","cn":"ranger 字面就是一个 range 的人：他沿着森林的边界线走。"},{"en":"A missile range and a mountain range are both measured lines drawn across the map.","cn":"导弹射程与山脉都是画在地图上的一条被量出的线。"},{"en":"The kitchen range is the odd one out: a stove, with no known reason for the name.","cn":"厨房炉灶是这里的异类：一个炉子，得名原因不明。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"One row, many scales: people, posts, bullets, peaks, numbers, all lined up.","cn":"一排，许多尺度：人、木桩、子弹、山峰、数字，全都排成线。"},{"en":"Range is what lies between the first and the last: the row defines an inside.","cn":"range 就是第一与最后之间的东西：这一排定义了一个“里面”。"},{"en":"The word moves from standing in a line to moving along one: row becomes roam.","cn":"这个词从“站成一排”走到“沿一条线移动”：排列变成漫游。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The course covers a wide range of topics, from history to chemistry.","cn":"这门课程涵盖从历史到化学的广泛主题。"},{"en":"Temperatures here range from minus ten to thirty degrees.","cn":"这里的气温从零下十度到三十度不等。"},{"en":"The deer ranged freely across the protected valley.","cn":"鹿群在受保护的山谷里自由漫游。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"ran（跑）+ ge —— 沿着一条排开的线一路跑过去，跑多远就是多大范围 → range 范围；射程；漫游","word":"range"},"root":"源自古法语 reng、renge“一排、一列”，上溯法兰克语 *hring 与原始日耳曼语 *hringaz“环、弯曲之物”，与 ring、rank、arrange 同族；核心是“排成一行，再由这一行量出跨度”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Ten senses all begin with a row: a row of people, a row of posts, a row of peaks. The row measures a distance, the distance becomes a span of values, and the same line is walked as roam.","cn":"十个义项都从“一排”开始：一排人、一排木桩、一排山峰。这一排量出一段距离，距离变成一段取值，而同一条线又被走成了漫游。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a row of posts marking off a stretch of ground.","cn":"核心意象：一排木桩在旷野上圈出一段地。"},"chain":["A ROW","A LINE OF PEOPLE","A MEASURED LINE","THE GROUND IT ENCLOSES","THE VALUES BETWEEN ENDS","TO WALK THAT LINE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S08 · S09","en":"THE ROW IN MOTION: lining things up, and roaming along the open line.","cn":"会动的一排：把东西排成行，以及沿开阔的线漫游。"},{"senses":"S05 · S07","en":"THE LANDSCAPE ROW: peaks standing in line, and the pasture the herd walks.","cn":"地貌的一排：连成线的山峰，以及牛群走过的那片牧场。"},{"senses":"S03 · S04","en":"THE MEASURED DISTANCE: how far a shot reaches, and the ground where it is tested.","cn":"被量出的距离：子弹能飞多远，以及检验这个距离的场地。"},{"senses":"S01 · S10","en":"THE SPAN OF VALUES: the scope between limits, and the verb of varying between its two ends.","cn":"取值的跨度：界限之间的范围，以及在两端之间变动的动词。"},{"senses":"S02 · S06","en":"THE HOUSEHOLD ROW: a line of goods on a shelf, and the kitchen stove.","cn":"家里的一排：货架上成列的商品，以及厨房里的炉灶。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Range is a bare borrowed noun; its family grows by prefixes (a-, de-) and suffixes (-er, -y, -ment). The row-root appears in rank and arrange.","cn":"range 是一个整体借来的名词；它的词族靠前缀（a-、de-）和后缀（-er、-y、-ment）生长。“排”这个词根出现在 rank 与 arrange 里。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin contributes nothing here: the line runs from Frankish *hring through Old French reng to English, with the Germanic 'ring' image behind it.","cn":"这里没有拉丁语的贡献：这条线从法兰克语 *hring 经古法语 reng 到英语，背后是日耳曼语的“环”意象。"},"items":[{"word":"range","structure":"Old French reng / renge (row) + English noun use","meaning":"a row, hence an extent or a span","meaningCN":"一排；范围；射程","example":"The library offers a wide range of services.","exampleCN":"图书馆提供广泛的服务。"},{"word":"ranger","structure":"range (to roam) + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"one who ranges; a forest or park officer","meaningCN":"护林员；漫游者；骑警","example":"A ranger checked our permits at the trailhead.","exampleCN":"一名护林员在步道口检查了我们的许可证。"},{"word":"rangy","structure":"range + -y (adjective)","meaning":"long-limbed and suited to roaming","meaningCN":"瘦长的；适于漫游的","example":"The rangy horse covered the distance easily.","exampleCN":"那匹瘦长的马轻松跑完了这段距离。"},{"word":"arrange","structure":"a- (ad-, to) + rangier (set in a row)","meaning":"to put in order, to plan","meaningCN":"排列；安排","example":"She arranged the flowers in a tall vase.","exampleCN":"她把花插在一个高花瓶里。"},{"word":"arrangement","structure":"arrange + -ment (result noun)","meaning":"an order or plan that has been set out","meaningCN":"安排；排列；布置","example":"We have an arrangement with the local school.","exampleCN":"我们与当地学校有一项安排。"},{"word":"derange","structure":"de- (away from) + range (row)","meaning":"to put out of order; to unsettle the mind","meaningCN":"打乱；使精神错乱","example":"The shock seemed to derange his judgement.","exampleCN":"那次打击似乎扰乱了他的判断。"},{"word":"range-finder","structure":"range + finder (compound agent noun)","meaning":"an instrument that measures distance","meaningCN":"测距仪","example":"The camera's range-finder focuses on the subject.","exampleCN":"相机的测距仪对准被摄主体。"},{"word":"downrange","structure":"down + range (compound adverb)","meaning":"along the path of a missile or spacecraft","meaningCN":"沿导弹或航天器飞行方向；顺射程方向","example":"The rocket tracked downrange for two minutes.","exampleCN":"火箭顺射程方向被追踪了两分钟。"},{"word":"free-range","structure":"free + range (compound adjective)","meaning":"kept in open ground rather than in a cage","meaningCN":"散养的；自由放养的","example":"The shop sells free-range eggs.","exampleCN":"这家店卖散养鸡蛋。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"ratio","ipa_uk":"/ˈreɪʃiəʊ/","ipa_us":"/ˈreɪʃioʊ/","definition_zh":"比率；比值；比例；配比；比例关系；（旧）理由；理性；计算；账目","definition_en":"the relationship between two amounts, shown as the number of times one contains the other, or more generally the proportion between two things","core_image":"一把木尺横在两堆谷物之间，左边三斗、右边一斗，尺上刻出的那道痕把两个量绑成一个可比较的数","scene":"A baker writes on the board and says: The ratio of flour to water is three to one; change it and the bread will not rise.","sceneCN":"这里 ratio 是「比率」（第 1 个义项：两个量之间的关系）；句意：面粉与水的比率是三比一，一旦改了这个比率，面包就发不起来。画面里有木案板、面粉袋和写着 3:1 的黑板。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"比率；比值；比例；配比；比例关系"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the ratio of A to B","zh":"A 与 B 的比率"},{"phrase":"in the ratio 3:1","zh":"以三比一的比例"},{"phrase":"a high ratio","zh":"高比率"},{"phrase":"student-teacher ratio","zh":"师生比"},{"phrase":"price-earnings ratio","zh":"市盈率"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"ratios"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"rational","pos":"adj.","zh":"理性的；合理的；有理数的"},{"word":"rationale","pos":"n.","zh":"理由；根本原因；原理说明"},{"word":"irrational","pos":"adj.","zh":"非理性的；无理的；无理数的"},{"word":"rationality","pos":"n.","zh":"理性；合理性"},{"word":"ration","pos":"n.","zh":"定量；配给量（同出 ratio“计算”）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"One number measured against another","titleCN":"比率：一个量里装得下几个另一个量","definition":"the relationship between two quantities, measured by the number of times one contains the other","definitionCN":"两个量之间的关系，以一个量包含另一个量的次数来衡量","example":"The ratio of boys to girls in the class is two to one.","exampleCN":"班上男生与女生的比率是二比一。","why":"Latin ratio is a reckoning, and the mathematical sense (1650s) asks a counting question: how many times does this quantity fit into that one? The answer is the ratio.","whyCN":"拉丁语 ratio 是一次清算，数学义（17 世纪 50 年代）问的是一个计数问题：这个量在那个量里装得下几次？答案就是比率。"},{"no":"02","title":"Proportion between things","titleCN":"比例关系：两件事之间对应的分寸","definition":"a general relationship in size, amount, or degree between two things that need not be exactly measurable","definitionCN":"两事物在大小、数量或程度上的一般关系，不必精确可测","example":"There is an obvious ratio between hours studied and marks earned.","exampleCN":"学习时数与所得分数之间存在明显的比例关系。","why":"The extended sense 'corresponding relationship between things not precisely measurable' is recorded from 1808. Once ratio means any ordered comparison, it can compare effort with results, not only metres with seconds.","whyCN":"“不可精确测量的事物之间的对应关系”这一扩展义记录于 1808 年。一旦 ratio 指任何有次序的比较，它就能比较努力与结果，而不只是米与秒。"},{"no":"03","title":"The recipe's fixed proportion","titleCN":"配比：配方里不许乱动的那几个数","definition":"the fixed proportion in which ingredients are combined","definitionCN":"各成分混合时所依的固定比例","example":"Mix the cement and sand in a ratio of one to three.","exampleCN":"把水泥和沙子按一比三的配比混合。","why":"A recipe is a set of counts: so much of this, so much of that. Ratio as a reckoning fits the kitchen exactly, because cooking is measuring one ingredient against another.","whyCN":"配方就是一组计数：这个多少、那个多少。作为“清算”的 ratio 正好贴合厨房，因为烹饪就是把一种配料对着另一种量。"},{"no":"04","title":"A number that reads a company","titleCN":"财务比率：用一个除法看穿一家公司","definition":"a figure comparing two financial quantities, used to judge performance or value","definitionCN":"比较两个财务数值的指标，用于判断业绩或价值","example":"A price-earnings ratio of 30 makes the stock look expensive.","exampleCN":"三十倍的市盈率让这只股票显得昂贵。","why":"Finance compresses a whole business into one division: price divided by earnings. The ratio is still a reckoning, now of value against profit, and the quotient is read as a verdict.","whyCN":"金融把一个完整的生意压缩成一次除法：价格除以盈利。这个比率仍是一次清算，只是算的是价值对利润，而商数被读成一句判决。"},{"no":"05","title":"Reason, in the old sense","titleCN":"理由、理性：这个词最早的意思","definition":"reason or rationale, especially in philosophy or theology","definitionCN":"理由或理性根据，尤用于哲学或神学","example":"The theologian wrote of faith and ratio, belief and reason.","exampleCN":"那位神学家谈到信仰与理性、信念与理由。","why":"The word enters English in the 1630s in theological writing meaning 'reason, rationale'. Latin ratio covered both 'calculation' and 'the reasoning faculty', so the counting word was also the thinking word.","whyCN":"这个词于 17 世纪 30 年代以神学写作中的“理由、理性根据”进入英语。拉丁语 ratio 兼指“计算”与“推理能力”，所以这个计数词同时也是思考词。"},{"no":"06","title":"Reckoning and account","titleCN":"计算、账目：拉丁语里的账本义","definition":"a reckoning, calculation, or account, the word's Latin literal sense","definitionCN":"计算、清算或账目，这是该词在拉丁语中的字面义","example":"In Latin, ratio could mean the accounts of a household.","exampleCN":"在拉丁语中，ratio 可以指一户人家的账目。","why":"Latin ratio meant 'a reckoning, account, numbering, calculation', and by transfer 'course, conduct, procedure'. The bookkeeping sense is the trunk from which the mathematical and philosophical branches grew.","whyCN":"拉丁语 ratio 意为“清算、账目、计数、计算”，再转指“进程、行为、程序”。记账义是树干，数学与哲学的分枝都从它长出。"},{"no":"07","title":"Gear ratio: teeth against teeth","titleCN":"传动比：大齿轮转一圈，小齿轮转几圈","definition":"the ratio between the speeds or teeth of two connected gears or parts","definitionCN":"两个相连齿轮或部件的转速或齿数之比","example":"A lower gear ratio gives more turning force to the wheels.","exampleCN":"较低的传动比给车轮更大的转动力。","why":"Two cogwheels are two counts of teeth meeting at a rim; their sizes are compared the same way as any two magnitudes. Engineering merely applies the arithmetic of ratio to metal.","whyCN":"两个齿轮就是两串齿数在轮缘相遇；它们的大小比较方式与任何两个量一样。工程只是把 ratio 的算术用到金属上。"},{"no":"08","title":"The social ratio","titleCN":"师生比：用一个分数描述一群人的处境","definition":"a figure comparing two groups in a population, such as students per teacher","definitionCN":"比较人口中两个群体的数字，如每位教师对应的学生数","example":"The school improved its student-teacher ratio to 12 to 1.","exampleCN":"这所学校把师生比改善到了十二比一。","why":"A social ratio counts one group against another and turns a human situation into a single readable number. It is the same move as the financial ratio, applied to classrooms and hospitals.","whyCN":"社会比率把一群人对另一群人计数，把人的处境变成一个可读的数字。这与财务比率是同一个动作，只是用在教室和医院里。"},{"no":"09","title":"The golden ratio","titleCN":"黄金比例：被当成美的那个数","definition":"a special proportion, about 1.618 to 1, believed to produce pleasing shapes","definitionCN":"约为 1.618 比 1 的特殊比例，被认为能产生悦目的形状","example":"Painters have long used the golden ratio in composing a picture.","exampleCN":"画家们长久以来在构图中使用黄金比例。","why":"The golden ratio is a fixed division of a line so that the whole is to the long part as the long part is to the short. A number born from reckoning acquired a reputation for beauty.","whyCN":"黄金比例是把一条线按“整体比长段，等于长段比短段”的方式分割。一个由清算诞生的数，由此获得了“美”的名声。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Ratio is Latin for 'reckoning'. It names an account, then the faculty that keeps accounts, then the relation between two amounts. Philosophy gave it reason; mathematics gave it the number that compares.","cn":"ratio 在拉丁语里意为“清算”。它先指账目，再指会记账的心智能力，最后指两个量之间的关系。哲学给了它“理性”，数学给了它“比较之数”。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE (reconstructed)","en":"The root *re- 'to think, reason, count' is reconstructed from Latin and related branches. There is no written record of the root itself, so this layer is marked source uncertain.","cn":"词根 *re-“思考、推理、计数”是从拉丁语及相关语支重构出来的。词根本身没有书面记录，因此这一层标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"LATIN (before 1C BC)","en":"Reri meant 'to reckon, calculate', also 'to think, believe'. Its past-participle stem rat- produced ratio 'a reckoning, account, numbering, calculation', and by transfer 'reason, judgement, understanding'.","cn":"reri 意为“计算、估算”，也指“思考、相信”。其过去分词词干 rat- 生出 ratio“清算、账目、计数、计算”，再转指“理性、判断、理解”。"},{"era":"LATIN (1C BC–4C AD)","en":"In philosophy ratio was often used to render Greek logos, 'computation, account, reason', though ratio lacked logos's 'speech, word' sense. Rationem, the accusative, is the source of English reason, ration and ratio's relatives.","cn":"在哲学中，ratio 常用来对译希腊语 logos“计算、账目、理性”，但 ratio 缺少 logos 的“言语、词”义。其宾格 rationem 是英语 reason、ration 等同源词的来源。"},{"era":"1630s ENGLISH","en":"Ratio is borrowed in theological writing meaning 'reason, rationale'. For its first decades in English it is a word about argument, not about division.","cn":"ratio 在 17 世纪 30 年代的神学写作中被借入，意为“理由、理性根据”。在英语里的最初几十年，它是一个关于论证的词，而不是关于除法的词。"},{"era":"1650s–1808 ENGLISH","en":"The mathematical sense, 'relation between two similar magnitudes in respect to quantity', is attested from the 1650s. The general sense, 'corresponding relationship between things not precisely measurable', is from 1808.","cn":"数学义“两个同类量在数量上的关系”记录于 17 世纪 50 年代。一般义“不可精确测量的事物之间的对应关系”始于 1808 年。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Compound uses such as price-earnings ratio, gear ratio and student-teacher ratio are later specializations of the mathematical sense. Their individual coinage dates are not given in the standard etymology and are marked source uncertain.","cn":"price-earnings ratio、gear ratio、student-teacher ratio 等复合用法，是数学义后来的专门化。通行词源没有给出各自的造词年代，故标为“来源不确定”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group differs from ratio by one or two letters but comes from the same Latin stem; the second group names other ways of comparing amounts.","cn":"第一组与 ratio 只差一两个字母，且出自同一个拉丁词干；第二组指比较数量的其他说法。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"ration","ipa":"/ˈræʃn/","tag":"same root, a measured share","definition":"a fixed allowance of food or supplies. It is ratio's sister: a measured portion.","definitionCN":"定量；配给量。它是 ratio 的姐妹词：一份被量出的份额。"},{"word":"rational","ipa":"/ˈræʃnəl/","tag":"same root, reasoning","definition":"based on reason; also a number expressible as a ratio of integers.","definitionCN":"理性的；合理的；有理数的（可写成两整数之比）。"},{"word":"rationale","ipa":"/ˌræʃəˈnɑːl/","tag":"same root, stated reason","definition":"the reasons or principles behind a decision. It looks plural but is a singular noun.","definitionCN":"理由；原理说明。它看起来像复数，其实是单数名词。"},{"word":"ratiocination","ipa":"/ˌrætiˌɒsɪˈneɪʃn/","tag":"same root, formal reasoning","definition":"the process of logical reasoning, from Latin ratiocinari 'to reckon'.","definitionCN":"推理过程；逻辑推演，来自拉丁语 ratiocinari“计算”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"proportion","ipa":"/prəˈpɔːʃn/","tag":"part against whole","definition":"the relation of one part to another or to the whole. It is broader and often more everyday than ratio.","definitionCN":"比例；部分与整体的关系。它比 ratio 更宽，也更日常。"},{"word":"percentage","ipa":"/pəˈsentɪdʒ/","tag":"a ratio out of a hundred","definition":"a proportion expressed as a number out of one hundred.","definitionCN":"百分比；以百为基数的比例。"},{"word":"fraction","ipa":"/ˈfrækʃn/","tag":"a part of a whole","definition":"a numerical part of a whole, written as one number over another.","definitionCN":"分数；一部分。"},{"word":"rate","ipa":"/reɪt/","tag":"a measure per unit","definition":"a measure of one quantity against another, often per unit of time. It shares the Latin reckoning root.","definitionCN":"比率；速率。它共享拉丁语“计算”的词根。"},{"word":"quotient","ipa":"/ˈkwəʊʃnt/","tag":"the result of division","definition":"the number produced by dividing one quantity by another.","definitionCN":"商；除法所得的数。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"The family is one act of reckoning: rational, rationale, ration and rate all come from Latin reri 'to reckon'.","cn":"这个词族是一次清算：rational、rationale、ration、rate 都来自拉丁语 reri“计算”。"},"normal":[{"en":"ratio and rational share the stem rat-: ratio is the number, rational is the mind that can follow it.","cn":"ratio 与 rational 共享词干 rat-：ratio 是那个数，rational 是能跟上它的心智。"},{"en":"A ration is a ratio made edible: a measured share of food.","cn":"ration 是可食用的 ratio：一份被量出的食物。"},{"en":"Rate and ratio both come from reri 'to reckon'; a rate is a ratio with a unit attached.","cn":"rate 与 ratio 都来自 reri“计算”；rate 是挂了一个单位的比率。"},{"en":"A price-earnings ratio is one division that turns a company into a single number.","cn":"市盈率就是一次除法，把一家公司变成一个数。"},{"en":"The golden ratio is the number 1.618, the proportion painters trust.","cn":"黄金比例就是 1.618 这个数，画家们信任的那个比例。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"One reckoning, two directions: outward it compares amounts, inward it becomes reason.","cn":"一次清算，两个方向：向外比较数量，向内变成理性。"},{"en":"Ratio is the shape of a relation: it tells you how many times, not how much.","cn":"ratio 是一段关系的形状：它告诉你“几次”，而不是“多少”。"},{"en":"From an account book to a classroom to a gearbox, the same division is read as a judgement.","cn":"从账本到教室再到齿轮箱，同一次除法都被读成一句判断。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The ratio of staff to patients has fallen to one to eight.","cn":"员工与病人的比率已降到一比八。"},{"en":"Combine the oil and vinegar in a ratio of two to one.","cn":"把油和醋按二比一的配比混合。"},{"en":"The chart plots the ratio of debt to income over ten years.","cn":"这张图表绘出了十年间债务与收入的比率。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音联想 · 非词源","text":"rat（老鼠）+ io —— 三只老鼠对一只猫，数一数“几比几” → ratio 比率；比例","word":"ratio"},"root":"源自拉丁语 reri“计算、估算”的过去分词词干 rat-，名词 ratio 意为“清算、账目、计算”，并转指“理性、理由”；与 reason、rate、ration 同出“计算”这一词根。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses built from one act of counting: an account, a reason, and then every comparison of one amount with another, from a recipe to a gearbox to the golden section.","cn":"九个义项都建在同一次计数上：先是账目，再是理由，然后是任何两个量的比较，从配方到齿轮箱再到黄金分割。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two amounts laid side by side, one measured against the other.","cn":"核心意象：两个量并排放着，一个对着另一个来量。"},"chain":["TO RECKON","AN ACCOUNT","REASON","TWO MAGNITUDES","HOW MANY TIMES","A FIXED PROPORTION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S06 · S05","en":"THE RECKONING: the account book, and the reasoning mind that keeps it.","cn":"清算：账本，以及记账的那颗推理之心。"},{"senses":"S01 · S03","en":"THE COUNTED RELATION: one number containing another, and the recipe's fixed measure.","cn":"被数出的关系：一个数量包含另一个，以及配方里固定的量。"},{"senses":"S02 · S09","en":"THE PROPORTION: loose correspondence between things, and the golden division praised as beauty.","cn":"比例：事物间宽泛的对应，以及被赞为美的黄金分割。"},{"senses":"S04 · S07","en":"THE WORKING NUMBER: a company read as a ratio, and teeth counted against teeth.","cn":"干活的数：被读成比率的公司，以及齿对齿的计数。"},{"senses":"S08","en":"THE HUMAN RATIO: one group counted against another in a school or a ward.","cn":"人的比率：在学校或病房里，一群人对着另一群人计数。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Ratio is the bare Latin noun rat- 'reckon' plus -io. Its family shows the suffixes -ional, -ionale, -ality, -alize and -ion, and the root rat- shared with rate and ration.","cn":"ratio 是不带前缀的拉丁名词：词干 rat-“计算”加 -io。它的词族展示后缀 -ional、-ionale、-ality、-alize、-ion，以及与 rate、ration 共享的词根 rat-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin reri 'to reckon' gives ratio 'reckoning', rationalis 'of reason', rationem 'account', and ratiocinari 'to reason'. English reason and rate descend from the same reckoning stem.","cn":"拉丁语 reri“计算”给出 ratio“清算”、rationalis“理性的”、rationem“账目”，以及 ratiocinari“推理”。英语 reason 与 rate 也出自同一“计算”词干。"},"items":[{"word":"ratio","structure":"rat- (reckon) + -io (noun)","meaning":"a reckoning; the relation between two amounts","meaningCN":"比率；比例","example":"The ratio of imports to exports widened last year.","exampleCN":"去年进口与出口的比率扩大了。"},{"word":"rational","structure":"ration- (reason) + -al (adjective)","meaning":"based on reason; expressible as a ratio","meaningCN":"理性的；合理的；有理数的","example":"There is a rational explanation for the delay.","exampleCN":"这次延误有一个合理的解释。"},{"word":"rationale","structure":"rational + -e (Latin noun ending)","meaning":"the stated reasons behind something","meaningCN":"理由；原理说明","example":"The report explains the rationale for the new policy.","exampleCN":"报告解释了新政策的理由。"},{"word":"irrational","structure":"ir- (not) + rational","meaning":"not based on reason; not expressible as a simple ratio","meaningCN":"非理性的；无理数的","example":"Fear of the dark is often irrational.","exampleCN":"怕黑常常是非理性的。"},{"word":"rationality","structure":"rational + -ity (quality noun)","meaning":"the quality of being guided by reason","meaningCN":"理性；合理性","example":"The debate tested the rationality of the plan.","exampleCN":"这场辩论检验了该计划的合理性。"},{"word":"rationalize","structure":"rational + -ize (make)","meaning":"to invent a reason for; to make more efficient","meaningCN":"为……找理由；使合理化","example":"He rationalized his mistake as a misunderstanding.","exampleCN":"他把自己的错误辩解成一场误会。"},{"word":"ration","structure":"rat- (reckon) + -ion (measured share)","meaning":"a fixed allowance of food or supplies","meaningCN":"定量；配给量","example":"Each soldier received a daily ration of bread.","exampleCN":"每名士兵每天领到一份面包。"},{"word":"ratiocination","structure":"ratiocinari (to reason) + -ation","meaning":"formal logical reasoning","meaningCN":"推理；逻辑推演","example":"The essay is a long piece of ratiocination.","exampleCN":"这篇文章是一长串推理。"},{"word":"rate","structure":"rat- (reckon) + -e (English noun)","meaning":"a measured amount per unit","meaningCN":"比率；速率；费率","example":"The unemployment rate fell to four percent.","exampleCN":"失业率降到了百分之四。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"reri","structure":"reri (deponent verb)","meaning":"to reckon, calculate; to think","meaningCN":"计算；估算；思考"},{"word":"ratio","structure":"rat- + -io (noun)","meaning":"a reckoning, account, reason","meaningCN":"清算；账目；理性"},{"word":"ratiocinari","structure":"ratio + -cinari (verb)","meaning":"to reason, deliberate","meaningCN":"推理；推演"}]}}]);
